  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. It seems they want a \"My Museum\" app featuring 3D models and they\'ve given a brief description in Banglish. My focus is on deciphering the core functionality - specifically the need for 3D models - before formulating a complete understanding of the scope.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI\'ve clarified the core app features. It\'s a 3D museum allowing users to add images that expand the museum\'s \"walls.\" There\'s a sorting system for all added images. Users can grant access to others and customize their 3D avatars. The home page allows avatar customization before entering the museum. I\342\200\231m focusing on full-stack development.\n\n\n**Implementing User Authentication**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing user authentication, considering Firebase for sign-in and account creation, along with user profile persistence. The core requirement necessitates distinguishing avatar models by gender upon login, ensuring images persist within the museum\'s 3D environment. Access control is another focus, as the app allows granting access to other users, also dictating gender-based model display. This dictates that user data must be persistently stored via Firebase or some other platform.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Avatar Customization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on avatar customization features. Users will personalize their 3D models before entering the museum; I am thinking of including options for gender, skin tone, hairstyles and colors, outfits, and accessories. There\'ll be a live preview during customization, and then the user can enter the 3D museum. Also, the museum expands dynamically as users add images.\n\n\n**Expanding Museum Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enhanced user interactions within the 3D museum. Key considerations include allowing users to jump directly to specific artworks, edit or delete existing ones, and upload new additions. I\'m also planning to implement shared museum access using invite codes and email grants, and share links, giving collaborators varying permissions: viewer or curator, and allowing users to switch between their own and shared museums. I\'ll utilize Firestore for real-time presence, so users in the same museum can see each other as their customized 3D avatars.\n\n\n**Integrating Relevant Skills**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial skills, focusing on a 3D spatial app. `threejs` is key for the 3D environment, expandable gallery, customizable avatars, and camera controls. `firebase-integration-rpc` handles persistent user data, artwork storage, museum access, and real-time presence. Browser verification requires `computer-use`. I am using the above to refine the user experience.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "HsQBa_ybLMHmz7IP-MaJwAE"
