  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Prioritizing System Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the overarching system architecture. My goal is to define the verification plan, visual assets, and a robust data model upfront, *before* coding commences. This systematic approach feels like the most efficient way forward, ensuring a solid foundation from the start. \"My Museum\" is the name I am working with in my own mind.\n\n\n**Defining Museum Editorial**\n\nI\'ve been solidifying the visual theme. Archival Warm Limestone is the core aesthetic now. I\'m focusing on the color palette (`#F8F6F1`, `#EFECE6`, `#1C1917`, `#8A5A2B`) and the 3D museum HUD. I\'m working with dark, warm obsidian frosted bars for the UI, with crisp alabaster text. I\'ve chosen `Cormorant Garamond`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, and `JetBrains Mono` for typography and I\'m avoiding static pills/capsules on metadata. My focus is on concise, clean presentations.\n\n\n**Mapping User Entry Points**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the initial user experience. The `/` route will feature a 3-zone top bar with the brand, navigation links, and a primary call to action. I want to make sure the Google sign-in flow is as smooth as possible using Firebase Auth, and that guest users have a frictionless path to enter a local preview mode with curated art. The guest option will be a deterministic curated seed artwork! I\'m thinking of using Firebase Auth (`signInWithPopup`), to accomplish this. The user should be able to create a user, and a cloud-synced museum.\n\n\n**Refining Guest Preview Flows**\n\nI\'m making Guest Preview mode seamless by mirroring the full experience locally using `localStorage`. This ensures every click is live. I\'m also planning the hero layout for the studio, balancing a 3D avatar stage on the left with customization controls on the right. The avatar will be fully procedural and interactive in Three.js, with distinct features for Man and Woman silhouettes.\n\n\n\n**Designing Avatar Studio**\n\nI\'m now detailing the avatar customization interface in the studio. I\'ve broken it down by function: name, skin, hair (style and color), attire, accessories, and the primary \"Enter Museum\" action. The avatar will be gendered, with distinct options for each: e.g. skirt or jumpsuit for women. I\'m focusing on simplicity, with a clean UI, so I\'ve chosen six skin tones and hair tones, with four hair styles each. Attire includes three silhouettes per gender, with color selection for the outfits and accessories. Once complete, pressing \"Enter Museum\" saves the avatar profile to Firestore or local state and transitions to the 3D museum!\n\nI\'m also working on the museum switcher and shared access features, which will be accessible from the Home Studio and inside the museum. I\'m focusing on \"My Personal Museum,\" \"Shared With Me\" museums, and also an access code. The ability to grant access to another user by email is a feature I\'m working with.\n\n\n**Envisioning Multi-Avatar Support**\n\nI\'m focused on multi-user interactions now. I\'m designing real-time, in-museum avatar display with nameplates when a user is signed in to the shared museum. I\'m exploring an \"Invited Visitors\" roster, and I\'m planning a \"Simulated Co-Visitor Preview\" feature, which would be visible to a user with granted access and would showcase a male and female avatar for testing shared access!\n\n\n**Architecting Expanding Galleries**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core museum structure using a modular approach of gallery bays. Each bay is meticulously defined, ensuring that it is unit-tested. I\'ve designed for automatic expansion, dynamically calculating the number of bays needed based on artwork count, which affects the museum\'s layout.\n\n\n**Expanding Gallery Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing seamless gallery expansions. If all slots are taken, a new Wing extends, visible on the HUD, which dynamically updates. Each artwork will feature a multi-part frame, archival passe-partout, and brass lighting, alongside an accession plaque for details. Clicking the artwork will open an inspection modal.\n\n\n**Implementing Gallery Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing avatar locomotion. I\'ve got the controls mapped: WASD/arrow keys for movement, Shift for brisk walking, and mouse drag for orbit. The avatar\'s movement is smooth, and I\'ve added a one-click toggle to first-person view. Wall collision bounds are perfectly clamped within the galleries. I\'m focusing on the teleport functionality: clicking artwork in the catalog instantly moves the avatar.\n\n\n\n**Defining Artwork Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on search and artwork interaction. I\'m implementing sorting by newest/oldest, and grouping by date for a chronological timeline or grid view. The user will be able to search by title, artist, or notes. I\'m focusing on \"Walk To Wall\" teleport and inspect/delete actions for each artwork, alongside a detailed upload modal, as well.\n\n\n**Refining Access Control**\n\nI\'m now detailing user access and the multi-user system. I\'m focusing on features such as email-based invites with role assignment (Visitor or Curator), the Museum Access Code for easy sharing, and a join tab. The goal is real-time user presence, syncing avatar state across users in shared museums. I\'m excited about smooth avatar interactions, while carefully throttling for performance. I\'m also planning the artwork upload modal.\n\n\n**Visualizing User Presence**\n\nI\'m now implementing real-time avatar previews for invited guests. I\'ve got a feature working that showcases a user\'s avatar, pre-sign-in, as a customized Man/Woman 3D model. Invited guests will populate in the \"Active & Invited Visitors\" strip, and the owner can toggle \"Preview Invited Guests in 3D\" to see these avatars immediately! I\'m also planning the museum-grade curated seed artwork implementation.\n\n\n**Generating Museum Artwork**\n\nI\'m now generating five diverse artworks for the galleries: landscapes, architecture, abstract expressionism, botanical study, and coastal photography, all with matched aspect ratios. I\'ve also batched the npm dependencies for installation and I\'m ensuring this happens in parallel with image generation. I\'m focusing on maximum visual impact as framed artworks.\n\n\n**Verifying Expansion Modules**\n\nI\'m now detailing an **Ultra-Mode Verification Plan** to guide our progress. Specifically, I\'m focusing on rigorous unit tests for pure modules like `calculateMuseumLayout`, `clampPlayerPosition`, `sortArtworksByDate`, `groupArtworksByDate`, `validateArtworkInput` and `validateAccessGrant`. These should verify museum layout expansion, player boundary restrictions, date sorting, and data validation rules, to ensure data and structural integrity.\n\n\n\n**Validating Core User Flows**\n\nI\'m now detailing user journeys for thorough verification. I\'m focusing on two key flows. The first validates home page 3D avatar customization and visual changes. The second tests 3D museum navigation, dynamic wall expansion, and chronological catalog sorting. I\'m prioritizing rigorous validation of all state updates.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "2ccBa-aIFcnV-sAPoZu8mQw"
