  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing the Backend**\n\nI\'m currently focused on coding the Firebase integration. My immediate task is defining the `src/firebase.ts` and `src/services/museumService.ts` files. Simultaneously, I\'m working to flesh out the Three.js procedural craft engine, specifically its components within `src/three/proceduralTextures.ts`, `src/three/avatarBuilder.ts`, and `src/three/museumBuilder.ts`. I am excited to see these concepts materialize.\n\n\n**Analyzing Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the `src/firebase.ts` and `src/services/museumService.ts` files, detailing their Firebase dependencies. I\'m focusing on the intricacies of `getFirestore` with `firebaseConfig.firestoreDatabaseId` and authentication with `signInWithPopup`. Additionally, I\'m examining the `testConnection()` function and its role in startup. On the service side, I\'m analyzing the persistence logic, especially methods like `loadOrCreateUserProfile` and `ensurePersonalMuseum`, including the critical atomic `writeBatch` operation. The data subscription and code lookup functions are also under review.\n\n\n**Refining Access Control**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the secure data access methods. I\'m deep in defining functions to manage artworks and members. I am working on `subscribeArtworks`, `addArtworkToMuseum`, `deleteArtworkFromMuseum`, `grantMuseumAccess`, and more. I\'m paying close attention to the Firestore `allow list` rules, and ensuring all queries include matching filter. My goal is for this to be a secure and responsive system. The presence features are also in progress.\n\n\n**Securing Database Access**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously defining the Firestore security rules. My focus is now on crafting robust queries that guarantee no `PERMISSION_DENIED` errors, following a strict pattern of `where(...)` clauses. I\'m prioritizing user authentication with email verification and refining the filtering logic for artworks, members, and presence data, based on ownership, open access codes, and viewer emails. I\'m also planning high-resolution procedural textures for the Three.js environment, aiming for realistic and detailed visuals, particularly focusing on materials like marble, plaster, wood, and accession plaques.\n\n\n**Designing the Avatars**\n\nI\'m now deep in the details of the avatar builder. I\'m building 3D human figures, distinguishing between man and woman with articulated pivots for realistic animation. The man avatars will have structured shoulders, tailored attire, and diverse hairstyles like taper, swept, curly, and crop. For women, I\'m focusing on refined shoulders, sculpted waistlines, flared dresses or tailored coats, aiming for a distinct visual presentation.\n\n\n**Detailing the Avatars**\n\nI\'m now implementing the accessories and facial features for the avatars. I\'m excited about the tortoiseshell glasses, curator scarf, and gallery pass. The face will feature dark eyes, eyebrows, a sculpted nose, and warm lip accents, along with varying PBR roughness for realistic textures. I\'m defining the museum builder based on MuseumLayout, WallTheme, and ArtworkItem[].\n\n\n"
    message_id: "tsoBa9DKI-WxsOIPxOSYoQw"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_9000168259040873825"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { initializeApp } from \'firebase/app\';\\nimport { getAuth, GoogleAuthProvider } from \'firebase/auth\';\\nimport { doc, getDocFromServer, getFirestore } from \'firebase/firestore\';\\nimport firebaseConfig from \'../firebase-applet-config.json\';\\n\\nconst app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);\\nexport const db = getFirestore(app, firebaseConfig.firestoreDatabaseId);\\nexport const auth = getAuth(app);\\nexport const googleProvider = new GoogleAuthProvider();\\ngoogleProvider.setCustomParameters({ prompt: \'select_account\' });\\n\\nexport enum OperationType {\\n  CREATE = \'create\',\\n  UPDATE = \'update\',\\n  DELETE = \'delete\',\\n  LIST = \'list\',\\n  GET = \'get\',\\n  WRITE = \'write\',\\n}\\n\\nexport interface FirestoreErrorInfo {\\n  error: string;\\n  operationType: OperationType;\\n  path: string | null;\\n  authInfo: {\\n    userId?: string | null;\\n    email?: string | null;\\n    emailVerified?: boolean | null;\\n    isAnonymous?: boolean | null;\\n    tenantId?: string | null;\\n    providerInfo?: {\\n      providerId?: string | null;\\n      email?: string | null;\\n    }[];\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function handleFirestoreError(\\n  error: unknown,\\n  operationType: OperationType,\\n  path: string | null\\n): never {\\n  const errInfo: FirestoreErrorInfo = {\\n    error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\\n    authInfo: {\\n      userId: auth.currentUser?.uid,\\n      email: auth.currentUser?.email,\\n      emailVerified: auth.currentUser?.emailVerified,\\n      isAnonymous: auth.currentUser?.isAnonymous,\\n      tenantId: auth.currentUser?.tenantId,\\n      providerInfo:\\n        auth.currentUser?.providerData?.map((provider) => ({\\n          providerId: provider.providerId,\\n          email: provider.email,\\n        })) || [],\\n    },\\n    operationType,\\n    path,\\n  };\\n  console.error(\'Firestore Error:\', JSON.stringify(errInfo));\\n  throw new Error(JSON.stringify(errInfo));\\n}\\n\\nasync function testConnection() {\\n  try {\\n    await getDocFromServer(doc(db, \'test\', \'connection\'));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    if (error instanceof Error && error.message.includes(\'the client is offline\')) {\\n      console.error(\'Please check your Firebase configuration.\');\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nvoid testConnection();\\n\", \"Description\":\"Initialize Firebase Auth, Firestore with configured database ID, startup connection check, and structured error handler\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/firebase.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating src/firebase.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create src/firebase.ts\"}"
