  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request**: Build **\"My Museum\"**, a grand, realistic, walkable 3D virtual art museum web application with top-notch UX/UI, project architecture, and full-stack persistence.\n- **Core Functional Requirements**:\n  1. **Home Page & Pre-Entry 3D Avatar Customization Studio**: Sign in (Firebase Google Auth + seamless Guest Studio preview fallback) on the Home page, customize a 3D avatar (distinct **Man** or **Woman** 3D models, display name, skin tone, 4 hair styles per gender, hair color, 3 outfit styles per gender, primary/accent wardrobe colors, accessories) with a live interactive 360\302\260 3D turntable preview, then click **Enter 3D Museum**.\n  2. **Walkable 3D Museum**: Large realistic neoclassical/architectural 3D hall (`Three.js` / WebGL) where the user walks around (WASD / Arrow keys / drag look / mobile D-pad, 3rd-person default + 1st-person toggle) as their customized Man or Woman 3D avatar viewing framed artworks with plaques and picture lights.\n  3. **Dynamic Wall Expansion**: As more images are added, the 3D museum corridor automatically expands (every 2 artworks = 1 architectural Gallery Wing with opposing West/East walls, columns, skylights, floor tiles, and central velvet benches; `bayCount = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(artworkCount / 2))`).\n  4. **Complete Date-Sorted Artwork List / Catalog**: One-click Catalog drawer showing all images in the museum sorted chronologically by date (`Newest First` / `Oldest First`, Timeline grouped by date or Grid view, search, inspect, delete, and `Walk To Wall` teleport in 3D).\n  5. **Shared Museum Access & Multi-Visitor Gender Avatars**: Owners can grant access to others by email (selecting `Visitor` or `Co-Curator` role and `Man`/`Woman` avatar gender) or share an Access Code (`MUS-XXXX`). Authorized users can switch/join shared museums and appear together inside the 3D museum as their gender-customized 3D models (via Firestore real-time presence + toggleable invited companion avatars in 3D).\n- **Runtime / Environment**:\n  - Applet ID: `4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4`\n  - Dev server on port 3000 (`DISABLE_HMR=true` \342\200\224 must call `restart_dev_server` after edits before browser verification).\n  - Provisioned Firebase Project ID: `bold-impulse-pkhlb`, Firestore DB ID: `ai-studio-4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4` (written in `/firebase-applet-config.json`).\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Skills & References Already Read\n- `/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md` + `references/games_3d.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md` + `references/5_threejs_3d_spatial.md` + `references/9_museum_editorial_institutional.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md` + `references/fundamentals.md`, `lighting.md`, `interaction.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` + `references/firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md`, `error-handling-and-sdk.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`\n\n### Completed Provisioning, Dependencies & Generated Assets\n- **Firebase**: Terms accepted, verified (`GetFirebaseTos`), provisioned (`ProvisionFirebase` -> `/firebase-applet-config.json`), hardened rules linted with `npx eslint firestore.rules` (exit 0), and deployed (`DeployRules` succeeded).\n- **Packages Installed**: `three` (`0.187.0`), `@types/three`, `firebase`, `eslint`, `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules`.\n- **Generated Local Fine-Art Images** (5 high-resolution assets via `generate_image`):\n  - `/src/assets/images/art_alpine_twilight_1795278906644.jpg`\n  - `/src/assets/images/art_botanical_atelier_1795278908731.jpg`\n  - `/src/assets/images/art_brutalist_courtyard_1795278907758.jpg`\n  - `/src/assets/images/art_coastal_horizon_1795278908179.jpg`\n  - `/src/assets/images/art_abstract_ochre_1795278909230.jpg`\n\n### Files Created / Updated (Complete Initial Build + Round 1 Bug Fixes)\n- `/metadata.json`, `/index.html`, `/src/index.css` (My Museum metadata + `Cormorant Garamond`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, `JetBrains Mono` fonts).\n- `/firebase-blueprint.json`, `/eslint.config.js`, `/security_spec.md`, `/firestore.rules` (Eight Pillars hardened rules; deployed).\n- `/src/types/museum.ts` \342\200\224 All TypeScript types & Man/Woman avatar presets.\n- `/src/museum/layout.ts` \342\200\224 Pure procedural expansion math (`calculateMuseumLayout`, `getArtworkPlacement`, `clampPlayerPosition`, `sortArtworksByDate`, `groupArtworksByDate`, `validateArtworkInput`, `validateAccessGrant`, `generateAccessCode`).\n- `/src/museum/layout.test.ts` \342\200\224 5 `node:test` unit tests (**all 5 passed** via `npx --yes tsx --test src/museum/layout.test.ts`).\n- `/src/data/seedMuseum.ts` \342\200\224 Deterministic curated exhibition using the 5 generated images + sample invited visitor (`Clara Moreau`, Woman).\n- `/src/firebase.ts` & `/src/services/museumService.ts` \342\200\224 Firebase Auth (`signInWithPopup`), Firestore `getFirestore(app, firebaseConfig.firestoreDatabaseId)`, startup `testConnection()`, `handleFirestoreError`, real-time listeners with secure `where` clauses matching `firestore.rules`.\n- `/src/three/webglUtils.ts` \342\200\224 Software WebGL detection (`detectSoftwareGl`), bounded `afterDraw` fenceSync scheduler, HTML5 Canvas photo compression (`compressUploadedImage`).\n- `/src/three/proceduralTextures.ts` \342\200\224 Procedural veined marble floor + bump map, Venetian plaster wall, contact shadow, museum wall accession plaque, floating visitor nameplate, fallback artwork texture.\n- `/src/three/avatarBuilder.ts` \342\200\224 Composite 16+ part procedural 3D human avatars with distinct Man vs Woman silhouettes, hair styles, outfits, accessories, and smooth walking stride animation (`animateAvatarRig`).\n- `/src/three/museumBuilder.ts` \342\200\224 Dynamic expanding 3D neoclassical museum hall, pilasters, coffered beams, skylights, velvet benches, grand north sculpture alcove, framed artworks with brass picture lights and plaques.\n- `/src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx`\n- `/src/components/AvatarPreview3D.tsx` \342\200\224 Interactive 3D avatar turntable (just updated with Round 1 fixes; **NOT YET RECOMPILED OR RE-VERIFIED**).\n- `/src/components/Museum3DView.tsx` \342\200\224 Full-viewport walkable 3D museum with collapsible zero-occlusion bottom dock (just updated with Round 1 fixes; **NOT YET RECOMPILED OR RE-VERIFIED**).\n- `/src/components/HomeStudio.tsx` \342\200\224 3-zone top bar + 2-column Avatar Studio + Collection + Shared Access + Guide (just tightened vertical spacing; **NOT YET RECOMPILED OR RE-VERIFIED**).\n- `/src/components/CatalogDrawer.tsx`, `/src/components/UploadArtworkModal.tsx`, `/src/components/AccessModal.tsx`, `/src/components/ArtworkInspectModal.tsx`, `/src/App.tsx`.\n\n### Verification Status\n- **Unit tests (`src/museum/layout.test.ts`)**: 5/5 passed before Round 1 UI edits (no changes made to `layout.ts` since, but re-run at end to be 100% current).\n- **Round 1 Browser Verification**: Completed on `1440x900` desktop (`r1-home-desktop.png`, `r1-museum-desktop.png`). Identified 4 defects (see Section 4) and applied fixes to `webglUtils.ts`, `AvatarPreview3D.tsx`, `Museum3DView.tsx`, and `HomeStudio.tsx`.\n- **Round 2 Browser Verification**: **NOT YET RUN** (app must be compiled, dev server restarted, and Round 2 screenshots + full journeys verified).\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- Headless Chromium runs on SwiftShader (`ANGLE (Google, Vulkan 1.3.0 (SwiftShader Device ...))`), so `detectSoftwareGl()` returns `true` and uses pixel ratio 1, shadows off, `afterDraw` pacing, and no `backdrop-filter` over WebGL.\n- `three@0.187.0` deprecated `THREE.Clock`; replaced with `performance.now()` delta tracking in `Museum3DView.tsx`.\n- Firestore `allow list` rules strictly forbid `get()` calls and require matching `where(...)` clauses; `museumService.ts` mirrors `isOpenByCode` and `viewerEmails` onto subcollection docs (`artworks`, `presence`) and uses exact `where(...)` queries.\n- Uploaded user photos are compressed client-side via Canvas to `< 360KB` JPEG data URLs so they store cleanly inside Firestore documents (1MB limit) and render directly as `THREE.TextureLoader` textures with zero external storage/CORS issues.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **Build Error \342\200\224 Duplicate `trackMat` identifier in `src/three/museumBuilder.ts:242`**:\n   - *Cause*: Local lighting rail material `const trackMat = trackMat(...)` shadowed the `trackMat` helper function.\n   - *Fix*: Renamed to `railMat`. Subsequent `compile_applet` succeeded.\n2. **Round 1 High Defect \342\200\224 `Museum3DView` initial camera spawned behind the South Wall (`r1-museum-desktop.png`)**:\n   - *Cause*: `camera.position.z = 7.6` exceeded `southWallZ = 6.5` (`southWall` spanned `z = 6.5..6.9`), so the camera stared into the plaster wall and only `depthTest: false` floating avatar nameplates were visible.\n   - *Fix Applied (unverified)*: Moved spawn to `(0, 0, 0.9)` facing `-Z` (`yaw = Math.PI`), initialized camera inside foyer at `(0, 2.25, 4.9)` looking at `(0, 1.6, -5)`, and kept `dist = 4.0` clamped inside walls.\n3. **Round 1 High Defect \342\200\224 `AvatarPreview3D` canvas appeared solid `#EBE6DD` (`r1-home-desktop.png`)**:\n   - *Cause*: `ResizeObserver` called `renderer.setSize(w, h)` outside the render callback (which clears the WebGL drawing buffer), and `requestRender` waited on `rAF`/`afterDraw` without an immediate initial draw.\n   - *Fix Applied (unverified)*: Deferred `renderer.setSize` into `drawNow()` inside the render frame, drew immediately on mount after adding `initialRig`, replaced curved cylinder niche with clean architectural flat back wall + molding at `z = -2.4`, and added a 40-poll safety cap to `createAfterDrawScheduler` in `webglUtils.ts`.\n   - *IMPORTANT WATCHPOINT FOR ROUND 2*: If `r2-home-desktop.png` or `r2-museum-desktop.png` STILL shows blank or invisible `MeshStandardMaterial` meshes on Three.js `0.187.0` + SwiftShader, immediately suspect `PMREMGenerator` / `RoomEnvironment` interaction with `three@0.187.0` on SwiftShader (test whether `scene.environment` is causing NaN/black/discarded PBR shading or if `AvatarPreview3D`\'s second `useEffect([avatar])` disposes the initial rig before `requestRender` redraws!). Look closely at `AvatarPreview3D.tsx` lines 239-250: on initial mount, Effect 1 builds `initialRig` & calls `drawNow()`, then Effect 2 (`[avatar]`) immediately removes/disposes `initialRig` and calls `requestRenderRef.current?.()` (async `rAF`) \342\200\224 so verify the `r2` screenshot after `sleep 1` to confirm the sculpted avatar clearly renders!\n4. **Round 1 Medium Defect \342\200\224 `HomeStudio` Atelier card slightly exceeded 900px viewport height**:\n   - *Fix Applied (unverified)*: Tightened vertical padding/gaps in `HomeStudio.tsx` so the full 3D Avatar Preview stage + `Enter 3D Museum` CTA fit cleanly above the fold on `1440x900`.\n5. **Round 1 Low Defect \342\200\224 `THREE.Clock` deprecation warning in console**:\n   - *Fix Applied (unverified)*: Replaced `THREE.Clock` with `performance.now()` in `Museum3DView.tsx`.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Browser sessions are closed (`playwright-cli close` ran via `trap` at the end of Round 1).\n- The 4 Round 1 fix edits (`webglUtils.ts`, `AvatarPreview3D.tsx`, `Museum3DView.tsx`, `HomeStudio.tsx`) are saved on disk, **not yet compiled or restarted in the dev server**.\n- Ultra-mode verification round budget: Round 1 is complete; **1 remaining browser verification round (Round 2)** is permitted (max 2 rounds for initial build).\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Compile & Restart Dev Server**:\n   - Run `compile_applet`, then `restart_dev_server` (sequentially with `waitForPreviousTools: true`).\n2. **Execute Round 2 Full Verification in Playwright (`playwright-cli`)** (unique filenames `.playwright-cli/r2-*.png`, always `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`, max 4 screenshots):\n   - **Check 1 \342\200\224 Home & 3D Avatar Studio (`1440x900`)**: Open `http://localhost:3000`, wait 1.5s, capture `.playwright-cli/r2-home-desktop.png`. Verify the 3D sculpted Man avatar + marble pedestal + `Enter 3D Museum` button are clearly visible above the fold with 0 console errors.\n   - **Check 2 \342\200\224 Avatar Customization + Enter 3D Museum**: Switch to `Woman Model`, change outfit/hair, verify `data-gender=\"woman\"`, click `Enter 3D Museum`, wait 2s, capture `.playwright-cli/r2-museum-desktop.png`. Verify the grand 3D museum corridor renders clearly: veined marble floor, framed paintings with lights and plaques on opposing walls, customized Woman 3D avatar in center corridor, invited companion avatar (`Clara Moreau`), skylights, benches, and collapsible bottom dock.\n   - **Check 3 \342\200\224 Interactive Journeys (DOM Snapshots + Dynamic Wall Expansion + Date Sorting + Shared Access)**:\n     - Hold `KeyW` (`keydown KeyW`, `sleep 1`, `keyup KeyW`) to walk forward down the gallery.\n     - Click `Add Artwork`: verify empty submit displays validation errors (never bypassed); then select a sample artwork, enter Title `\"Evening Harbor Study\"`, Artist `\"Abid Sarker\"`, Date `\"2026-11-21\"`, submit -> verify artwork count increments `5 -> 6`. Add one more artwork (`\"Morning Studio\"`, Date `\"2024-03-10\"`) -> verify `data-artworks=\"7\"` and **dynamic wall expansion** `data-wings=\"4\"` (expands from 3 Wings / 6 wall slots to 4 Wings / 8 wall slots!).\n     - Click `Catalog by Date`: capture `.playwright-cli/r2-catalog-desktop.png` or verify via DOM snapshot that `2026-11-21` is first under `Newest First`, then click `Oldest First` and verify `2024-03-10` moves to the top! Click `Walk To Wall` on an artwork.\n     - Click `Share Access`: test granting access to `\"rafi@gallery.example\"` (`Rafi Ahmed`, `Man Model`, `Visitor`), verify `members-list` updates and `data-visitors` increments in the 3D museum.\n   - **Check 4 \342\200\224 Mobile Responsive Check (`390x844`)**: Navigate back to `/` (Home Studio) at `390x844`, capture `.playwright-cli/r2-home-mobile.png`, verify no horizontal overflow and clean stacked layout.\n3. **If Any High-Severity Visual/WebGL Issue Appears in Round 2**:\n   - Perform surgical fix (e.g., if `MeshStandardMaterial` has any SwiftShader `RoomEnvironment` artifact or camera framing tweak), re-run unit tests, and run final verification.\n4. **Final Mandatory Gate**:\n   - Run unit tests: `npx --yes tsx --test src/museum/layout.test.ts` (must pass 5/5).\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in the same turn (must both pass cleanly after the final edit).\n5. **Final Response**:\n   - Deliver a concise, scannable summary of My Museum\'s features, what was verified (unit tests, desktop/mobile viewports, journeys, and fixes made), and include the Firebase skill\'s humble reminder encouraging the user to review and harden `firestore.rules` before sharing the app broadly.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Ultra Mode**: Max 2 browser verification rounds total (we are on Round 2). Always inspect every screenshot/snapshot. Never finish on stale checks or unverified edits. Close browser cleanly (`trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`).\n- **Frontend Design Constitution**: Strict 3-zone top bar on Home, zero static pill badges on metadata, no `//` headers, no pulsing dots, no thick left borders, no `backdrop-filter` over WebGL canvas, collapsible bottom control dock in 3D view.\n- **Firebase Skill**: Never skip `handleFirestoreError`; if `firestore.rules` is ever modified, re-run `npx eslint firestore.rules` and re-deploy via `rpc_action(service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"DeployRules\")`; humbly encourage the user to review `firestore.rules` before broad sharing.\n- **Communication**: Action over talk, concise summary on completion, no internal step IDs or raw file paths in user-facing summary.\n</summary>"
