  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Fidelity**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with how the latest visual data materialized. Seeing the screenshots brought the architecture\'s beauty to life. Immediately, I zeroed in on the exact three visual flaws in the real renders, which have now been cataloged and flagged. The flaws, once rectified, would improve the visual experience greatly.\n\n\n**Refining Aesthetic Details**\n\nI have identified specific areas to refine, and I believe the solutions are quite manageable. The avatar hair\'s position needs adjustment to avoid the \"ski mask\" look by raising its y-axis position. The skirt geometry requires adjustment to prevent leg clipping. Both issues are related to the avatar dress.\n\n\n**Optimizing Avatar Appearance**\n\nI\'m focusing now on precise avatar styling. For male characters, I\'m ensuring a completely exposed forehead with a specific hair arrangement for crisp facial clarity. I\'m also addressing the female avatar hair to maintain a clear face frame, and I\'ve designed a dress with radius adjustments and tailored trousers/slacks underneath to prevent any leg clipping or geometry issues.\n\n\n**Improving Avatar Integration**\n\nI\'m now working to refine the avatars further. I\'m focusing on the shoulder and torso transitions for both male and female avatars. My goal is to ensure they look sleek and stylish in both turntable and 3D gallery settings. I\'m aiming for smoother deltoid capsules and tailored collar/lapel proportions to enhance their visual appeal.\n\n**Adjusting Visual Exposure**\n\nI\'ve identified a specific exposure issue with the `r2-museum-desktop.png` render. The North sculpture alcove and central marble floor appear washed out due to excessive brightness and potentially the `toneMappingExposure` setting. I\'ll tone down the ambient light, enhance the alabaster/stone contrast, and adjust the floor veining to improve visibility, particularly for the golden sculpture ring and nameplates.\n\n\n**Enhancing Render Visibility**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on architectural clarity. I\'m reducing the fog to sharpen the gallery vista, ensuring the far sculpture alcove is readable. Also, I\'ve scaled down the visitor nameplate sprite for a more elegant look, making sure it hovers gently above the head and does not dominate the overall scene. I will also make sure the 3D render loop is paused whenever a modal or drawer is open.\n\n\n"
