  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Design Details**\n\nI\'m struck by the quality of the \"man\" avatar; the crispness, the details in the attire, it\'s impressive. The structured blazer, belt, and gold plinth make it an elevated design. The editorial Home Studio above the fold is incredibly clean. Now, I will look at the other desktop image.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Render**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the rendering issue. The problem isn\'t with fog settings, but the canvas itself! It looks like the drawing buffer is either being cleared or never presented. Specifically, `preserveDrawingBuffer` is false, and timing issues with SwiftShader and `afterDraw` are likely the culprits. The Playwright screenshot is capturing a blank or incomplete frame. Now I see that `r2b-museum-desktop.png` shows a completely different render from `r2-museum-desktop.png`.\n\n\n"
