  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering The Culprit**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I\'ve pinpointed the reason for the transparent WebGL buffer in `r2b-museum-desktop.png`. The problem stems from line 1 of `Museum3DView.tsx`. This single observation reveals a critical cause.\n\n\n**Unveiling The Details**\n\nI\'ve got more clarity on the root cause! The `preserveDrawingBuffer` defaulting to `false` in the WebGLRenderer is key. When the WebGL loop pauses, Chromium\'s compositor clears the buffer to transparent. This explains the background color showing through when the catalog is open. I\'m also digging into the initial background color of the image after entering the museum, and exploring lines 604\342\200\223606 in `Museum3DView.tsx` against `webglUtils.ts`, to understand more, for our current problem set.\n\n\n"
