    thinking: "**Analyzing Renderer Mismatch**\n\nOkay, hold on. I\'ve hit a snag. I\'ve re-examined `Museum3DView.tsx`, lines 183-188, and also `AvatarPreview3D.tsx`, plus the Playwright output. Something\'s clearly off. My `gl.RENDERER` is `\"WebKit WebGL\"`, yet the `UNMASKED_RENDERER_WEBGL` is SwiftShader! This discrepancy needs immediate attention.\n\n\n**Investigating Frame Rendering**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the rendering loop in `Museum3DView.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m comparing the behavior of `r2` versus `r2b` and `r2c`. The crucial difference seems to hinge on `isPausedRef.current`. When it\'s paused, the render loop is skipped, which is the only difference. I\'m trying to figure out how this pause influences the renderer\'s pixel buffer. Something in that flow is changing the initial state of `glPx`. I need to figure out how.\n\n\n**Examining Script Differences**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously comparing the scripts used for `r2` and `r2b`, to isolate the factor influencing pixel buffer initialization. The timing and sleep duration appear to be the key differentiator, especially the delay before the first screenshot and navigating to the Museum. It\'s becoming clearer that the initial state of the render buffer might be affected by the timing and the way the initial screenshot is handled.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Culprit**\n\nI\'ve been going through the diffs between `r2` and `r2b` and I\'ve found something \342\200\224 the initial pixel color in `r2b` *is* a stark `#1C1917` black instead of the expected color! Now, I\'m carefully reviewing the file edits, specifically focusing on `src/components/Museum3DView.tsx`, lines 370-410, and also 591-596 and 563-589! I am comparing line 206 with lines 531, and I am reviewing `r2c`\'s `App.tsx` and the differences to `r2b`, which, for `r2b`, should *also* contain the React DevTools download console message. I\'m focusing on why the `gl.readPixels` in `r2b` returned `[0, 0, 0, 0]`!\n\n\n**Unveiling Glitch Causes**\n\nOkay, I think I\'m onto something. I\'ve re-examined the code, focusing on `Museum3DView.tsx` line 556 and line 531. I\'m now looking at why `gl.readPixels` could be returning all zeros after calling `renderer.render`. The scene\'s fog is a potential lead. I am going to try `http://localhost:3000/?autostart=1` and check the canvas styles, plus `gl.getParameter` and if `window.__tickCount` increments. I think there is a key difference.\n\n\n"
