  planner_response {
    response: "**My Museum** has been built as a full-stack 3D virtual art gallery and curatorial platform with Firebase Authentication, Firestore persistence, and procedural Three.js architecture.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n- **Home Page & Pre-Entry 3D Avatar Studio**:\n  - Sign in with Google (backed by Firebase Auth and Firestore persistence) or explore immediately in Guest Studio mode before entering the gallery.\n  - Customize your 3D visitor on a live 360\302\260 interactive turntable: switch between distinct **Man** and **Woman** 3D models, set your nameplate, and personalize skin tone, 4 gender-specific hair styles, hair color, 3 tailored outfits per gender, wardrobe/accent colors, and curator accessories (glasses, scarf, gallery pass).\n- **Walkable Neoclassical 3D Museum**:\n  - Explore a realistic marble-floored neoclassical corridor with architectural pilasters, skylights, velvet benches, brass picture lamps, framed works with museum wall plaques, and a focal bronze sculpture alcove.\n  - Walk with **WASD / Arrow keys** (or touch D-pad on mobile), drag to look around, toggle **3rd-Person / 1st-Person** view (`V`), switch wall finishes (`Alabaster`, `Travertine`, `Charcoal`), click any framed painting to inspect its details, and collapse the bottom control dock (`H`) for unobstructed viewing.\n- **Automatic Dynamic Wall Expansion**:\n  - Each gallery wing holds 2 opposing framed works; uploading additional images automatically expands the 3D museum corridor, adding new wall bays, columns, skylights, and benches without rebuilding your visit.\n  - Supports uploading your own photos (automatically compressed for reliable cloud storage) or hanging curated studio samples with frame styles (`Museum Brass`, `Dark Walnut`, `Matte Ebony`, `Minimal Gallery`).\n- **Complete Chronological Catalog (Sorted by Date)**:\n  - Open **Catalog by Date** from the Home page or inside the 3D museum to view all artworks grouped by date in **Timeline** or **Grid** view, switch between **Newest First** and **Oldest First**, search by title/artist/date, inspect or remove pieces, and click **Walk To Wall** to move your 3D avatar directly in front of any artwork.\n- **Shared Museum Access & Multi-Visitor Gender Avatars**:\n  - Grant access to others by email with **Visitor** or **Co-Curator** permissions and their **Man** or **Woman** 3D model, or share your museum\'s **Access Code** (`MUS-XXXX`) so invited guests can join and walk the gallery alongside you with real-time presence.\n\n### Verification & Polish Completed\n- **Logic & Build**: All 5 automated unit tests for dynamic wing expansion, alternating wall placement, collision clamping, chronological sorting, and input validation pass (`5/5`), alongside clean TypeScript linting and production build verification.\n- **Browser & Visual Checks**: Verified end-to-end across desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and mobile (`390\303\227844`) viewports with zero console errors, including Man/Woman 3D avatar customization, walking navigation, adding artworks to trigger dynamic expansion from 3 wings (6 walls) to 4 wings (8 walls), switching `Newest First` / `Oldest First` chronological catalog sorting, and granting access to a new visitor. Refined avatar hair forehead clearance, eliminated dress-to-leg clipping during walking, calibrated gallery lighting contrast, and ensured the 3D scene stays crisp while browsing modals and drawers.\n\n*Security note*: Firestore security rules have been validated and deployed for user-scoped and shared-museum access; please review and tailor your `firestore.rules` before sharing the application broadly in production."
    message_id: "gdIBa8CnGLO639IPuIPasAs"
    modified_response: "**My Museum** has been built as a full-stack 3D virtual art gallery and curatorial platform with Firebase Authentication, Firestore persistence, and procedural Three.js architecture.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n- **Home Page & Pre-Entry 3D Avatar Studio**:\n  - Sign in with Google (backed by Firebase Auth and Firestore persistence) or explore immediately in Guest Studio mode before entering the gallery.\n  - Customize your 3D visitor on a live 360\302\260 interactive turntable: switch between distinct **Man** and **Woman** 3D models, set your nameplate, and personalize skin tone, 4 gender-specific hair styles, hair color, 3 tailored outfits per gender, wardrobe/accent colors, and curator accessories (glasses, scarf, gallery pass).\n- **Walkable Neoclassical 3D Museum**:\n  - Explore a realistic marble-floored neoclassical corridor with architectural pilasters, skylights, velvet benches, brass picture lamps, framed works with museum wall plaques, and a focal bronze sculpture alcove.\n  - Walk with **WASD / Arrow keys** (or touch D-pad on mobile), drag to look around, toggle **3rd-Person / 1st-Person** view (`V`), switch wall finishes (`Alabaster`, `Travertine`, `Charcoal`), click any framed painting to inspect its details, and collapse the bottom control dock (`H`) for unobstructed viewing.\n- **Automatic Dynamic Wall Expansion**:\n  - Each gallery wing holds 2 opposing framed works; uploading additional images automatically expands the 3D museum corridor, adding new wall bays, columns, skylights, and benches without rebuilding your visit.\n  - Supports uploading your own photos (automatically compressed for reliable cloud storage) or hanging curated studio samples with frame styles (`Museum Brass`, `Dark Walnut`, `Matte Ebony`, `Minimal Gallery`).\n- **Complete Chronological Catalog (Sorted by Date)**:\n  - Open **Catalog by Date** from the Home page or inside the 3D museum to view all artworks grouped by date in **Timeline** or **Grid** view, switch between **Newest First** and **Oldest First**, search by title/artist/date, inspect or remove pieces, and click **Walk To Wall** to move your 3D avatar directly in front of any artwork.\n- **Shared Museum Access & Multi-Visitor Gender Avatars**:\n  - Grant access to others by email with **Visitor** or **Co-Curator** permissions and their **Man** or **Woman** 3D model, or share your museum\'s **Access Code** (`MUS-XXXX`) so invited guests can join and walk the gallery alongside you with real-time presence.\n\n### Verification & Polish Completed\n- **Logic & Build**: All 5 automated unit tests for dynamic wing expansion, alternating wall placement, collision clamping, chronological sorting, and input validation pass (`5/5`), alongside clean TypeScript linting and production build verification.\n- **Browser & Visual Checks**: Verified end-to-end across desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and mobile (`390\303\227844`) viewports with zero console errors, including Man/Woman 3D avatar customization, walking navigation, adding artworks to trigger dynamic expansion from 3 wings (6 walls) to 4 wings (8 walls), switching `Newest First` / `Oldest First` chronological catalog sorting, and granting access to a new visitor. Refined avatar hair forehead clearance, eliminated dress-to-leg clipping during walking, calibrated gallery lighting contrast, and ensured the 3D scene stays crisp while browsing modals and drawers.\n\n*Security note*: Firestore security rules have been validated and deployed for user-scoped and shared-museum access; please review and tailor your `firestore.rules` before sharing the application broadly in production."
