    thinking: "**Analyzing User\'s Request**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the Banglish request. My focus is on deciphering the user\'s intent: image saving after upload and 3D model movement through keyboard input within a museum setting. I\'m focusing on the implied workflow and constraints to extract actionable requirements, starting with image storage.\n\n\n**Verifying Guest Persistence**\n\nI\'m now investigating potential persistence issues in guest mode with local storage and Firestore, specifically focusing on upload saving. I need to confirm data reliability in both signed-in and guest modes. Next, I\'ll move on to confirming the 3D model\'s ability to navigate the entire museum via keyboard input, checking for any constraints within `Museum3DView.tsx`. Finally, I am doing Skill Checks.\n\n\n**Reviewing Key Processes**\n\nI\'m now revisiting core processes to pinpoint potential bottlenecks. The `ultra-mode` workflow is active and under review. I\'m focusing on the integration of Firebase, looking at `SKILL.md`, `src/App.tsx`, `src/services/museumService.ts`, and `src/components/Museum3DView.tsx` to ensure uploaded images are correctly saved (Firestore versus browser `localStorage`, with quota handling check), and diagnosing any responsiveness issues with keyboard-based 3D model navigation within the React app, particularly considering iframe/focus concerns.\n\n\n**Examining Input Handling**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into input handling. I\'ve pinpointed a key issue: without `e.preventDefault()` on arrow keys and spacebar, browsers may scroll or trigger buttons, interfering with the 3D model control. Further investigation shows that using `e.code` for WASD is sound, and checking both `e.code` and `e.key.toLowerCase()` strengthens keyboard layout resilience. I\'ve also implemented `window.addEventListener(\'blur\', clearKeys)` to prevent sticky keys. Finally, I\'m analyzing the camera movement within `Museum3DView.tsx`, with a sharp focus on how `clampPlayerPosition` in `src/museum/layout.ts` restricts player movement.\n\n\n**Investigating Player Movement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on player controls and camera restrictions within the museum environment. I\'m investigating player movement in `src/museum/layout.ts`, considering how to refine the camera clamping within the layout, particularly near the benches. I am looking into how tabIndex and auto-focus interact with key event handling. I need to make the walking experience more fluid, so users can seamlessly traverse and turn, with optional turning or strafing. I\'m also examining the best keybindings for walking, strafing, and turning based on standard museum user experience.\n\n\n"
