  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. Where Uploaded Images Are Saved\n- **When signed in with Google**: Uploaded photos are automatically compressed into optimized JPEGs (`<= 360 KB`) and saved permanently in your **Firebase Firestore** cloud database (`ai-studio-4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4`) under `museums/{museumId}/artworks/{artworkId}` (inside each artwork document\'s `imageUrl` field along with its title, artist, date, frame style, and notes). They stay synced across sessions, devices, and any visitors you share your museum with.\n- **In Guest Studio Mode (not signed in)**: Uploaded images are saved locally in your browser\'s `localStorage` on that device only. To keep them permanently in the cloud and share them with others, sign in with Google on the Home page.\n- A live **Storage** indicator is now shown directly inside the **Hang New Artwork** modal so you always know whether your upload is saving to Firebase Cloud or local browser storage, and a toast warning alerts you if local browser storage fills up.\n\n### 2. Full-Museum Keyboard Walking Fixed & Upgraded\nA bug that kept the 3D museum loop paused after entering has been fixed, and keyboard navigation has been upgraded so your 3D avatar can walk smoothly through every wing from the Entrance Foyer all the way to the North Sculpture Alcove:\n- **`W` / `S`** or **`\342\206\221` / `\342\206\223`**: Walk forward and backward (automatically glides around central velvet benches so you never get stuck).\n- **`A` / `D`**: Sidestep left and right along gallery walls.\n- **`\342\206\220` / `\342\206\222`** or **`Q` / `E`**: Smoothly turn left and right to face West/East paintings using only the keyboard.\n- **`Shift`**: Walk faster across long expanded wings.\n- **`V`**: Toggle between 3rd-Person (seeing your customized avatar walk) and 1st-Person gallery view.\n- **`H`**: Hide or show the bottom control dock.\n- Keyboard focus is automatically captured when entering the museum or closing modals, and arrow/space keys are prevented from scrolling or triggering focused buttons.\n\n*Reminder*: Since this app uses Firebase Firestore for persistent cloud storage and shared museum access, please review and tailor your `firestore.rules` before sharing the app broadly in production."
    thinking: "**Observing The Scene**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on the image, specifically `r3-final-verify.png`. The camera\'s path is visible! It enters \"Wing 1 of 3,\" passes the velvet bench, and turns left, perfectly mimicking `ArrowLeft`, finally viewing the framed paintings (`Alpenglow Over Glacial`). The level of detail and realism is astounding.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "mtkBa5zBCamsz7IPp-KKqAI"
    modified_response: "### 1. Where Uploaded Images Are Saved\n- **When signed in with Google**: Uploaded photos are automatically compressed into optimized JPEGs (`<= 360 KB`) and saved permanently in your **Firebase Firestore** cloud database (`ai-studio-4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4`) under `museums/{museumId}/artworks/{artworkId}` (inside each artwork document\'s `imageUrl` field along with its title, artist, date, frame style, and notes). They stay synced across sessions, devices, and any visitors you share your museum with.\n- **In Guest Studio Mode (not signed in)**: Uploaded images are saved locally in your browser\'s `localStorage` on that device only. To keep them permanently in the cloud and share them with others, sign in with Google on the Home page.\n- A live **Storage** indicator is now shown directly inside the **Hang New Artwork** modal so you always know whether your upload is saving to Firebase Cloud or local browser storage, and a toast warning alerts you if local browser storage fills up.\n\n### 2. Full-Museum Keyboard Walking Fixed & Upgraded\nA bug that kept the 3D museum loop paused after entering has been fixed, and keyboard navigation has been upgraded so your 3D avatar can walk smoothly through every wing from the Entrance Foyer all the way to the North Sculpture Alcove:\n- **`W` / `S`** or **`\342\206\221` / `\342\206\223`**: Walk forward and backward (automatically glides around central velvet benches so you never get stuck).\n- **`A` / `D`**: Sidestep left and right along gallery walls.\n- **`\342\206\220` / `\342\206\222`** or **`Q` / `E`**: Smoothly turn left and right to face West/East paintings using only the keyboard.\n- **`Shift`**: Walk faster across long expanded wings.\n- **`V`**: Toggle between 3rd-Person (seeing your customized avatar walk) and 1st-Person gallery view.\n- **`H`**: Hide or show the bottom control dock.\n- Keyboard focus is automatically captured when entering the museum or closing modals, and arrow/space keys are prevented from scrolling or triggering focused buttons.\n\n*Reminder*: Since this app uses Firebase Firestore for persistent cloud storage and shared museum access, please review and tailor your `firestore.rules` before sharing the app broadly in production."
