  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nWe are building and refining **\"My Museum\"**, a full-stack walkable 3D virtual art museum web app (React + TypeScript + Three.js + Firebase Auth & Firestore).\n- **Provisioned Firebase**: Project ID `bold-impulse-pkhlb`, Firestore database ID `ai-studio-4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4` (`/firebase-applet-config.json`).\n- **Active User Request (Current Turn \342\200\224 Banglish)**:\n  1. **Strict Per-User Database Isolation & Sign-Out Bug Fix**:\n     - Currently, images uploaded while signed in can still appear after signing out, and users must **only** see their own database images (never another user\'s museum unless explicitly granted access).\n     - Fix the fallback/storage mixing bug so signed-in users save strictly to their own Firestore museum (`museums/museum_{uid}/artworks/...`), never write to shared `localStorage` guest state, start private (`isOpenByCode: false`) with their own personal gallery, and signing out immediately clears all signed-in artworks/state so nothing from the signed-in account leaks after sign-out or into another signed-in account.\n  2. **Multi-Room Architecture (8 Walls Per Room + Automatic New Rooms)**:\n     - Replace the single continuous straight corridor with distinct **architectural museum rooms** where each room has **8 artwork wall slots** (`ARTWORKS_PER_ROOM = 8`).\n     - When a room\'s 8 walls are full and a 9th artwork is added, a **new distinct room** (with 8 more wall slots) is automatically added (Room 1: slots 0\342\200\2237, Room 2: slots 8\342\200\22315, Room 3: slots 16\342\200\22323, etc.).\n  3. **Interactive Doors Between Rooms + Keyboard Shortcut to Open/Close**:\n     - Every room connects via a real **3D double-leaf museum door** that blocks passage when closed and smoothly swings open (`rotation.y`) when opened.\n     - Provide a dedicated **keyboard key** (e.g., `F` or `Space`, plus clicking the 3D door) when near a door, with a clear on-screen prompt (`Press [F] or [Space] to Open Door`) to open/close doors and walk into the next room.\n  4. **Clickable Editable Room Name Signboard Above Every Door**:\n     - Mount a 3D architectural **Room Name Signboard** above every doorway displaying the room\'s name.\n     - Clicking the signboard above any door opens a modal to rename that room; saving updates the 3D signboard texture immediately and persists `roomNames` in Firestore (`museums/{museumId}.roomNames`) for signed-in owners (and local state in Guest preview).\n  5. **Distinct Room Shapes, Styles & Curated Flower Vases/Props Per Room**:\n     - Give each room a different architectural shape/style and unique centerpiece decor (cycling across 4 distinct designs: e.g., Chamfered Octagonal Rotunda with Celadon Porcelain Amphora & White Magnolias; Botanical Atrium Pavilion with Terracotta Urn & Olive/Pampas; Classical Salon with Cobalt Chinoiserie Vase & Crimson Peonies; Modernist Pavilion with Brushed Bronze Ribbed Vase & Orchids/Eucalyptus), plus distinct ceilings, skylights, floor inlays, and corner botanicals.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Already Completed & Verified in Earlier Turns\n- Full working React + Three.js + Firebase app: Home 3D Avatar Studio (Man & Woman 3D models with refined hair/dress/shoulders), walkable 3D Museum with keyboard walking (`WASD`/Arrows/`Q`/`E`/`Shift`/`V`/`H`) and `isPaused` fixed (`Boolean(inspectState.artwork)`), chronological Date-Sorted Catalog drawer, UploadArtworkModal with Storage destination banner, AccessModal, ArtworkInspectModal, 5 high-res generated fine-art assets in `/src/assets/images/`.\n- All earlier unit tests (`5/5` in `src/museum/layout.test.ts`), ESLint on `firestore.rules`, TypeScript lint (`tsc --noEmit`), Vite production build, and multi-round Playwright browser checks passed.\n\n### Skills & Reference Files Read\n- `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` (read this turn)\n- `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/references/firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md` (read lines 1\342\200\223260 this turn)\n- Previous turns also read `ultra-mode`, `frontend-design`, `threejs`, `computer-use`.\n\n### Completed So Far on Current Turn\n1. **Updated `/firebase-blueprint.json`**: Added optional `roomNames` (`type: \"object\"`, bounded map up to 30 custom room names keyed by room index) to the `Museum` entity.\n2. **Drafted `/DRAFT_firestore.rules`**: Added `isValidRoomNames(val)` (`val is map && val.size() <= 30`), allowed optional `roomNames` in `isValidMuseum(data)`, and allowed `incoming().diff(existing()).affectedKeys().hasOnly([\'roomNames\', \'updatedAt\'])` in `museums/{museumId}` `allow update` (owner only).\n   - **NOT YET LINTED OR DEPLOYED**: Must still run `npx eslint DRAFT_firestore.rules`, audit, copy to `/firestore.rules`, remove `/DRAFT_firestore.rules`, run `npx eslint firestore.rules`, and call `rpc_action(service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"DeployRules\")`.\n\n### Not Yet Modified (Planned for Immediate Implementation)\n- `/src/types/museum.ts` \342\200\224 Add `roomNames?: Record<string, string>` to `MuseumMeta`, add `RoomShape` type (`\'rotunda\' | \'atrium\' | \'salon\' | \'pavilion\'`).\n- `/src/services/museumService.ts` \342\200\224 Make new personal museums strictly private (`isOpenByCode: false`) and empty (`artworkCount: 0`, no shared seed photos polluting a new user\'s private DB), include `roomNames: {}`, add `updateMuseumRoomNames(museum, roomNames)` helper, ensure `mapMuseumDoc` maps `roomNames`.\n- `/src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Fix per-user isolation bug completely (see Section 3 & Section 6), add `cloudReady` / `cloudError` state so signed-in users NEVER fall back to or write to `guestArtworks`/`localStorage`, clear all state cleanly on sign-out, add `handleRenameRoom(roomIndex, newName)` handler.\n- `/src/museum/layout.ts` & `/src/museum/layout.test.ts` \342\200\224 Refactor pure procedural layout from corridor bays (2 walls/bay) to **Multi-Room Architecture (8 walls/room)** with `RoomDefinition`, `DoorDefinition` (between Room `i` and Room `i+1`, plus ceremonial entrance/end doors), 8 non-overlapping artwork wall placements per room (3 West + 3 East + 2 North-flanking or chamfered walls), door-aware `clampPlayerPosition(x, z, layout, openDoorIds)`, `findNearbyDoor(x, z, layout)`, `getRoomIndexAtZ(z, layout)`, `getDefaultRoomName(roomIndex, shape)`, and update unit tests (`node:test`) to cover 8-wall rooms, 9th-artwork room creation, closed-door blocking vs open-door passage, and room renaming validation.\n- `/src/three/proceduralTextures.ts` \342\200\224 Add `createDoorSignboardTexture(roomNumber, roomName, subtitle)` for high-contrast architectural gilded-walnut signboards above every door, plus distinct floor/accent patterns if desired.\n- `/src/three/museumBuilder.ts` \342\200\224 Build the **Multi-Room 3D Architecture** with 4 distinct room shapes/ceilings/floor inlays (`rotunda`, `atrium`, `salon`, `pavilion`), **4 unique procedural 3D flower vases & floral arrangements** (`LatheGeometry` vessels + stems + blossoms/foliage) + room decor, **interactive 3D double-leaf doors** with animated `leftLeafPivot` & `rightLeafPivot` returned in `BuiltMuseum.doors`, and **clickable 3D Room Name Signboards** above every door (`userData.renameRoomIndex`) added to `interactables`.\n- `/src/components/RenameRoomModal.tsx` (new) \342\200\224 Clean modal opened when clicking any 3D door signboard (or HUD rename button) to edit and save a room\'s custom name.\n- `/src/components/Museum3DView.tsx` \342\200\224 Integrate multi-room doors (smooth door swing animation in `tick`, `F` / `Space` keyboard toggle when near a door, clicking a door toggles it, door-aware collision clamping), clicking a 3D signboard opens `RenameRoomModal`, HUD displays active room name + nearby door prompt (`Press [F] or [Space] to Open/Close Door`) + nearby signboard hover hint (`Click signboard to rename ...`), auto-open connecting doors when teleporting via Catalog `Walk To Wall`.\n- `/src/components/HomeStudio.tsx`, `/src/components/UploadArtworkModal.tsx`, `/src/components/CatalogDrawer.tsx`, `/src/components/ArtworkInspectModal.tsx` \342\200\224 Update labels/copy from \"Wings (2 walls)\" to **\"Rooms (8 walls per room)\"** (e.g., `Room 1 \302\267 5/8 Walls`, `Creates Room 2` when adding 9th artwork), show Room Name in Catalog & Inspect modal, and show a clean loading/empty state for newly signed-in users.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Root Cause of Sign-Out / Cross-User Leakage Bug (`App.tsx`)**:\n  1. `App.tsx` lines 176\342\200\223185 fell back to `guestMuseum` / `guestArtworks` whenever `cloudMuseums.length === 0` \342\200\224 even while `user` was signed in! If `ensurePersonalMuseum` took a moment or failed, uploads wrote to `guestArtworks` (`localStorage`), which remained visible after sign-out AND to any other user before their `cloudMuseums` loaded.\n  2. `museumService.ts` line 151 defaulted new museums to `isOpenByCode: true`, which allowed `where(\'isOpenByCode\', \'==\', true)` list queries to read artworks across open museums. Changing default to `isOpenByCode: false` ensures strict privacy by default.\n  3. Newly signed-in users should NEVER inherit `guestArtworks` from `localStorage`. On sign-out, reset guest preview cleanly (don\'t carry over any signed-in uploads), and in Guest Studio Mode consider storing guest previews in memory/session or strictly separate from authenticated accounts while prompting clearly that signing in with Google saves to their private personal Firebase account.\n- **Root Cause of Earlier WebGL Issues (Already Fixed \342\200\224 Do Not Regress!)**:\n  - Keep `preserveDrawingBuffer: true`, `alpha: false`, `renderer.setClearColor(fogHex, 1)`, `isPaused={catalogOpen || uploadOpen || accessOpen || Boolean(inspectState.artwork)}` (NEVER `Boolean(inspectState)`!), and separate `window` blur key-clear from modal pause cancellation (`clearTimeout(frameId)`).\n  - Headless Chromium runs on SwiftShader (`detectSoftwareGl() === true`), so avoid `backdrop-filter` over WebGL and keep point lights capped (`<= 4` active lights tracked near the player\'s current room!).\n  - When rebuilding `Museum3DView` scene for multi-room expansion or room rename, preserve open door states (`openDoorIdsRef`) and player position!\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- Earlier turn: Fixed duplicate `trackMat` identifier in `museumBuilder.ts`.\n- Earlier turn: Fixed `Museum3DView` spawn camera behind South wall, `AvatarPreview3D` `ResizeObserver` buffer clear, `THREE.Clock` deprecation (using `performance.now()`), avatar hair forehead clearance, woman dress leg clipping (`DoubleSide` + flared `LatheGeometry` + `maxLegSwing`), and `Boolean(inspectState)` always-true `isPaused` bug that froze walking.\n- Earlier turn: Fixed `AccessModal` Playwright race (wait 300ms between clicking `Man Model` and submitting).\n- No unresolved build or test errors currently exist; `/DRAFT_firestore.rules` is newly written and awaits ESLint + deployment.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running on port 3000 (`DISABLE_HMR=true` \342\200\224 always run `compile_applet` and `restart_dev_server` after edits before browser testing).\n- `/DRAFT_firestore.rules` exists on disk (temporary file \342\200\224 must be linted, promoted to `/firestore.rules`, deleted, and deployed via `rpc_action`).\n- Browser sessions are closed.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Lint & Deploy Updated Firestore Rules**:\n   - Run `npx eslint DRAFT_firestore.rules`. If clean (exit 0), copy `/DRAFT_firestore.rules` to `/firestore.rules`, delete `/DRAFT_firestore.rules`, run `npx eslint firestore.rules`, and call `rpc_action(service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"DeployRules\")`.\n2. **Update Types & Firebase Service (`/src/types/museum.ts`, `/src/services/museumService.ts`)**:\n   - Add `RoomShape = \'rotunda\' | \'atrium\' | \'salon\' | \'pavilion\'` and `roomNames?: Record<string, string>` to `MuseumMeta`.\n   - In `museumService.ts`: set `isOpenByCode: false` and `artworkCount: 0` (empty private museum \342\200\224 no shared seed images!) + `roomNames: {}` in `ensurePersonalMuseum`; map `roomNames` in `mapMuseumDoc`; add `updateMuseumRoomNames(museum, roomNames)`. Also make sure `subscribeArtworks` / `subscribeAccessibleMuseums` strictly query by `ownerId == user.uid` for personal museum and `memberEmails array-contains user.email` ONLY for explicitly shared museums.\n3. **Implement Pure Multi-Room Layout Math & Unit Tests (`/src/museum/layout.ts`, `/src/museum/layout.test.ts`)**:\n   - `ARTWORKS_PER_ROOM = 8`, `ROOM_WIDTH = 16.4`, `ROOM_DEPTH = 18.0`, `DOOR_WIDTH = 3.2`, `DOOR_HEIGHT = 3.8`, `DOOR_INTERACT_RADIUS = 3.9`.\n   - Each room `r` (`0 .. roomCount - 1`) has:\n     - `index: r`, `shape: ROOM_SHAPES[r % 4]`, `centerZ: -r * ROOM_DEPTH`, `southZ: centerZ + ROOM_DEPTH / 2`, `northZ: centerZ - ROOM_DEPTH / 2`, `defaultName` (e.g., `Grand Rotunda`, `Botanical Atrium`, `Imperial Salon`, `Sculpture Pavilion`).\n     - **8 Artwork Wall Slots per room**:\n       - Slots 0, 2, 4 on **West wall** (`z = centerZ + 4.8, centerZ, centerZ - 4.8`)\n       - Slots 1, 3, 5 on **East wall** (`z = centerZ + 4.8, centerZ, centerZ - 4.8`)\n       - Slot 6 on **North-West flanking wall** (`x = -4.6, z = northZ + 0.14`, facing South `rotY = 0`)\n       - Slot 7 on **North-East flanking wall** (`x = +4.6, z = northZ + 0.14`, facing South `rotY = 0`)\n       - All 8 slots sit cleanly away from the center `x \342\210\210 [-1.6, 1.6]` South & North doorways!\n     - **Doors**: For every room boundary `r -> r + 1` (`r = 0 .. roomCount - 2`), create a `DoorDefinition` at `(x: 0, z: room[r].northZ)` connecting `fromRoomIndex: r` to `toRoomIndex: r + 1` with `id: \"door-${r}-${r + 1}\"`, plus a ceremonial Entry Signboard above Room 0\'s South entrance (`x: 0, z: room[0].southZ`) and North End Signboard/Portal above the final room\'s North wall so EVERY room (even Room 1 when there is only 1 room!) has a visible clickable Room Name Signboard above its doorway!\n     - **Door-aware Collision (`clampPlayerPosition(x, z, layout, openDoorIds)`)**:\n       - Allow player to walk freely inside any room, and across the wall between Room `r` and Room `r+1` ONLY if `|x| <= DOOR_WIDTH / 2 - 0.45` AND `openDoorIds.has(door.id)`! If the door is closed, stop smoothly at `door.z \302\261 0.85` so the closed 3D door physically blocks entry until opened with `F` / `Space` / click!\n       - Keep collision bounds around each room\'s central floral vase pedestal (`radius ~ 1.25m` at `(0, centerZ)`) with smooth edge-sliding in `Museum3DView`.\n   - Write comprehensive unit tests in `/src/museum/layout.test.ts` and run `npx --yes tsx --test src/museum/layout.test.ts` (must pass 100%).\n4. **Upgrade 3D Textures & Multi-Room Architectural Builder (`/src/three/proceduralTextures.ts`, `/src/three/museumBuilder.ts`)**:\n   - Add `createDoorSignboardTexture(roomLabel, customName, hint)` for crisp gilded-bronze & dark-walnut plaques mounted above every doorway.\n   - Rebuild `museumBuilder.ts` to construct each room according to its `shape` (`rotunda`, `atrium`, `salon`, `pavilion`):\n     - Distinct corner geometry (chamfered octagonal piers in Rotunda, arched column bays in Atrium, fluted pilasters & dark walnut wainscoting in Salon, architectural light fins in Pavilion).\n     - Distinct ceilings/skylights (circular oculus dome, vaulted skylight beams, coffered lantern, minimalist baffle skylights) and floor inlays.\n     - **4 Distinct Procedural 3D Flower Vases & Botanical Arrangements** on each room\'s central sculptural pedestal (plus corner potted plants):\n       1. Rotunda: Celadon porcelain amphora + white magnolia blooms & dark foliage\n       2. Atrium: Sculpted terracotta urn + olive branches & golden pampas plumes\n       3. Salon: Cobalt & gold chinoiserie baluster vase + crimson/blush peonies\n       4. Pavilion: Brushed bronze ribbed vase + sculptural white orchids & eucalyptus\n     - **Interactive 3D Double-Leaf Doors**: Partition walls between rooms with a real framed doorway opening (left wall segment + right wall segment + top lintel header \342\200\224 NEVER a solid wall covering the doorway!), hinged `leftLeafPivot` and `rightLeafPivot` with bronze handles, glass/walnut panels, `userData.doorId` on clickable door meshes, and a clickable **Room Name Signboard** mounted on the doorway lintel (`userData.renameRoomIndex = roomIndex`) on BOTH sides of the door (and above Room 1\'s focal portal/entrance)!\n     - Keep light count bounded (`<= 4` dynamic `PointLight`s repositioned in `Museum3DView` to illuminate the player\'s current & adjacent rooms).\n5. **Add Rename Room Modal & Update Interactive 3D View + App Isolation**:\n   - Create `/src/components/RenameRoomModal.tsx`.\n   - Update `/src/components/Museum3DView.tsx`:\n     - Track `openDoorIds` state/ref, animate door leaves smoothly (`0` closed \342\206\222 `Math.PI * 0.48` open) in `tick()`.\n     - Detect nearby door (`findNearbyDoor`) and display subtle prompt: `Press [F] or [Space] to Open [Room Name] Door` (or `Close Door`), plus an on-screen button for mouse/touch users.\n     - Handle `KeyF` / `Space` to toggle nearby door; handle raycast click on `userData.doorId` (toggle door) and `userData.renameRoomIndex` (open `RenameRoomModal` for that room!).\n     - Update HUD top-left placard to show active room name (e.g., `Room 1 \302\267 Grand Rotunda \302\267 5/8 Walls`) with a small pencil/rename button when `canCurate` is true, and update bottom keyboard hint (`WASD / \342\206\221\342\206\223 Walk \302\267 \342\206\220\342\206\222 Turn \302\267 F / Space Door \302\267 Click Signboard to Rename`).\n     - When `teleportTargetId` triggers `Walk To Wall` in Catalog, automatically add all doors leading to that artwork\'s room to `openDoorIds` so the player is never trapped behind a closed door!\n   - Update `/src/App.tsx`:\n     - Strict per-user isolation: track `cloudLoading` / `cloudMuseumReady`. When `user` is signed in, NEVER show or mutate `guestArtworks` / `guestMuseum`; show a clean loading banner until their personal Firestore museum loads, and clear all cloud state & reset guest preview cleanly on `handleSignOut`.\n     - Wire `handleRenameRoom(roomIndex, newName)` to `updateMuseumRoomNames` (Firestore when signed in, local state in Guest preview) and pass `roomNames` to `Museum3DView`, `CatalogDrawer`, `HomeStudio`, and `RenameRoomModal`.\n   - Update `/src/components/HomeStudio.tsx`, `/src/components/UploadArtworkModal.tsx`, `/src/components/CatalogDrawer.tsx`, `/src/components/ArtworkInspectModal.tsx` to display Rooms (8 walls/room), room names, and \"Adds Room N\" expansion messaging accurately.\n6. **Verify End-to-End (Unit Tests + Build + Lint + Real Browser Verification)**:\n   - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/museum/layout.test.ts` (all tests pass).\n   - Run `compile_applet` + `restart_dev_server`.\n   - Run Playwright (`playwright-cli` with `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`) to test and visually inspect screenshots:\n     - Room 1 visual quality (distinct Rotunda shape, central flower vase, 8 framed walls, clickable Room Name Signboard above doorway).\n     - Add artworks up to 9 artworks \342\206\222 verify **Room 2 automatically spawns** (`data-rooms=\"2\"`, 16 total walls, closed 3D double door between Room 1 and Room 2).\n     - Walk up to Door 1 (`KeyW`), verify closed door blocks walking through, press **`F`** (or `Space`), verify door swings open and player walks straight through the doorway into **Room 2** (different shape + different flower vase!).\n     - Click the Room Name Signboard (or Rename Room modal), rename Room 2 to `\"Botanical Sanctuary\"`, verify updated name renders on HUD & 3D signboard!\n     - Verify zero console errors and responsive layout.\n   - Final gate: co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in the same turn, restart dev server if needed, and summarize clearly with the humble `firestore.rules` review reminder.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Firebase Skill**: Always run `npx eslint` on `firestore.rules` after any edit and deploy via `rpc_action(service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"DeployRules\")`. Never skip `handleFirestoreError`. Include a humble reminder encouraging the user to review `firestore.rules` before broad sharing.\n- **Strict Per-User Isolation**: Signed-in users must ONLY ever see their own private Firestore museum (and museums explicitly shared with their email), `isOpenByCode` must default to `false`, and signing out must immediately hide all signed-in user uploads.\n- **Frontend Design Constitution**: Editorial museum aesthetic, zero static pills on metadata, no `backdrop-filter` over WebGL, collapsible bottom control dock, zero console errors.\n- **Ultra Mode**: Always run unit tests, inspect every Playwright screenshot, close Playwright cleanly (`trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`), and co-execute `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` before finishing.\n</summary>"
