  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Capturing Playwright Frames**\n\nI\'m now integrating Playwright with `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT` to ensure clean process termination. Screenshots are being saved for frame-by-frame visual inspection using `view_`. This comprehensive approach should allow for meticulous debugging.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "iuIBa7LBHc24mtkPkdfCuQY"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1732024410528979"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"bash -lc \'\\nset -e\\ntrap \\\"playwright-cli close || true\\\" EXIT\\n\\nplaywright-cli open \\\"http://localhost:3000/?autostart=1\\\"\\nplaywright-cli resize 1440 900\\nsleep 2\\n\\n# 1. Inspect initial Room I (Grand Rotunda)\\nplaywright-cli run-code \\\"async page => {\\n  await page.waitForSelector(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=museum-3d-view]\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(1200);\\n  const view = page.locator(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=museum-3d-view]\\\\\\\");\\n  const info = {\\n    rooms: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-rooms\\\\\\\"),\\n    currentRoom: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-current-room\\\\\\\"),\\n    artworks: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-artworks\\\\\\\"),\\n    playerZ: await view.locator(\\\\\\\"div\\\\\\\").first().getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-player-z\\\\\\\"),\\n    frames: await view.locator(\\\\\\\"div\\\\\\\").first().getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-frames\\\\\\\"),\\n  };\\n  console.log(\\\\\\\"ROOM1_INIT:\\\\\\\", JSON.stringify(info));\\n}\\\"\\nplaywright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/01_room1_rotunda.png\\n\\n# 2. Add 4 artworks (5 -> 9) to trigger automatic Room II creation\\nplaywright-cli run-code \\\"async page => {\\n  for (let i = 6; i <= 9; i++) {\\n    await page.getByRole(\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\", { name: \\\\\\\"Add Artwork\\\\\\\" }).click();\\n    await page.waitForSelector(\\\\\\\"#artwork-title\\\\\\\");\\n    await page.locator(\\\\\\\"button[aria-label^=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Use sample artwork\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\").nth((i - 1) % 5).click();\\n    await page.fill(\\\\\\\"#artwork-title\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Gallery Masterwork \\\\\\\" + i);\\n    await page.fill(\\\\\\\"#artwork-artist\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Curator Studio\\\\\\\");\\n    await page.getByRole(\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\", { name: \\\\\\\"Hang on Museum Wall\\\\\\\" }).click();\\n    await page.waitForSelector(\\\\\\\"#artwork-title\\\\\\\", { state: \\\\\\\"hidden\\\\\\\" });\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(350);\\n  }\\n  const view = page.locator(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=museum-3d-view]\\\\\\\");\\n  console.log(\\\\\\\"AFTER_9_WORKS:\\\\\\\", JSON.stringify({\\n    rooms: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-rooms\\\\\\\"),\\n    artworks: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-artworks\\\\\\\"),\\n  }));\\n}\\\"\\n\\n# 3. Walk North toward the connecting door between Room I and Room II (verify closed door stops player + prompt appears)\\nplaywright-cli run-code \\\"async page => {\\n  await page.keyboard.down(\\\\\\\"ShiftLeft\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.keyboard.down(\\\\\\\"KeyW\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(2600);\\n  await page.keyboard.up(\\\\\\\"KeyW\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.keyboard.up(\\\\\\\"ShiftLeft\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(450);\\n\\n  const view = page.locator(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=museum-3d-view]\\\\\\\");\\n  const promptVisible = await page.locator(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=door-prompt]\\\\\\\").isVisible();\\n  const promptText = promptVisible ? await page.locator(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=door-prompt]\\\\\\\").innerText() : \\\\\\\"NONE\\\\\\\";\\n  console.log(\\\\\\\"AT_CLOSED_DOOR:\\\\\\\", JSON.stringify({\\n    currentRoom: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-current-room\\\\\\\"),\\n    openDoors: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-open-doors\\\\\\\"),\\n    playerZ: await view.locator(\\\\\\\"div\\\\\\\").first().getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-player-z\\\\\\\"),\\n    promptVisible,\\n    promptText,\\n  }));\\n}\\\"\\nplaywright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/02_closed_door_signboard.png\\n\\n# 4. Press F to open the door, wait for smooth swing, then walk into Room II!\\nplaywright-cli run-code \\\"async page => {\\n  await page.keyboard.press(\\\\\\\"KeyF\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(700);\\n  const view = page.locator(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=museum-3d-view]\\\\\\\");\\n  console.log(\\\\\\\"DOOR_OPENED:\\\\\\\", await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-open-doors\\\\\\\"));\\n}\\\"\\nplaywright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/03_door_swinging_open.png\\n\\nplaywright-cli run-code \\\"async page => {\\n  await page.keyboard.down(\\\\\\\"ShiftLeft\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.keyboard.down(\\\\\\\"KeyW\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(1600);\\n  await page.keyboard.up(\\\\\\\"KeyW\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.keyboard.up(\\\\\\\"ShiftLeft\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(500);\\n  const view = page.locator(\\\\\\\"[data-testid=museum-3d-view]\\\\\\\");\\n  console.log(\\\\\\\"INSIDE_ROOM2:\\\\\\\", JSON.stringify({\\n    currentRoom: await view.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-current-room\\\\\\\"),\\n    playerZ: await view.locator(\\\\\\\"div\\\\\\\").first().getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-player-z\\\\\\\"),\\n    heading: await page.locator(\\\\\\\"h1\\\\\\\").innerText(),\\n  }));\\n}\\\"\\nplaywright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/04_room2_atrium.png\\n\\n# 5. Rename Room II via Rename Room dialog and verify HUD + signboard update\\nplaywright-cli run-code \\\"async page => {\\n  await page.getByRole(\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\", { name: \\\\\\\"Rename Room II\\\\\\\" }).click();\\n  await page.waitForSelector(\\\\\\\"#room-signboard-name\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.fill(\\\\\\\"#room-signboard-name\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Botanical Sanctuary\\\\\\\");\\n  await page.getByRole(\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\", { name: \\\\\\\"Save Room Name\\\\\\\" }).click();\\n  await page.waitForSelector(\\\\\\\"#room-signboard-name\\\\\\\", { state: \\\\\\\"hidden\\\\\\\" });\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(500);\\n  console.log(\\\\\\\"RENAMED_ROOM2:\\\\\\\", await page.locator(\\\\\\\"h1\\\\\\\").innerText());\\n}\\\"\\nplaywright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/05_room2_renamed.png\\n\\n# 6. Check console errors\\nplaywright-cli console error\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Verifying multi-room doors and signboards in browser\", \"toolSummary\":\"Run Playwright multi-room E2E test\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\221\003\n\216\003\001i\024}\0237\233\227\'\3604+X\225\275u\242\345\335I\333\027\a\267\247\364\005\246\343\351\205\227\326\276\342\360TgA\213\267Q\002c\033\267\226\036\000p\002K\214\314^\211b\344\320,_\300D?\240]~\306\315\211\242\277s\335\177\017Kmk\035:\200\276it\344T\232\254\376b\312\n\333\332\350\027\205a\332a\230\301R.\037dR\217@9\255\270\223\214\251\313\251\bP\341.\343\306sgy\323\201\365\037\'fqG\250\2604 \027\t\275\004\304E\245\332\026\373\2267:\220(/\032\265\315@\350x\264s\351\224\354`\034\374\276oj\f7X\357\245;\004\202\374\316{\337\205\221\255\035\326\247\366l\016\376\026A\206\344\027\235\224\275\033b\330?b{X\247\022\267&\231\270\fn\n~\346\261(\005\354X\263\333\320\276\020CoygA\326\210I\201\246d%\000\025&=E\372\004\274\220-\231\002\256\211]\004hZ\355->\332M\205\254P\215i\207\023y\215\023\240\214\\\223\023\341Q\314A\333\231\203\212\375\b\f\361\373\r\315!{qs\322\243tg\322\274\250\312\261C\a\217J\221\341T\226\'\217]\361\207\351,4i\241\223\t\030>\375\275\215\234\377\354\243\232|\\h^\f\020\353}P?\372V<\205\306km4PE\027\372\264`/\020\021\3473\273\200\205\026D\230Z\276\220\373\241\211\267\023N5*\356q\217\262\236\233z\370\250U\n\b\223\344"
