  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Visualizing Potential**\n\nI\'m incredibly excited! Examining `01_room1_rotunda.png`, I immediately identified three key visual enhancements we can implement. The level of detail is amazing.\n\n\n**Enhancing Readability**\n\nI\'ve been focusing on the \"Grand Rotunda\" signboard. The current lighting washes it out. To fix this, I propose adjusting the material properties. We can make the signboard darker and more emissive, using a roughness of 0.85, metalness of 0.0, and an emissive color of `0x2a2118` with an intensity of 0.45. This should make the gilded frame and lettering much clearer, or use a crisp MeshBasicMaterial.\n\n\n**Refining Texture Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the details. I\'m noticing subtle issues with the texture on the chamfered corner pilasters in `01_room1_rotunda.png`, and a quick fix is in order. We can avoid the diagonal shadow banding by giving each wall segment uniform plaster tiling and a warmer, richer alabaster tone, `\"#ECE6DC\"`, which will add some depth to the space. Also, I am now focused on why the player walks past the central pedestal when pressing `W` from `(0, 4.5)` using the `Museum3DView.tsx` code.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "KuMBa_6uGNutz7IPgYDPkQI"
