  planner_response {
    response: "I have fixed the per-user account isolation bug and upgraded **My Museum** into a multi-room architectural 3D gallery with interactive doors, custom door signboards, and unique room designs.\n\n### What Changed\n\n1. **Strict Per-User Private Database Isolation & Sign-Out Fix**\n   - Signed-in users now store and load artworks, room names, and visitors **exclusively** from their own personal Firebase Firestore museum (`isOpenByCode` now defaults to `false` for strict privacy, and new signed-in accounts start with their own empty private gallery rather than shared sample images or local guest data).\n   - Authenticated uploads no longer fall back to or write into browser `localStorage` guest state, preventing signed-in photos from appearing after signing out or across different Google accounts.\n   - Signing out immediately clears all authenticated cloud artworks/state and resets the local guest preview cleanly.\n\n2. **Multi-Room Architecture (8 Walls Per Room + Automatic Room Creation)**\n   - Replaced the single continuous corridor with distinct **8-wall rooms** (3 West walls, 3 East walls, and 2 North walls flanking the central doorway).\n   - Once a room\'s 8 walls are filled, uploading the 9th artwork automatically builds **Room II** (with 8 new walls), the 17th builds **Room III**, and so on.\n\n3. **Interactive Double-Leaf Doors + Keyboard Control (`F` / `Space`)**\n   - Adjacent rooms are separated by real partition walls with hinged 3D walnut-and-glass double doors that block passage while closed and smoothly swing open when activated.\n   - Walk near any connecting door and press **`F`** or **`Space`** (or click the door / on-screen **Open Door** button) to open or close it and walk into the next room.\n\n4. **Clickable Room Name Signboards Above Every Door**\n   - Mounted gilded architectural signboards directly above every doorway displaying each room\'s custom name.\n   - Click any 3D signboard above a door (or the pencil icon next to the room title in the top-left HUD) to rename that room. Custom room names save directly to your Firebase museum when signed in.\n\n5. **Distinct Room Shapes & Curated Floral Vase Centerpieces**\n   - Each room cycles through 4 unique architectural designs and sculptural 3D centerpieces:\n     - **Grand Rotunda** \342\200\224 chamfered octagonal corner piers, circular domed oculus skylight, brass floor medallion, and a **Celadon Porcelain Amphora with White Magnolias**.\n     - **Botanical Atrium** \342\200\224 glass conservatory roof trusses, corner potted olive trees, and a **Terracotta Urn with Olive Branches & Golden Pampas**.\n     - **Imperial Salon** \342\200\224 dark walnut wainscoting, coffered lantern ceiling, and a **Cobalt & Gold Chinoiserie Vase with Crimson & Blush Peonies**.\n     - **Sculpture Pavilion** \342\200\224 architectural oak light fins, linear twin skylights, and a **Brushed Bronze Vessel with White Orchids & Eucalyptus**.\n\n> **Security Note:** The updated Firestore security rules (including per-user privacy and custom room-name updates) have been linted and deployed. Please review `firestore.rules` before sharing your museum publicly with broader audiences."
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Result**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the output, and things look promising. Two rooms are defined, I\'m currently in room 1, the door \"door-0-1\" is open, and the heading is correct. Plus, the console is clean! This is a solid starting point.\n\n\n"
