  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Necessary Scope**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! Reading `workspace-integration/SKILL.md` was incredibly insightful. Now, the mandatory rules are becoming crystal clear. We need to implement the **Least Privilege Scope** principle. Our goal is strictly confined: beautifully formatted HTML invitation emails sent through Gmail. This is a critical first step.\n\n\n**Confirming Minimal Gmail Access**\n\nI\'ve narrowed the scope down: it\'s solely `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send`. Before setting up OAuth, I\'ll quickly review `/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/references/gmail.md` and `/src/firebase.ts` to check for existing scopes and best practices. Then, I will call `set_up_oauth` with specific parameters: the scope, a concise title (\"Use Gmail to send museum invitations\"), \"My Museum\" as the brand, and `userConfirmedInUI: false`. The key is to halt execution immediately after and await user confirmation, adhering to Section 6\'s response rules.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "q0gCa63PEPinmtkP6e_m2Ao"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_2321300778943731031"
      name: "view_file"
