  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nWe are adding **Real Gmail Invitation Emails with Direct Museum Entry Links** to **\"My Museum\"** (React + TypeScript + Three.js + Firebase Auth/Firestore + Google Workspace Gmail API).\n- **Active User Request (Banglish)**:\n  > \"ami jokhn invite korbo amr musuem e kauke je mail dbo sei mail address e shundr ekta mail ar amr musiuem e dhukar link access thakbe jeta diye se dhukte parbe amr musem e\"\n  - When the museum owner invites someone by email, a **beautifully formatted HTML email** must be sent to that email address via **Gmail**, containing a **direct entry link** (`/?invite=<museumId>&code=<accessCode>&museum=...&host=...`) and pass details so the invited person can click the link and directly enter the owner\'s private museum.\n- **Configured Resources**:\n  - Firebase Firestore DB: `ai-studio-4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4` (already provisioned, rules deployed).\n  - Google Workspace OAuth (`gmail.send`): **Already completed and confirmed** (`set_up_oauth` succeeded with `userConfirmedInUI: true` for project `gen-lang-client-0648146997`, project number `781174767330`, brand `Ashfaq Sarker Abid\'s Apps`, scope `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send`).\n  - Shared App URL: `https://ais-pre-joduy6dwiquofhbaal2niv-406307866378.asia-northeast1.run.app`\n  - Dev App URL: `https://ais-dev-joduy6dwiquofhbaal2niv-406307866378.asia-northeast1.run.app`\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed & Verified Earlier\n- Full multi-room 3D museum (8 walls/room, automatic Room II/III/IV creation, 4 distinct architectural room shapes + 4 procedural 3D flower vases, interactive hinged double-leaf doors opened with `F`/`Space`/click, clickable room-name signboards above doorways, strict per-user Firebase database isolation on sign-in/sign-out).\n- `firestore.rules` already enforces strict per-user privacy (`isOpenByCode: false` by default) while allowing `get` on `/museums/{museumId}` and `list`/`get` on `/museums/{museumId}/artworks`, `/members`, `/presence` whenever `request.auth.token.email in mData.memberEmails` (exact match for invited email recipients!).\n\n### Skills & References Read This Turn\n- `/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/SKILL.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/references/gmail.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md`\n\n### Completed Edits This Turn (Not Yet Tested/Compiled)\n1. **OAuth Setup Complete**:\n   - Called `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false`, received user acceptance (`user_confirmed_in_ui: true`), and immediately called `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: true` (`scopes_to_add: [\"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send\"]`, `project_id: \"gen-lang-client-0648146997\"`, `project_number: 781174767330`, `brand_name: \"Ashfaq Sarker Abid\'s Apps\"`). Succeeded.\n2. **Updated `/src/firebase.ts`**:\n   - Added `WORKSPACE_SCOPES = [\'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send\']` and `googleProvider.addScope(...)`.\n   - Implemented strict **in-memory** access token cache (`cachedGmailAccessToken`, never stored in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`), auto-cleared on `onAuthStateChanged` sign-out.\n   - Exported `signInWithGoogleWorkspace()`, `getGmailAccessToken()`, `clearGmailAccessToken()`, and `requestGmailSendToken()`.\n3. **Created `/src/services/gmailService.ts`**:\n   - `buildMuseumInviteUrl(baseOrigin, { museumId, accessCode, museumTitle, hostName })` -> generates `${origin}/?invite=...&code=...&museum=...&host=...`.\n   - `parseMuseumInviteFromSearch(search)` -> validates and parses incoming invite URL params (`PendingMuseumInvite | null`).\n   - `encodeMimeMessageBase64Url(mime)` -> UTF-8 safe RFC 4648 base64url encoder.\n   - `buildMuseumInvitationEmail(input)` -> composes a museum-editorial HTML + plain-text multipart MIME email with obsidian/gilded-bronze header, personal note box, credentials card (Invited Email, Access Level, 3D Avatar Preset, Museum Pass Code), primary **Enter {Museum} \342\206\222** CTA button linking to `inviteUrl`, fallback plain URL, and 3D controls footer.\n   - `sendMuseumInvitationEmail(accessToken, input)` -> `POST https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/messages/send` with `Authorization: Bearer ${accessToken}` and `{ raw }`.\n4. **Created `/src/services/gmailService.test.ts`**:\n   - Unit tests for invite URL round-trip, malformed invite rejection, HTML escaping & MIME formatting, and UTF-8/Bengali base64url encoding. **Not yet run.**\n5. **Updated `/src/services/museumService.ts`**:\n   - Added `fetchInvitedMuseum(museumId, accessCode?)` to resolve an invited museum directly from Firestore (`getDoc(doc(db, \'museums\', safeId))` with fallback to `findMuseumByAccessCode(accessCode)`).\n\n### Not Yet Modified (Remaining Work)\n1. **`/src/components/AccessModal.tsx`** \342\200\224 Upgrade invite flow with:\n   - Copy **Direct Invite Link** button right beside Copy Code.\n   - Optional **Personal Invitation Note** textarea in the invite form.\n   - **MANDATORY Explicit User Confirmation Dialog** (per `workspace-integration/SKILL.md` \342\200\224 sending an email on behalf of the user MUST show an explicit in-app confirmation dialog before calling Gmail API!):\n     - When owner submits the invite form (or clicks a **\"Send Email\"** button on any existing invited visitor row in the Authorized Visitors list), open an in-app **Confirm & Send Invitation Email** preview panel showing: Recipient Email, Subject, Museum Title, Direct Access Link, Pass Code, Personal Note, and an editorial visual preview of the invitation card, with explicit **Cancel** and **Confirm & Send Invitation Email** buttons (plus a secondary **Grant Access Without Email** option for Guest mode or manual link sharing!).\n   - Clean error recovery if Gmail token is missing/expired (clicking Confirm triggers `requestGmailSendToken()` inside the click handler so the popup is allowed).\n2. **`/src/components/HomeStudio.tsx`** \342\200\224\n   - Style the **Sign in with Google** button with the official 4-color Google \"G\" SVG icon (per `workspace-integration/SKILL.md` Section \"Authentication & UI\").\n   - Render a clean **Private Invitation Welcome Banner** when `pendingInvite` is active (showing `{hostName} invited you to \"{museumTitle}\"`, with a prominent **Sign in with Google to Enter** button when signed out, or **Invitation Accepted \342\200\224 Enter {museumTitle}** button once signed in!).\n3. **`/src/App.tsx`** \342\200\224\n   - Switch `handleSignInGoogle` to use `signInWithGoogleWorkspace()` from `./firebase` and clear token via `clearGmailAccessToken()` in `handleSignOut`.\n   - Parse `pendingInvite` on mount via `parseMuseumInviteFromSearch(window.location.search)`.\n   - When `user` is signed in and `pendingInvite` is present:\n     - Call `fetchInvitedMuseum(pendingInvite.museumId, pendingInvite.accessCode)`.\n     - If found: merge into `cloudMuseums`, set `activeMuseumId(found.id)`, clean the URL query string cleanly via `window.history.replaceState({}, \'\', window.location.pathname)`, keep an `acceptedInviteMuseum` banner (or toast + switch active museum) so the visitor can customize their Man/Woman 3D avatar and immediately click **Enter 3D Museum** (or jump straight in)!\n     - If denied/not found: show a clear helpful message (\"This private museum invite belongs to another email address. Sign in with the invited Google email or ask the curator to verify your email.\").\n   - Wire `handleGrantAndSendInvite` / `handleSendInviteEmail`:\n     - Uses `buildMuseumInviteUrl(window.location.origin, ...)`\n     - Calls `requestGmailSendToken()` (with retry once on 401 after `clearGmailAccessToken()`) and `sendMuseumInvitationEmail(token, ...)`.\n     - Note: in Guest Studio Mode (`!user`), `AccessModal` clearly lets the user grant guest access & copy the invite link, or sign in with Google to send real Gmail invitations!\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Mandatory `workspace-integration` Rules**:\n  - In-memory token caching ONLY (no `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` for access tokens). Done in `/src/firebase.ts`.\n  - Official Google \"G\" SVG icon on the \"Sign in with Google\" button.\n  - **MANDATORY explicit user confirmation dialog** before calling Gmail `messages/send` \342\200\224 never send an email silently without the user reviewing recipient/subject/link and clicking Confirm!\n  - Reuse existing Firebase `app` instance (do NOT call `initializeApp` twice). Done in `/src/firebase.ts`.\n- **Firestore Security Rules Compatibility**:\n  - `firestore.rules` already allows `museums/{museumId}` `allow get` when `request.auth.token.email in existing().memberEmails` OR `existing().isOpenByCode == true`, and `artworks`/`presence` list queries already filter by `viewerEmails array-contains user.email.toLowerCase()` when `isOpenByCode == false`. No `firestore.rules` changes are needed!\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- Earlier turn: Fixed SwiftShader screenshot timing by reducing point lights to 2 on software GL, removing transparent glass overdraw, raising `door-prompt` to `bottom-[116px]`, and tuning `afterDraw` to `105ms`.\n- No errors encountered on the current Gmail invitation turn so far (`set_up_oauth` succeeded cleanly).\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running on port 3000 (`DISABLE_HMR=true`).\n- `/src/firebase.ts`, `/src/services/gmailService.ts`, `/src/services/gmailService.test.ts`, and `/src/services/museumService.ts` have been updated/created and await UI integration (`AccessModal.tsx`, `HomeStudio.tsx`, `App.tsx`) + unit tests + build + lint + Playwright verification.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Run Unit Tests for `gmailService.test.ts` and `layout.test.ts`**:\n   - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/services/gmailService.test.ts src/museum/layout.test.ts` to verify all pure URL/MIME/layout tests pass.\n2. **Update `/src/components/AccessModal.tsx`**:\n   - Add `isSignedIn: boolean`, `inviteBaseUrl: string`, `onSendInviteEmail: (input: { email: string; displayName: string; role: MemberRole; gender: Gender; personalNote?: string; alreadyMember?: boolean }) => Promise<void>` props.\n   - Add **Copy Invite Link** button next to Copy Code.\n   - Add optional **Personal Invitation Message** field in the invite form.\n   - Add a **Confirm & Send Invitation Email** in-app confirmation modal/step (explicit confirmation dialog required by `workspace-integration/SKILL.md`) displaying Recipient Email, Subject, Direct Museum Link, Pass Code, and a clean visual preview of the editorial email card, with **Cancel**, **Grant Access Only**, and **Confirm & Send Gmail Invitation** buttons.\n   - Add a **\"Send Email\"** button next to the revoke trash button on each row in Authorized Visitors so the owner can also email any previously added visitor!\n3. **Update `/src/components/HomeStudio.tsx`**:\n   - Add the official 4-color Google \"G\" SVG icon to the **Sign in with Google** button.\n   - Accept optional `pendingInvite: PendingMuseumInvite | null`, `inviteStatusMsg: string | null`, and `onDismissInvite: () => void` props, and render a prominent, editorial **Private Museum Invitation Banner** at the top of the studio when an invite link is opened (`?invite=...&code=...`), allowing 1-click Google Sign-In to accept the invite or 1-click **Enter Invited Museum**.\n4. **Update `/src/App.tsx`**:\n   - Wire `signInWithGoogleWorkspace`, `clearGmailAccessToken`, `requestGmailSendToken`, `parseMuseumInviteFromSearch`, `buildMuseumInviteUrl`, `sendMuseumInvitationEmail`, and `fetchInvitedMuseum`.\n   - Handle incoming `?invite=...&code=...` links automatically for both signed-out visitors (shows banner prompting Google sign-in) and signed-in visitors (loads invited museum from Firestore, switches `activeMuseumId`, cleans URL query params, shows confirmation banner/toast).\n   - Handle `handleSendInviteEmail`: grants Firestore access if `alreadyMember` is false, obtains Gmail token via `requestGmailSendToken()`, sends the email via `sendMuseumInvitationEmail()`, retries once with a fresh popup token if Gmail returns 401, and shows clear toast feedback.\n5. **Compile, Lint, Restart Dev Server, and Verify End-to-End in Playwright**:\n   - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/services/gmailService.test.ts src/museum/layout.test.ts`.\n   - Run `compile_applet` + `restart_dev_server`.\n   - Verify in Playwright (`playwright-cli` with `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`):\n     - Open Home Studio (`http://localhost:3000/`): verify official Google \"G\" Sign-in button renders cleanly.\n     - Open `Share Access` modal -> verify **Copy Invite Link** button, fill out visitor invite (name, email, gender, role, personal note) -> click **Preview & Send Email Invite** -> verify the **Confirm & Send Invitation Email** preview modal renders with the exact recipient email, subject, direct link (`/?invite=...&code=...`), and editorial preview card! Take screenshot and visually inspect with `view_file`.\n     - Open a direct invite URL (`http://localhost:3000/?invite=museum_test123&code=MUS-742A&museum=Abid%27s+Museum&host=Ashfaq+Abid`): verify the **Private Museum Invitation Banner** renders cleanly at top of Home Studio with host name, museum title, and Sign in with Google button! Take screenshot and visually inspect with `view_file`.\n     - Verify zero browser console errors.\n   - Final gate: co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in the same turn, then present a concise summary to the user (including the humble `firestore.rules` reminder).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **`workspace-integration` Skill**: Never store OAuth access tokens in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`; always require an explicit user confirmation dialog before sending any email via Gmail; use official Google \"G\" branding on the Sign in with Google button.\n- **`firebase-integration-rpc` Skill**: Never skip `handleFirestoreError`, keep strict per-user isolation (`isOpenByCode: false` default), and include a humble reminder to review `firestore.rules`.\n- **Ultra Mode**: Run all unit tests, inspect every Playwright screenshot, close Playwright cleanly (`trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`), and co-execute `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` before finishing.\n</summary>"
