  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Config Flaw**\n\nI\'ve been examining the configuration files closely, and I\'ve made a key discovery. Specifically, after running `set_up_oauth`, the `/firebase-applet-config.json` file gets updated with `oAuthClientId`, which is critical for Google Workspace OAuth. However, it *also* omits `firestoreDatabaseId`. That\'s a problem, because our Firestore database ID is `ai-studio`.\n\n\n**Verifying Database Connection**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the Firestore database connection is established. It seems the code defaults to a specific database ID if none is configured. I\'ve re-examined the project ID and database ID, confirming their relationship. I\'m considering reading the `firestoreDatabaseId` from the config file if it exists, otherwise, falling back to a hardcoded default. This helps ensure we\'re always connected to the right instance, even without manual config changes.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "fVECa8j4AoL0z7IP0OKVgQ8"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_15007838205246073497"
