  planner_response {
    response: "**Real Gmail Museum Invitations & Direct Entry Links** are now live in **My Museum**:\n\n### What Was Added\n1. **Styled HTML Invitation Emails via Gmail**\n   - When you open **Share Access** and enter a visitor\'s name, email address, 3D avatar gender (Man/Woman), permission level (Visitor or Co-Curator), and optional personal note, clicking **Preview & Send Email Invite** opens a **Confirm & Send Museum Invitation** review modal.\n   - The confirmation modal displays the recipient, subject, direct entry link, pass code, and a live preview of the obsidian-and-gilded-bronze HTML invitation email before sending via your connected Gmail account.\n   - You can also click **Email** next to any previously added visitor in the Authorized Visitors list to preview and send (or re-send) their direct invitation email anytime, or use **Copy Invite Link** to share the link manually.\n\n2. **Direct One-Click Museum Entry Links**\n   - Every invitation email contains a prominent **Enter {Your Museum} \342\206\222** button and direct URL (`/?invite=...&code=...`) plus pass details and 3D navigation controls.\n   - When your invited friend clicks the link, **My Museum** greets them with a **Private Exhibition Invitation Banner** showing your name and museum title.\n   - Once they sign in with the invited Google email address, your private museum automatically unlocks and becomes their active gallery so they can customize their Man or Woman 3D avatar and step right inside.\n\n3. **Security & Privacy**\n   - Google OAuth tokens for Gmail are kept strictly in memory and cleared on sign-out, and no email is ever sent without your explicit confirmation in the preview modal.\n   - Private per-user isolation stays enforced: only invited emails can unlock your private museum. (As always, feel free to review your Firestore security rules whenever you adjust sharing behavior.)"
    message_id: "4VICa6SMA76f6dkP0NnmwAI"
    modified_response: "**Real Gmail Museum Invitations & Direct Entry Links** are now live in **My Museum**:\n\n### What Was Added\n1. **Styled HTML Invitation Emails via Gmail**\n   - When you open **Share Access** and enter a visitor\'s name, email address, 3D avatar gender (Man/Woman), permission level (Visitor or Co-Curator), and optional personal note, clicking **Preview & Send Email Invite** opens a **Confirm & Send Museum Invitation** review modal.\n   - The confirmation modal displays the recipient, subject, direct entry link, pass code, and a live preview of the obsidian-and-gilded-bronze HTML invitation email before sending via your connected Gmail account.\n   - You can also click **Email** next to any previously added visitor in the Authorized Visitors list to preview and send (or re-send) their direct invitation email anytime, or use **Copy Invite Link** to share the link manually.\n\n2. **Direct One-Click Museum Entry Links**\n   - Every invitation email contains a prominent **Enter {Your Museum} \342\206\222** button and direct URL (`/?invite=...&code=...`) plus pass details and 3D navigation controls.\n   - When your invited friend clicks the link, **My Museum** greets them with a **Private Exhibition Invitation Banner** showing your name and museum title.\n   - Once they sign in with the invited Google email address, your private museum automatically unlocks and becomes their active gallery so they can customize their Man or Woman 3D avatar and step right inside.\n\n3. **Security & Privacy**\n   - Google OAuth tokens for Gmail are kept strictly in memory and cleared on sign-out, and no email is ever sent without your explicit confirmation in the preview modal.\n   - Private per-user isolation stays enforced: only invited emails can unlock your private museum. (As always, feel free to review your Firestore security rules whenever you adjust sharing behavior.)"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
