  planner_response {
    response: "**Gmail Invitation Emails & Direct Museum Entry Links** are now live in **My Museum**.\n\n### What Was Added\n1. **Styled HTML Museum Invitation Emails (via Gmail API)**\n   - Open **Manage Access & Join Museum** (or **Share Access** inside the 3D museum), enter your guest\'s name, email address, 3D avatar gender (Man/Woman), permission level (Visitor / Co-Curator), and an optional personal note.\n   - Click **Preview & Send Email Invite** to review the recipient, subject, direct museum link, pass code, and a live preview of the obsidian-and-bronze invitation email card before confirming.\n   - Clicking **Confirm & Send Invitation Email** grants Firestore access for that email address and sends the formatted HTML invitation directly from your connected Gmail account (with an **Email** button next to every existing authorized visitor if you want to resend anytime).\n   - A **Copy Invite Link** button is also available right beside **Copy Code** for quick sharing.\n\n2. **Direct Museum Entry Experience for Invited Guests**\n   - Every invitation email contains a prominent **Enter [Your Museum] \342\206\222** button linked directly to your museum (`/?invite=...&code=...`).\n   - When your guest clicks the link in their inbox, **My Museum** greets them with a **Private Exhibition Invitation** banner showing your name, museum title, and pass code.\n   - Once they click **Sign in with Google to Enter** using the invited email address, your private museum unlocks automatically\342\200\224letting them customize their 3D Man or Woman avatar and walk straight inside.\n\n3. **Google Workspace OAuth & Security**\n   - Sign-in uses the official Google branding and keeps the Gmail access token strictly in memory (automatically cleared on sign-out, never stored in browser storage).\n   - *Note*: Before publishing to production, please take a quick look at your Firestore security rules (`firestore.rules`) to make sure the private access and invited-email permissions match your exact sharing preferences."
    message_id: "G1MCa_DBDe2LqtsPjNyN8QQ"
    modified_response: "**Gmail Invitation Emails & Direct Museum Entry Links** are now live in **My Museum**.\n\n### What Was Added\n1. **Styled HTML Museum Invitation Emails (via Gmail API)**\n   - Open **Manage Access & Join Museum** (or **Share Access** inside the 3D museum), enter your guest\'s name, email address, 3D avatar gender (Man/Woman), permission level (Visitor / Co-Curator), and an optional personal note.\n   - Click **Preview & Send Email Invite** to review the recipient, subject, direct museum link, pass code, and a live preview of the obsidian-and-bronze invitation email card before confirming.\n   - Clicking **Confirm & Send Invitation Email** grants Firestore access for that email address and sends the formatted HTML invitation directly from your connected Gmail account (with an **Email** button next to every existing authorized visitor if you want to resend anytime).\n   - A **Copy Invite Link** button is also available right beside **Copy Code** for quick sharing.\n\n2. **Direct Museum Entry Experience for Invited Guests**\n   - Every invitation email contains a prominent **Enter [Your Museum] \342\206\222** button linked directly to your museum (`/?invite=...&code=...`).\n   - When your guest clicks the link in their inbox, **My Museum** greets them with a **Private Exhibition Invitation** banner showing your name, museum title, and pass code.\n   - Once they click **Sign in with Google to Enter** using the invited email address, your private museum unlocks automatically\342\200\224letting them customize their 3D Man or Woman avatar and walk straight inside.\n\n3. **Google Workspace OAuth & Security**\n   - Sign-in uses the official Google branding and keeps the Gmail access token strictly in memory (automatically cleared on sign-out, never stored in browser storage).\n   - *Note*: Before publishing to production, please take a quick look at your Firestore security rules (`firestore.rules`) to make sure the private access and invited-email permissions match your exact sharing preferences."
