  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Admiring Architectural Clarity**\n\nI\'m struck by the clean modular design! The integration feels seamless. I\'m focusing on crafting an exceptional 3D signature model (abid_signature) with zero setup, exclusively for abidsarker213@gmail.com. We\'re aiming for top-tier craftsmanship, a 10/10 design to meet all requirements.\n\n\n**Refining Texture Details**\n\nI\'m deep in the weeds, getting the plaid texture *just* right!  I\'m focusing on the shirt, matching every visual detail of the video.  Specifically, I am recreating the textures, making sure to hit the deep burgundy, dark indigo plaid, and charcoal cross-stripes.  The goal is a realistic, tailored, untucked plaid shirt, complete with rolled-up sleeves and subtle button details.\n\n\n**Detailing Outfit Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the outfit elements! I\'m adding a dark charcoal-obsidian watch strap and slim rectangular watch face. Next, I\'m working on the ivory/off-white tailored chinos. I\'m focusing on getting the correct woven cotton roughness and tailored fit. Following that, I\'ll be detailing the charcoal-grey casual sneakers, ensuring the right canvas/suede upper and ivory-white rubber soles. Lastly, I will be working on the head and facial features.\n\n\n**Defining Facial Features**\n\nI am now focusing on the finer points of the face. Specifically, I\'m working on a clean beard on the chin and jawline, matching the reference frames. The hair will be thick, jet-black, and modern with a textured crown. I am matching all angles from the reference. I\'m also adding rose-silver metallic rectangular eyeglasses. The goal is to capture the details of the frames, nose bridge, lens tint, and temples.\n\n\n**Implementing Exclusive Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating an \"Upload Tripo .GLB (Optional)\" button directly into Abid\'s exclusive Signature Avatar Studio panel for easy `.glb` file import. The uploaded file is stored in browser IndexedDB (keyed to abidsarker213@gmail.com). I\'m automatically centering, normalizing height, enabling shadows, and calibrating PBR. If animations are embedded, they are played via `THREE.AnimationMixer`. Static Tripo meshes will use smooth dynamic walking motion, with an easy button to revert.\n\n\n**Defining Exclusive Avatar**\n\nI\'ve just created a helper module `/src/museum/exclusiveAvatar.ts` with relevant constants and functions. I\'ve defined `EXCLUSIVE_ABID_EMAIL`, `ABID_SIGNATURE_STYLE`, video, and Tripo source URLs, and implemented `isExclusiveAbidAccount` for email validation. Also, I\'ve created the `getAbidSignatureAvatar` function and am working on `enforceAccountAvatarPolicy`.\n\n\n**Enforcing Account Policy**\n\nI\'m now making sure that Abid\'s model is exclusive to him, as requested. I\'ve designed `enforceAccountAvatarPolicy` to enforce that only Abid can see his model. A public URL flag will not be implemented. Instead, I\'ll use unit tests and Playwright visual verification. I\'ll make sure to inspect Abid\'s model in Playwright to ensure the glasses, plaid shirt, rolled sleeves, watch, chinos, and sneakers look amazing.\n\n\n\n**Securing Inspection Method**\n\nI\'ve got a secure inspection plan! To verify Abid\'s model in Playwright without compromising security, I\'ll leverage a dev-only Vite module import in Playwright. This lets me render a headless snapshot of `buildAvatarRig` using `localhost:3000` via Vite, ensuring 100% strict exclusivity and comprehensive visual verification. I\'ll test it from all angles!\n\n\n**Integrating New Procedural Textures**\n\nI\'m expanding the toolkit! I\'m adding `createAbidPlaidTexture()` to `/src/three/proceduralTextures.ts` for high-res burgundy/navy plaid woven shirt canvas, making the shirt come alive. I\'ve also finalized IndexedDB persistence for optional `.glb` uploads in `/src/services/customModelStore.ts`, exclusively for abidsarker213@gmail.com. I\'m focusing on the integration with the avatar builder.\n\n\n\n"
    message_id: "A18Ca9vjD7uhz7IPpKvNqQI"
