  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Clean Separations**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the current modular structure of `/src/firebase.ts` and `/src/App.tsx`. My focus is now on designing a clean, rock-solid separation. I\'m starting by defining the `WORKSPACE_SCOPES` within `/src/firebase.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining Authorization Flows**\n\nI\'m now implementing distinct `GoogleAuthProvider` instances. The first handles basic sign-in, requesting only standard Google scopes for a seamless initial login. The second, which I\'ve called `googleGmailProvider`, adds the `WORKSPACE_SCOPES` for Gmail sending. I\'m focusing on ensuring users only grant the Gmail scope *when explicitly requesting* to send an email invitation, by triggering `reauthenticateWithPopup`.\n\n\n**Optimizing Gmail Integration**\n\nI\'ve discovered a brilliant method for Gmail integration. I can now avoid the \"Google hasn\'t verified this app\" warning completely during normal login by never asking for Gmail permission upfront. I\'m using `reauthenticateWithPopup` to request the Gmail send token only when the owner confirms and sends an email.  This approach leverages `login_hint` and `prompt: \'consent\'` on a new `GoogleAuthProvider` instance for reauthentication, ensuring a clean and secure authorization flow.\n\n\n"
