  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 4
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Application**: **\"My Museum\"** \342\200\224 a 3D architectural personal & shared virtual art museum built with React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Three.js, Firebase Auth + Firestore, and Gmail Workspace API.\n- **Core Project / Environment Identifiers**:\n  - User Email (Exclusive 3D Character Owner): `abidsarker213@gmail.com`\n  - Firebase / GCP Project ID: `gen-lang-client-0648146997` (Project Number: `781174767330`, Brand: `Ashfaq Sarker Abid\'s Apps`)\n  - Firestore Database ID: `ai-studio-4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4`\n  - Dev URL: `https://ais-dev-joduy6dwiquofhbaal2niv-406307866378.asia-northeast1.run.app`\n  - Shared/Preview URL: `https://ais-pre-joduy6dwiquofhbaal2niv-406307866378.asia-northeast1.run.app`\n  - Local Dev Server: Vite 8 on `http://localhost:3000` (`DISABLE_HMR=true`).\n- **All User Requests Completed Across Session**:\n  1. Full 3D multi-room museum (\"My Museum\") with Home Avatar Studio (Man/Woman 3D model customization), `WASD`/Arrow/D-pad walking, date-sorted Catalog Drawer, Artwork Upload, Shared Access & Live Multi-Visitor Presence.\n  2. Strict per-user Firebase cloud isolation (signed-in users see only their own private museum & explicitly invited museums; signing out hides cloud artworks and resets guest preview).\n  3. Multi-room architecture: 8 walls per room, automatic new room spawning when exceeding 8 artworks, unique room shapes & floral vases, interactive double doors (`F`/`Space`/click), and clickable gilded room signboards to rename rooms.\n  4. Real Gmail invitation emails with styled exhibition pass HTML + direct `?invite=<museumId>&code=<code>` unlock link & explicit confirmation preview modal.\n  5. **Exclusive Personal 3D Character Model locked strictly to `abidsarker213@gmail.com`** matching the user\'s uploaded Tripo 360\302\260 reference video (`/public/assets/aistudio/tripo-showcase-bca99e5e-94d8-4496-ae11-dab79a275a2d_2cd94ade.mp4`), plus optional `.glb` import persisted in IndexedDB.\n  6. **Fixed Dev Server startup/403 issue** (`server.allowedHosts: true as const` in `vite.config.ts`).\n  7. **Separated Basic Google Sign-In from On-Demand Gmail Send OAuth** so invited friends can sign in cleanly without requesting `gmail.send` scope, and guided the user through publishing their OAuth Consent Screen (`Testing` \342\206\222 `In production`) in Google Cloud Console (`gen-lang-client-0648146997`).\n\n## 2. Progress\n### All Code Changes Completed & Verified\n1. **Exclusive Personal 3D Character (`abidsarker213@gmail.com` ONLY)**:\n   - `/src/museum/exclusiveAvatar.ts`: `EXCLUSIVE_ABID_EMAIL`, `ABID_SIGNATURE_STYLE`, `ABID_SIGNATURE_VIDEO_URL`, `ABID_TRIPO_SOURCE_URL`, `isExclusiveAbidAccount()`, `isAbidSignatureAvatar()`, `getAbidSignatureAvatar()`, `enforceAccountAvatarPolicy()`.\n   - `/src/museum/exclusiveAvatar.test.ts`: 3 unit tests verifying case-insensitive email match, locking `abidsarker213@gmail.com` to `abid_signature`, and stripping `abid_signature` for guests & other accounts.\n   - `/src/services/customModelStore.ts`: IndexedDB (`mymuseum_custom_models_v1`) persistence for optional user-uploaded `.glb` (`saveCustomGlbForAccount`, `loadCustomGlbForAccount`, `clearCustomGlbForAccount`).\n   - `/src/three/proceduralTextures.ts`: `createAbidPlaidTexture()` woven burgundy/indigo tartan plaid `CanvasTexture` (`SRGBColorSpace`).\n   - `/src/three/avatarBuilder.ts`:\n     - `buildAbidSignatureRig()`: Seamless `LatheGeometry` untucked burgundy/indigo plaid button-down shirt, spread collar, front placket & buttons, rolled-up 3/4 plaid sleeves, bare golden-brown forearms, dark wristwatch on left wrist, ivory chinos, charcoal sneakers with off-white soles, sleek contoured jawline beard & moustache, textured black side-swept hair, and thin rose-silver rectangular glasses with flush temples.\n     - `buildCustomGlbAvatarRig()`: Loads optional binary `.glb` via `GLTFLoader.parse`, normalizes height to `1.76m`, grounds flush at `y = 0`, plays embedded walk animations via `AnimationMixer` if rigged, or applies smooth walk bounce/sway/lean in `animateAvatarRig()`.\n   - `/src/components/AvatarPreview3D.tsx` & `/src/components/Museum3DView.tsx`: Support `customGlbBuffer` (with cancellation guard & fallback to `buildAvatarRig`) and `isExclusiveModel` badge.\n   - `/src/components/HomeStudio.tsx` & `/src/App.tsx`: Conditionally show Abid\'s Exclusive 3D Model atelier card (with 360\302\260 Tripo reference video toggle and optional `.glb` import/reset) **strictly** when `isExclusiveAbidAccount(user?.email)` is true; guests and other emails see the standard Man/Woman studio with zero leak.\n2. **Vite 8 Cloud Run Preview Host Fix**:\n   - `/vite.config.ts`: Added `port: 3000`, `host: \'0.0.0.0\'`, `allowedHosts: true as const` to both `server` and `preview` blocks (preserving `DISABLE_HMR` settings).\n   - Verified `HTTP 200` on `localhost:3000`, `ais-dev-\342\200\246.run.app`, and `ais-pre-\342\200\246.run.app`.\n3. **Separated Basic Google Login vs. On-Demand Gmail Permission**:\n   - `/src/firebase.ts`:\n     - `googleProvider`: Basic `GoogleAuthProvider` (`prompt: \'select_account\'`, **zero** extra Workspace scopes \342\200\224 only standard `profile`/email login).\n     - `signInWithGoogle()`: Uses `signInWithPopup(auth, googleProvider)` for clean visitor login.\n     - `requestGmailSendToken()`: Lazily creates a Gmail-scoped provider (`WORKSPACE_SCOPES = [\'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send\']`, `prompt: \'consent\'`, `login_hint: currentUser?.email`), uses `reauthenticateWithPopup(currentUser, gmailProvider)` (or `signInWithPopup` if signed out), and caches the token strictly in memory keyed by `cachedGmailTokenUid` (cleared on sign-out or account change via `onAuthStateChanged`).\n   - `/src/App.tsx`: Updated `handleSignInGoogle` to call `signInWithGoogle()` instead of requesting Gmail scope on initial sign-in.\n   - `/src/components/AccessModal.tsx`: Clarified confirmation text noting Google will prompt once for Gmail sending permission if not yet granted.\n\n### Verification Outcomes (All Passing)\n- **Unit Tests**: `npx --yes tsx --test src/museum/exclusiveAvatar.test.ts src/museum/layout.test.ts src/services/gmailService.test.ts` \342\206\222 **15/15 passing** across 6 suites.\n- **Playwright Browser Verification**:\n  - Verified guest studio isolation (`hasExclusivePanel: false`), Abid\'s 3D signature model visuals across 3 iterative screenshot rounds (front 3/4, closeup, rear 3/4, mid-stride walk), museum `W`-key walking, and separated auth scopes (`loginScopes: [\"profile\"]`, `workspaceScopes: [\"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send\"]`), with **0 console errors**. Temporary `.playwright-cli/` screenshots were cleaned up.\n- **Build & Lint**: Co-executed `compile_applet` (Build succeeded) and `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit` exit code 0) after the final edits.\n\n### Skills Read in Session\n- `/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md` (+ `references/loaders.md`, `references/animation.md`)\n- `/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/SKILL.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md`\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Vite 8 `allowedHosts`**: Vite `^8.3.0` rejects requests whose `Host` header is a Cloud Run preview URL with `HTTP 403 Forbidden` unless `server.allowedHosts: true` (typed `true as const` for TS 7 compatibility in `vite.config.ts`).\n- **Google OAuth Testing Mode**: Project `gen-lang-client-0648146997` (displayed in GCP Console as `Default Gemini Project`) currently has its OAuth Consent Screen in **Testing** mode. We guided the user on their **Google Auth Platform \342\206\222 Branding** screenshot (`Developer contact information \342\206\222 Email addresses *` = `abidsarker213@gmail.com`, do NOT upload an App logo as that triggers mandatory verification, then click **Audience \342\206\222 PUBLISH APP \342\206\222 CONFIRM**).\n- **Separated Login Scopes**: Keeping `gmail.send` strictly on-demand inside `requestGmailSendToken()` means once the user clicks **PUBLISH APP** in Google Cloud Console, all invited friends can sign in via Google without encountering sensitive-scope verification warnings.\n- **Tripo Studio API**: Direct unauthenticated API download from `studio.tripo3d.ai` returns `401/1002 Authentication failed`, so Abid\'s zero-setup articulated procedural 3D model + optional `.glb` import covers both immediate usability and exact raw-mesh import.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **Abid 3D Model Visual Defects (caught in Playwright Round 1 & 2)**:\n   - *Boxy cheek beard flaps*, *horizontal z-fighting seam across chest from overlapping sphere yoke*, *squished hem stripes*, and *slightly perched shoulder caps*.\n   - *Fix*: Rebuilt shirt torso as a single smooth `LatheGeometry` profile from hem to collar, replaced boxy cheek boxes with a single flush lower-skull `jawBeardShell` sphere segment, aligned front placket (`z = 0.151`), and tucked shoulder pivots (`shoulderY = 1.398`, `shoulderX = 0.236`). Re-verified cleanly in Round 3 screenshots.\n2. **Dev Server Rejected Preview Host (`403 Forbidden`)**:\n   - *Error*: `Blocked request. This host (\"ais-dev-joduy6dwiquofhbaal2niv-406307866378.asia-northeast1.run.app\") is not allowed.`\n   - *Fix*: Added `allowedHosts: true as const` to `server` and `preview` in `/vite.config.ts` and restarted dev server; verified `HTTP 200` on localhost and both Cloud Run host headers.\n3. **TypeScript Error on `allowedHosts: true`**:\n   - *Error*: `vite.config.ts(7,29): error TS2769` \342\200\224 `boolean` not assignable to `true | string[] | undefined`.\n   - *Fix*: Narrowed with `allowedHosts: true as const`; `tsc --noEmit` passed cleanly.\n4. **OAuth Testing Block for Friends (`gen-lang-client-0648146997.firebaseapp.com has not completed the Google verification process`)**:\n   - *Root Cause*: `signInWithGoogleWorkspace()` previously requested `gmail.send` on every sign-in while GCP OAuth Consent Screen was in Testing status.\n   - *Fix*: Split `signInWithGoogle()` (basic profile/email only) from `requestGmailSendToken()` (on-demand `reauthenticateWithPopup` only when sending Gmail invitations) and provided step-by-step instructions to publish the OAuth Consent Screen in GCP Console (`Audience \342\206\222 PUBLISH APP`).\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- All code changes are built, linted, tested, and running cleanly on port 3000 (`HTTP 200` on localhost and preview hosts).\n- No pending code tasks or broken builds remain.\n- The user is currently in **Google Cloud Console** (`Default Gemini Project` / `gen-lang-client-0648146997`) following the 3-step instructions to save Developer contact email on **Branding** (leaving App logo blank) and click **Audience \342\206\222 PUBLISH APP \342\206\222 CONFIRM**.\n- User prefers concise, friendly Banglish/Bengali + English explanations matching their prompt language.\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n- Wait for the user\'s next message:\n  - If they share another Google Cloud Console screenshot (e.g., from **Audience** or **Verification centre**), guide them through confirming **PUBLISH APP** (or adding **Test users** if they prefer staying in Testing mode).\n  - If they request any new features, UI adjustments, or Firebase/database changes, remember to reload `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` whenever modifying Firebase/Firestore code or rules, and follow `ultra-mode` verification (unit tests, Playwright visual verification, co-executed `compile_applet` + `lint_applet`).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Strict Exclusivity**: NEVER expose Abid\'s exclusive 3D signature model (`abid_signature`) or custom `.glb` to guests or any email other than `abidsarker213@gmail.com`.\n- **Firebase & Workspace Skills**: Always load `firebase-integration-rpc` when interacting with Firestore/Firebase services; never store OAuth access tokens in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` (in-memory only, cleared on sign-out); always keep explicit confirmation UI before sending Gmail emails; never call `remove_oauth` unless actually removing `gmail.send` from code.\n- **No Unsolicited Code Edits**: When the user asks a console/setup question, answer clearly without modifying working code unless asked.\n</summary>"
