  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning Privacy Policy Creation**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a `/public/privacy.html` file for a clean privacy policy, hosted directly on the application domain. I plan to verify the rendering using `playwright-cli`, `compile_applet`, and `lint_applet` to ensure everything functions as intended. I\'m aiming for a concise verification process.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "faACa_znCLvQz7IP-MzWsA4"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14044451046089453231"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\" />\\n    <title>Privacy Policy \342\200\224 My Museum</title>\\n    <meta\\n      name=\\\"description\\\"\\n      content=\\\"Privacy Policy for My Museum, a private 3D virtual art gallery and exhibition platform.\\\"\\n    />\\n    <style>\\n      :root {\\n        --bg: #f6f3ed;\\n        --surface: #ffffff;\\n        --ink: #1e1c19;\\n        --muted: #666057;\\n        --accent: #8c6d46;\\n        --border: #e5dfd3;\\n      }\\n      * {\\n        box-sizing: border-box;\\n      }\\n      body {\\n        margin: 0;\\n        background: var(--bg);\\n        color: var(--ink);\\n        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", Roboto, Georgia, serif;\\n        line-height: 1.65;\\n        padding: 40px 20px 72px;\\n      }\\n      main {\\n        max-width: 760px;\\n        margin: 0 auto;\\n        background: var(--surface);\\n        border: 1px solid var(--border);\\n        border-radius: 16px;\\n        padding: 40px 36px;\\n        box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(30, 28, 25, 0.05);\\n      }\\n      .eyebrow {\\n        font-size: 12px;\\n        letter-spacing: 0.16em;\\n        text-transform: uppercase;\\n        color: var(--accent);\\n        font-weight: 600;\\n        margin: 0 0 8px;\\n      }\\n      h1 {\\n        font-family: Georgia, \\\"Times New Roman\\\", serif;\\n        font-size: 32px;\\n        font-weight: 600;\\n        margin: 0 0 8px;\\n        line-height: 1.2;\\n      }\\n      .updated {\\n        font-size: 14px;\\n        color: var(--muted);\\n        margin: 0 0 28px;\\n      }\\n      h2 {\\n        font-family: Georgia, \\\"Times New Roman\\\", serif;\\n        font-size: 20px;\\n        margin: 28px 0 10px;\\n        color: var(--ink);\\n      }\\n      p,\\n      li {\\n        font-size: 15px;\\n        color: #34302b;\\n      }\\n      ul {\\n        padding-left: 20px;\\n        margin: 8px 0 16px;\\n      }\\n      li {\\n        margin-bottom: 6px;\\n      }\\n      a {\\n        color: var(--accent);\\n        text-decoration: underline;\\n      }\\n      .footer {\\n        margin-top: 36px;\\n        padding-top: 20px;\\n        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);\\n        display: flex;\\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\\n        justify-content: space-between;\\n        align-items: center;\\n        gap: 12px;\\n        font-size: 14px;\\n        color: var(--muted);\\n      }\\n      .back-link {\\n        display: inline-block;\\n        padding: 9px 16px;\\n        border-radius: 999px;\\n        background: var(--ink);\\n        color: #ffffff;\\n        text-decoration: none;\\n        font-size: 14px;\\n        font-weight: 500;\\n      }\\n      .back-link:hover {\\n        opacity: 0.9;\\n      }\\n      @media (max-width: 600px) {\\n        main {\\n          padding: 28px 20px;\\n        }\\n        h1 {\\n          font-size: 26px;\\n        }\\n      }\\n    </style>\\n  </head>\\n  <body>\\n    <main>\\n      <p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">My Museum</p>\\n      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>\\n      <p class=\\\"updated\\\">Last updated: November 22, 2026</p>\\n\\n      <p>\\n        My Museum (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;our&rdquo;, or &ldquo;the App&rdquo;) provides a private 3D\\n        virtual museum where signed-in curators can organize artworks, customize avatars, and invite\\n        selected guests to explore their gallery.\\n      </p>\\n\\n      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>\\n      <ul>\\n        <li>\\n          <strong>Google Account Profile:</strong> When you sign in with Google, we receive your basic\\n          profile details (display name, email address, and profile photo) via Firebase Authentication\\n          solely to identify your private museum and verify invited access.\\n        </li>\\n        <li>\\n          <strong>Museum Content:</strong> Artworks, room names, gallery metadata, avatar preferences,\\n          and invite permissions you create are stored securely in Google Cloud Firestore and restricted\\n          to you and the guests you explicitly invite.\\n        </li>\\n        <li>\\n          <strong>Live Presence:</strong> When you walk inside a shared museum, your avatar position and\\n          display name are temporarily shared with other authorized visitors in that same museum.\\n        </li>\\n      </ul>\\n\\n      <h2>2. Optional Gmail Permission</h2>\\n      <p>\\n        Basic sign-in does not request access to your Gmail account. Only when a museum owner explicitly\\n        chooses to email an invitation pass to a guest does the App request the\\n        <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send</code> permission to send that single invitation\\n        email on your behalf after your confirmation. We never read, store, or scan your inbox, and the\\n        temporary access token is kept strictly in memory for the current session.\\n      </p>\\n\\n      <h2>3. How We Use &amp; Protect Data</h2>\\n      <p>\\n        Your data is used exclusively to run your virtual museum experience. We do not sell, rent, or\\n        share your personal information with third-party advertisers. All museum records are protected\\n        by Firebase Authentication and Firestore security rules.\\n      </p>\\n\\n      <h2>4. Your Choices &amp; Deletion</h2>\\n      <p>\\n        You may delete uploaded artworks, revoke guest access, or sign out at any time within the App.\\n        You may also revoke Google OAuth permissions at any time from your\\n        <a href=\\\"https://myaccount.google.com/permissions\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\n          >Google Account Permissions</a\\n        >\\n        page.\\n      </p>\\n\\n      <h2>5. Contact</h2>\\n      <p>\\n        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or want to request account data deletion, please\\n        contact the developer at <a href=\\\"mailto:abidsarker213@gmail.com\\\">abidsarker213@gmail.com</a>.\\n      </p>\\n\\n      <div class=\\\"footer\\\">\\n        <span>My Museum &middot; Ashfaq Sarker Abid&rsquo;s Apps</span>\\n        <a class=\\\"back-link\\\" href=\\\"/\\\">Return to My Museum</a>\\n      </div>\\n    </main>\\n  </body>\\n</html>\\n\", \"Description\":\"Add a standalone static Privacy Policy page at /privacy.html for Google Auth Platform OAuth branding and production publishing\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/public/privacy.html\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating Privacy Policy page\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create public/privacy.html\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\341\n\n\336\n\001i\024}\023E\036\016\266\3434\363\240b\'\353%5Q\375\237\027)o\362\224\201l\364\217\006_\363\0201@U\250CU\254\353\313\260\017\246\237\213\261,\342\254\367p\352\310I\3303\215\033{\035\326\251\364{\276\201\265\035u\356A9\213\305\320\260\367O\357{vA\276\345|\270\212\251\260\354\020F#\237p\240\315w\250\270\356\251\264\276\036\003o\3623\b\333\331-\362\355\245\305y=\0055\a\213\362\3348\033!W\334#\375\367\336eX\030vA\215\003\324\215\220\317\230G\322\325c#H\215t\206\347-\307~\234h-\366G\262\314J\205\331\245\330KY\343~\000\271I\331\245\234\020\022&\034\nE2\f+\334.\247=\203\255\365<\177\367J\307\a\333-\202\003\033a(\306\3404]\327\235\207R\300_\177\354\303e\354\004LiR\304\211\257\2654)\t\200\3250\333\320\322\350\245\347y\317]\357\335\371\321\262%L+\261\303q0\\c`\222R\222$%\367Y\335\\\204\375\340-aC\016\rF+\024\273\245b\331 uJ\b\317\343\372\323*?\027\202x\325#\333$\016\344!F\334\340S\260{.\260\2143\n`\320\3276C\227\002skv\245\312*\234eq\'Zf\027\352\030\276t\256\305zK\vj\033Z\241\272FZ\262F\330(W\207\230MS?B\023q\233\240\373\360\322C\313\034_\017R\250\377\242\375r\372j\201\335|}\261-F\220\336\227bX\240\\\004\341\331K\200\301\245\320j\367\303\n\227\312\2444\304y\355X\001j\236\034\022\027z_\353\307\327?\327\223\375\220\364Aw7\215P>\250\364);\\)\a\261\261ic87sX\274\345\252:\f\213\331^\231\3734k\036B?=yH;\a\303\330\356A\367\273&V\326\331\025\361\305\356\vW\200\203e\346\221K\224\377\26227HN\265%2\324\330\352\330\350\344\341\367\255w\270\030\207)P\365\364d\242j\365\022\001\020\000\250\216\242\232\fsQ\251\016\t\333\031\357\252\345\037\314\264~\343\024\347i\253r\256\336V\021G\234S\330\036p4p\310m\262\"\214\t^\370\204\261$\364a\237\265mD\230\365\261R@)\304wk\023.}G\313\\}\264\315h9y\316\230\337:\301\337\240\311N\201\261\357)P\253R\215\260\332\037{&\3044\344\313\325`\241 \367\321\273\204\227\315\211C\323\226\220S\343\006P\'J\035\263\304\343\343uOW\365\263_\n\277m2\224\333\251\341N\224\f\377\302\323 \203\260\244n\344\277\006\354\360\f\215G\366