    thinking: "**Analyzing Website Aesthetic**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with `/privacy.html`\'s design. The zero console errors and authentic typography feel spot on. The warm parchment aesthetic creates a welcoming, informative user experience. Clear explanations of Google Sign-In, Firestore, and the `gmail.send` function are crucial for transparency, and I\'m happy with how these are presented.\n\n\n**Clarifying Publication Steps**\n\nI\'m focusing now on streamlining the \"Publish app\" process. The key is making the instructions crystal clear, and providing all needed context. I\'m crafting a concise, copy-pasteable guide to unlock the \"Publish app\" button in 30 seconds. This includes explaining *why* the button is disabled (Branding page requirements), and highlighting the newly created `/privacy.html` page for easy URL input.\n\n\n**Defining Publication Steps**\n\nI\'ve got more steps outlined for the Branding page. I will provide application details (home page, privacy policy link), contact info and, surprisingly, to leave the app logo blank. I am explaining that then the user must click save and navigate back to Audience to press Publish App! I will provide bonus alternative instructions too.\n\n\n"
