    thinking: "**Analyzing the User Input**\n\nOkay, I\'m carefully dissecting this user request. I\'ve noted the email addresses provided and am translating the Banglish snippet, ensuring I understand the nuances of the intended action for these test users. I am making sure not to make any assumptions!\n\n\n**Defining Access Protocols**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the access protocols. My key focus is automating shared access for specific email addresses. I understand that the users associated with `abidsarker098@gmail.com` and `suraia475@gmail.com` must have immediate and comprehensive access to the museum owned by `abidsarker213@gmail.com`. This includes viewing, interacting with, and potentially contributing to the museum\'s content as soon as they log in with the specified emails.\n\n\n**Clarifying Museum Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how museum persistence impacts new users. Specifically, I\'m working to ensure that when `suraia475@gmail.com` signs in, if the museum owned by `abidsarker213@gmail.com` already exists in Firestore, they can immediately access it. I am verifying this functionality, even if the owner hasn\'t signed in yet. I am digging into how the `firestore.rules` and `museumService.ts` code handle pre-existing museum access for invited users.\n\n\n**Visualizing User Presence**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the 3D avatar behavior within the museum. I\'m focusing on the real-time synchronization so that I clearly see the avatar\'s active movement, and the subtle \"resting\" state for offline users. I am ensuring that the visual cues, like the avatar\'s state, are clear and intuitive.\n\n\n**Implementing Avatar Distinction**\n\nI\'m now implementing distinct 3D models. I\'ve committed that only `abidsarker213@gmail.com` receives Abid\'s signature 3D model. `suraia475@gmail.com` will receive a default female avatar, and `abidsarker098@gmail.com` will receive a default male avatar. I\'ll prioritize user customization as the next step.\n\n**Synchronizing Screen Rotation**\n\nI\'m turning my attention to camera synchronization with the avatar\'s movement. I\'m checking `src/components/Museum3DView.tsx` to verify if the camera currently rotates with the avatar when moving left or right, or remains fixed. The goal is to make the screen rotate seamlessly with the avatar\'s turns, providing a third-person follow-behind camera experience.\n\n\n**Refining Camera Control**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `Museum3DView.tsx` to ensure smooth third-person camera rotation with avatar movement. I am prioritizing a natural feel, like a real 3D exploration camera, where turning left/right rotates both the character and the camera smoothly. I need to make sure mouse drag can still orbit if desired, or smoothly follow the character\'s heading. I\'ll be reading `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` and `/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md` first.\n\n\n"
