  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Solution**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a comprehensive, robust engineering solution that addresses all three parts cleanly and modularly. The emphasis is on a rock-solid design. I\'m prioritizing modularity for scalability and maintainability.\n\n\n**Refining the Math**\n\nI\'ve been working on the pure math aspects, specifically around camera and player rotation. I\'ve got functions to normalize angles to the [-\317\200, \317\200] range, find the shortest angle difference, and compute forward yaw. The `stepPlayerSteering` function handles both camera and character yaw rotation, taking input and delta time into account for smooth movement and rotation. I\'m making progress.\n\n\n**Defining the Trust Circle**\n\nI\'m now implementing the museum\'s trusted circle in code. I\'ve defined Abid\'s trusted email circle with owner and pre-authorized members and helpers to manage the circle. The logic includes an owner and pre-authorized members. I\'m focusing on merging presence data. The owner and members\' roles, gender, and standby slot data are also included.\n\n\n**Implementing Presence Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the online presence logic. I\'m focusing on identifying active users by checking online status and recent heartbeat updates, excluding the current viewer. Standby 3D avatars are planned for the museum owner and trusted members without presence data, ensuring they stand calmly in a default position when offline. Additionally, I\'m ensuring Abid\'s signature 3D model is exclusively used for his email. I\'m also addressing how users select their initial museum, prioritizing Abid\'s shared museum for specific users. Finally, I will be working on Firebase Blueprint and hardened Firestore security rules to secure the system.\n\n\n**Securing Database Access**\n\nI\'m currently working on security rules for Firestore. I\'ve added optional, tightly-bounded fields to `VisitorPresence`, namely `email` (matching the authenticated user\'s email) and `isOnline`. This prevents email spoofing. I\'m ensuring full backward compatibility with existing data by maintaining the current `Museum` schema.\n\n\n**Defining Access Privileges**\n\nI\'m now implementing secure access for specific users to Abid\'s museum, even before Abid logs back in. I\'m focusing on allowing `suraia475@gmail.com` and `abidsarker098@gmail.com` immediate access to the museum, as well as read its content, while adhering to robust zero-trust security. I\'ve introduced a `isAbidCircleVisitor()` helper function within `firestore.rules` to facilitate this, and I\'m updating `canAccessMuseumData()` to account for these new access rules.\n\n\n**Refining Data Permissions**\n\nI\'m now revising the security rules based on the PII isolation principle to secure the data. I\'m focusing on restricting access to member emails and presence data in shared collections, particularly within Abid\'s museum. I will verify how to allow access by specific members from Abid\'s trusted circle to the member\'s data while keeping the sensitive fields private.\n\n\n**Implementing Member Keys**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a critical security enhancement. Storing raw emails in `/presence/{visitorId}` poses a privacy risk. To address this, I\'m implementing a non-PII `memberKey` instead, using a deterministic hash of the lowercase email (like an FNV hash) in `/presence`. This ensures zero email leakage, aligning with Pillar 6 and maintaining accurate member deduplication across systems, regardless of display names. I will be updating access rules to accommodate the change.\n\n\n\n**Enhancing Data Access**\n\nI\'m now implementing automatic addition of trusted members\' emails upon new logins, synchronizing them across various museum data locations for consistent access. I\'m also refining data access rules to include checks for `isOnline` and `memberKey` within the `isValidPresence` function, ensuring data integrity. I\'ve updated the `yaw` range in the firestore rules as well.\n\n\n**Refining Sync Logic**\n\nI\'ve optimized the presence data sync. I\'m now broadcasting presence updates more frequently at 260ms when moving/turning, only when significant changes in position or yaw occur, and sending keepalive heartbeats every 6 seconds when standing still. Upon leaving the museum, the system marks the user as offline, saving their last position for immediate visual feedback on other users\' screens. This gives the visitor\'s avatar an active or stand-still visual change, improving the quality of the live presence.\n\n\n**Optimizing Avatar States**\n\nI\'m now implementing distinct avatar states. I\'m prioritizing smooth interpolation of coordinates and yaw for active visitors, coupled with walking animations when moving. Active users will be indicated with an emerald-accented subtitle. Offline avatars maintain a still, upright posture at their last known position, marked with a muted stone subtitle, ensuring clear visual distinction for Abid and Suraia.\n\n\n**Implementing Avatar Behaviors**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing dynamic avatar behaviors in the presence model. I will be rebuilding avatars\' rigs when their visual styling or active state changes, ensuring smooth transitions without position jumps. I\'ve designed an automatic museum selection and switcher logic for trusted users. When `suraia475@gmail.com` or `abidsarker098@gmail.com` signs in, both their own museum and Abid\'s shared museum are fetched, and Abid\'s museum is set as active with a clear toast notification.\n\n\n**Verifying Navigation Flow**\n\nI\'m now writing tests to ensure smooth camera and player rotation in the application, including handling walk behaviors during turns. I will verify guest avatars stand calmly when in the museum, with clearly rendered nameplates, and zero console errors. I\'ll also add unit tests for `cameraSteering.test.ts` and `trustedCircle.test.ts`. I will also perform browser verification (`playwright-cli`) for camera and model rotations.\n\n\n"
