  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Parallel Modules**\n\nI\'m currently focused on constructing two independent logic modules, along with their respective unit tests. My attention is now on developing `/src/museum/cameraSteering.ts` and its test counterpart, `/src/museum/cameraSteering.test.ts`. Concurrently, I\'m working on `/src/museum/trustedCircle.ts` and `/src/museum/trustedCircle.test.ts`.\n\n\n**Verifying Angle Calculations**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the coordinate system of `Museum3DView.tsx` and have started scrutinizing the angle calculations within `cameraSteering.ts`. I need to ensure the accuracy of the world coordinate system, specifically regarding how the camera\'s yaw interacts with the forward and right unit vectors. My immediate focus is on the math for player and camera rotations, with emphasis on confirming the correct behavior when the player turns left. I\'m carefully double-checking everything.\n\n\n**Confirming Screen Rotations**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the camera\'s behavior, specifically focusing on how input actions affect the screen\'s rotation in relation to the 3D character. When the player turns left, I\'m verifying the counter-clockwise rotation, and when turning right, the clockwise behavior. I\'m checking that the camera\'s positioning relative to the player matches these rotations. I\'m also ensuring that the screen rotates smoothly in sync with the 3D character.\n\n\n**Refining Camera Control Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the camera control logic, specifically how the avatar faces the camera. I\'m focusing on the condition where `forwardIn` is negative and ensuring the avatar faces `-forward`, mimicking a classic third-person view where you see the avatar\'s front. Alternatively, I\'m exploring an approach where `camYaw` continuously rotates when `turnInput` is present, seamlessly rotating both screen and character. The key formulas are coming together.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Lb0Ca46lFo2lqfkPj92OmQ8"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14649775009512157179"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface SteeringInput {\\n  forward: number; // +1 (W / Up), -1 (S / Down), 0\\n  turn: number; // +1 (Left: A / ArrowLeft / Q), -1 (Right: D / ArrowRight / E), 0\\n  sprint: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SteeringState {\\n  camYaw: number;\\n  avatarYaw: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SteeringStepResult {\\n  camYaw: number;\\n  avatarYaw: number;\\n  moveDirX: number;\\n  moveDirZ: number;\\n  walkSpeed: number;\\n  animSpeed: number;\\n  isTurning: boolean;\\n  isMoving: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport const DEFAULT_WALK_SPEED = 4.8;\\nexport const SPRINT_WALK_SPEED = 7.4;\\nexport const CAMERA_TURN_SPEED = 2.05; // radians/sec when turning left or right\\n\\n/**\\n * Wraps any angle in radians strictly into [-PI, PI].\\n * Keeps Firestore presence yaw values bounded and avoids wrap-around jumps.\\n */\\nexport function normalizeAngle(angle: number): number {\\n  let a = angle;\\n  while (a > Math.PI) a -= Math.PI * 2;\\n  while (a < -Math.PI) a += Math.PI * 2;\\n  return a;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Returns the signed shortest angular delta from `from` to `to` in [-PI, PI].\\n */\\nexport function shortestAngleDelta(from: number, to: number): number {\\n  return normalizeAngle(to - from);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Computes the avatar Y rotation matching the camera\'s forward look vector (-sin(camYaw), -cos(camYaw)).\\n */\\nexport function computeForwardYaw(camYaw: number): number {\\n  return normalizeAngle(Math.atan2(-Math.sin(camYaw), -Math.cos(camYaw)));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Advances third-person / first-person player heading and camera yaw together:\\n * - Turning left (A / ArrowLeft / Q / mobile left) rotates BOTH camera & 3D avatar smoothly left.\\n * - Turning right (D / ArrowRight / E / mobile right) rotates BOTH camera & 3D avatar smoothly right.\\n * - Walking forward/back moves along the rotated camera axis so steering feels natural and cohesive.\\n */\\nexport function stepPlayerSteering(\\n  input: SteeringInput,\\n  state: SteeringState,\\n  delta: number\\n): SteeringStepResult {\\n  const dt = Math.min(Math.max(delta, 0.001), 0.1);\\n  const turn = Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, input.turn));\\n  const forward = Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, input.forward));\\n\\n  const isTurning = Math.abs(turn) > 0.01;\\n  const isMoving = Math.abs(forward) > 0.01;\\n\\n  // Rotate camera smoothly left/right whenever left/right steering is held\\n  const nextCamYaw = isTurning\\n    ? normalizeAngle(state.camYaw + turn * CAMERA_TURN_SPEED * dt)\\n    : normalizeAngle(state.camYaw);\\n\\n  const forwardX = -Math.sin(nextCamYaw);\\n  const forwardZ = -Math.cos(nextCamYaw);\\n\\n  const moveDirX = isMoving ? forwardX * Math.sign(forward) : 0;\\n  const moveDirZ = isMoving ? forwardZ * Math.sign(forward) : 0;\\n  const walkSpeed = isMoving ? (input.sprint ? SPRINT_WALK_SPEED : DEFAULT_WALK_SPEED) : 0;\\n\\n  let nextAvatarYaw = normalizeAngle(state.avatarYaw);\\n  if (isMoving || isTurning) {\\n    const baseFacing = computeForwardYaw(nextCamYaw);\\n    const desiredAvatarYaw =\\n      isMoving && forward < 0 ? normalizeAngle(baseFacing + Math.PI) : baseFacing;\\n    const yawDiff = shortestAngleDelta(nextAvatarYaw, desiredAvatarYaw);\\n    const yawLerp = 1 - Math.exp(-13 * dt);\\n    nextAvatarYaw = normalizeAngle(nextAvatarYaw + yawDiff * yawLerp);\\n  }\\n\\n  // Gentle foot-pivot stride animation when turning in place so the 3D model rotates naturally\\n  const animSpeed = isMoving ? walkSpeed : isTurning ? 1.65 : 0;\\n\\n  return {\\n    camYaw: nextCamYaw,\\n    avatarYaw: nextAvatarYaw,\\n    moveDirX,\\n    moveDirZ,\\n    walkSpeed,\\n    animSpeed,\\n    isTurning,\\n    isMoving,\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Add pure third-person camera and 3D avatar left/right rotation steering module\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/museum/cameraSteering.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating camera steering module\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create src/museum/cameraSteering.ts\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\305%\n\302%\001i\024}\023\221V\024\261\365G\363\221\3017\032}\224R)\340\322)\277m\024$\342\003\371\362\300\021\365\272\235\201\205ol\374\344sIr\225l\243\370\242o\354\310\327m\016Q\343\253d\020\257\372zaI\252+p\375\371\230\312\233^I`\ax\2129\333_\236\236,\351\365g+#\022\023lM\005\002\333v\3556\333\336Xo\313\350\0320H\037\204~[\263\320@\033\t\277\222\262\250_\300\031&>\312\272o\325M>\242ms9\337\025\271N\200\253F\224g\377<*\365\307y\355\343[m\205\021R@YqwD\023u\324q\321\350\2724\255M\336\017\373y\275Jr\005;\033@\312UT\364\204kX>\315\370\"=\243\245p\037\324\244O/\020\034H\364\214\vL\310\222\303\224\243\367Q\nV\000\006y\246|\323\276\274\264$=\312\006\\>\231\037\257\340\371(\355R\017#\263\3313\352K\332\245\016\0261\212\346\r\036\336M#;\2203\000\234T\254\260\343q~7k\3076\343kf\354\036\323\336\256\215\323\373\034\242b@\220>\205\233\371uWoo\240\344\330\250.\220\205\322\n\apE\230\224\237|\243\354)\224\260<\231\222Il2p\354\245\357o1\035G75\004\203\206\240\0028\3029\313h\3714\270\214a\237*j}\2115.\360\304\356\024\033:\337\273\'\037)}\274\230\325J\016\021\243\bMQ\374\026\324>\251\204\240\004-\003gZ\262L\377\t?|\274\373\372\377}\257r\250\200\250_\036\311;4\312F\332\344\302@\355RF\365\021\030\331\036^[\347\033\214\314\334!\255\273\232\n\363s\215mub\377Dj\320I\336\017@\377\367\334C\321\353\177\222J\232\226\227D\364\276\227e\306\207z\020RM\240\271\213\203\266\a\240~j\313\337\302\226\356f~\230\021\353\227\t\037\207\332\317E6pb\216\234\257\310kA\033\203N5\b\t%\366l\226\a\376zj\327\a\r\325\222\231\210h%\016\202=\376\245\023[Z\213\226\316(\353PA\232~p5\235\177)_\005\226\306fsW\276\n>s\213@$\252\244\260xF-{<\357\002\261\215\377\370\257L\221\352\017\203\264e\220\240\221\373\337\370k\360\016\025\251\024y\242\217h\344\263\"\225\251\322\217\023\025\215\207\340\234\253(\306Yrr\220f:r\241\344\032\254\002\222\2526<!\244\262\034J\202\017V\306\3753\002\017\241?\003X\346/\273~\371 \301\307\016\366\224r\206\262\241\226\363\000\304\215a8\227\252\206!\006\205\t%~\305\2