  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Celebrating Deployment Success**\n\nI\'m thrilled! The linter and ruleset deployment went flawlessly. Now, I\'m diving into the application code, specifically focusing on `/src/services/museumService.ts`. My initial task is to refine the `ensurePersonalMuseum` function, concentrating on user management and ownership within the application logic. I\'m taking a surgical approach, breaking down each logical segment into small steps.\n\n\n**Refining Member Management**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user access control within the museum service. For new museums, I\'ll initialize member emails, including deterministic member documents. For existing museums, I\'ll ensure trusted emails are present and sync artwork viewer lists to grant immediate access. Additionally, I\'m integrating logic to subscribe to a primary owner\'s museum for trusted visitors. This ensures quicker access upon creation, and for existing museums.\n\n\n**Implementing Real-time Updates**\n\nI\'m currently working on real-time data updates. I\'ve implemented a check within `subscribeArtworks` to ensure the primary owner and trusted Abid visitors always see all artworks. Also, I\'m normalizing the yaw value in `upsertPresence` for consistent 3D model orientation. I\'m also writing the `isOnline` status and the non-PII `memberKey` to maintain user presence. Finally, I\'ve added a function `markPresenceOffline` which calls `upsertPresence` with `isOnline` set to false, which allows the visitor\'s model to persist in the virtual world!\n\n\n**Enhancing Visitor Visibility**\n\nI\'m now refining real-time presence updates, focusing on enhanced visibility for the primary owner and trusted visitors. Within `subscribePresence`, I\'m implementing a check to ensure the owner or trusted Abid visitors see each other\'s presence. I\'m also parsing `isOnline`, `memberKey`, and `updatedAt` for proper presence data. I\'m taking a surgical approach, making it easy to create an appropriate avatar and nameplate for all museum visitors!\n\nI\'m also working on `createNameplateTexture` in `proceduralTextures.ts`, and I\'m adding static color options for `ACTIVE \302\267 LIVE` and `STANDING \302\267 OFFLINE`. I\'m also adding `subtitle` and `statusTone` to `buildAvatarRig` in `avatarBuilder.ts` to improve the avatar\'s appearance!\n\n\n**Refining Avatar Animation**\n\nI\'m now focused on avatar animation for clear online/offline status indication. I\'m adding `ACTIVE \302\267 LIVE` and `STANDING \302\267 OFFLINE` status to the companion avatars. In `animateAvatarRig`, I\'m making standing offline avatars stand straight by setting limb rotations and body position to zero. Finally, I\'m integrating camera steering, utilizing `stepPlayerSteering` to synchronize both camera and 3D character rotation for a smoother experience.\n\n\n**Updating Companion Avatars**\n\nI\'m now implementing persistent standing vs. active live companion models. I\'m replacing the old `companionVisitors` and patrol logic with `resolveMuseumCompanionAvatars(...)`. I\'ve added a lightweight 5-second `presenceClock` interval for automatic status transitions from `ACTIVE` to `STANDING`. Now, for each companion avatar, I\'m smoothly interpolating position and yaw and playing the walking animation when moving. I\'m leveraging `shortestAngleDelta` to correct the 360-degree wrap bug in the process!\n\n\n**Improving Presence Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on persistence for visitors within the virtual museum space. If a visitor is offline, I\'ll hold their exact position and orientation, ensuring the `animateAvatarRig` function sets their limbs to zero and body position to zero. To improve live broadcast performance, I will broadcast position, rotation, and an online status every 260ms when the player moves or turns, and use a heartbeat every 6000ms. I\'m also tracking last broadcast position to accurately mark visitors as offline upon leaving the museum. I\'m also adding a static live status indicator on the top left of the UI!\n\n\n"
    message_id: "58ACa4iAF9yA694P1prRwQI"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1779252516843243032"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Support Abid trusted circle auto-access, shared artwork/presence queries, and persistent online/offline standing presence in museumService.ts\", \"Instruction\":\"Update museumService.ts imports, ensurePersonalMuseum, subscribeAccessibleMuseums, subscribeArtworks, upsertPresence, markPresenceOffline, and subscribePresence\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":33, \"ReplacementContent\":\"import { CURATED_SAMPLES } from \'../data/seedMuseum\';\\nimport { generateAccessCode } from \'../museum/layout\';\\nimport { normalizeAngle } from \'../museum/cameraSteering\';\\nimport {\\n  ABID_PRIMARY_OWNER_UID,\\n  computeMemberKey,\\n  getDefaultTrustedMembersForOwner,\\n  isAbidMuseum,\\n  isTrustedAbidVisitorEmail,\\n} from \'../museum/trustedCircle\';\", \"StartLine\":30, \"TargetContent\":\"import { CURATED_SAMPLES } from \'../data/seedMuseum\';\\nimport { generateAccessCode } from \'../museum/layout\';\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":190, \"ReplacementContent\":\"export async function ensurePersonalMuseum(\\n  user: User,\\n  ownerName: string\\n): Promise<MuseumMeta> {\\n  const museumId = sanitizeId(`museum_${user.uid}`);\\n  const museumPath = `museums/${museumId}`;\\n  let opType = OperationType.GET;\\n  const trustedSeeds = getDefaultTrustedMembersForOwner(user.email);\\n  const trustedEmails = trustedSeeds.map((m) => m.email.toLowerCase());\\n\\n  try {\\n    const snap = await getDoc(doc(db, \'museums\', museumId));\\n    if (snap.exists()) {\\n      const existingMuseum = mapMuseumDoc(snap.id, snap.data());\\n\\n      // Automatically ensure pre-authorized trusted circle emails are registered on Abid\'s museum\\n      if (trustedSeeds.length > 0 && user.emailVerified) {\\n        const existingLower = new Set(existingMuseum.memberEmails.map((e) => e.toLowerCase()));\\n        const missingSeeds = trustedSeeds.filter((s) => !existingLower.has(s.email.toLowerCase()));\\n        if (missingSeeds.length > 0) {\\n          const nextMembers = Array.from(\\n            new Set([...existingMuseum.memberEmails.map((e) => e.toLowerCase()), ...trustedEmails])\\n          ).slice(0, 10);\\n          try {\\n            const batch = writeBatch(db);\\n            for (const seed of missingSeeds) {\\n              batch.set(doc(db, \'museums\', museumId, \'members\', seed.id), {\\n                museumId,\\n                ownerId: user.uid,\\n                email: seed.email.toLowerCase(),\\n                displayName: seed.displayName,\\n                role: seed.role,\\n                gender: seed.gender,\\n                createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n              });\\n            }\\n            batch.update(doc(db, \'museums\', museumId), {\\n              memberEmails: nextMembers,\\n              curatorEmails: existingMuseum.curatorEmails,\\n              updatedAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n            });\\n            await batch.commit();\\n            await syncArtworkViewerLists(\\n              museumId,\\n              user.uid,\\n              existingMuseum.isOpenByCode,\\n              nextMembers\\n            );\\n            return { ...existingMuseum, memberEmails: nextMembers };\\n          } catch (syncErr) {\\n            console.warn(\'Trusted circle sync skipped:\', syncErr);\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n      return existingMuseum;\\n    }\\n\\n    opType = OperationType.CREATE;\\n    const safeOwner = (ownerName || user.displayName || \'Curator\').trim().slice(0, 80);\\n    const accessCode = generateAccessCode(user.uid);\\n    const title = `${safeOwner.split(\' \')[0]}\'s Museum`.slice(0, 100);\\n    const description =\\n      \'Personal 3D architectural gallery showcasing curated artworks and chronological photographic memories.\';\\n\\n    const batch = writeBatch(db);\\n    const museumRef = doc(db, \'museums\', museumId);\\n    batch.set(museumRef, {\\n      ownerId: user.uid,\\n      ownerName: safeOwner,\\n      title,\\n      description,\\n      accessCode,\\n      wallTheme: \'alabaster\',\\n      isOpenByCode: false,\\n      memberEmails: trustedEmails.slice(0, 10),\\n      curatorEmails: [],\\n      artworkCount: 0,\\n      roomNames: {},\\n      createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n      updatedAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n    });\\n\\n    const codeRef = doc(db, \'museumCodes\', accessCode);\\n    batch.set(codeRef, {\\n      accessCode,\\n      museumId,\\n      ownerId: user.uid,\\n      title,\\n      createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n    });\\n\\n    await batch.commit();\\n\\n    // Seed trusted member records after parent museum exists (satisfies Master Gate rule)\\n    if (trustedSeeds.length > 0 && user.emailVerified) {\\n      try {\\n        const memBatch = writeBatch(db);\\n        for (const seed of trustedSeeds) {\\n          memBatch.set(doc(db, \'museums\', museumId, \'members\', seed.id), {\\n            museumId,\\n            ownerId: user.uid,\\n            email: seed.email.toLowerCase(),\\n            displayName: seed.displayName,\\n            role: seed.role,\\n            gender: seed.gender,\\n            createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n          });\\n        }\\n        await memBatch.commit();\\n      } catch (seedErr) {\\n        console.warn(\'Trusted member seed skipped:\', seedErr);\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    return {\\n      id: museumId,\\n      ownerId: user.uid,\\n      ownerName: safeOwner,\\n      title,\\n      description,\\n      accessCode,\\n      wallTheme: \'alabaster\',\\n      isOpenByCode: false,\\n      memberEmails: trustedEmails.slice(0, 10),\\n      curatorEmails: [],\\n      artworkCount: 0,\\n      roomNames: {},\\n    };\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    handleFirestoreError(error, opType, museumPath);\\n  }\\n}\", \"StartLine\":124, \"TargetContent\":\"export async function ensurePersonalMuseum(\\n  user: User,\\n  ownerName: string\\n): Promise<MuseumMeta> {\\n  const museumId = sanitizeId(`museum_${user.uid}`);\\n  const museumPath = `museums/${museumId}`;\\n  let opType = OperationType.GET;\\n  try {\\n    const snap = await getDoc(doc(db, \'museums\', museumId));\\n    if (snap.exists()) {\\n      return mapMuseumDoc(snap.id, snap.data());\\n    }\\n\\n    opType = OperationType.CREATE;\\n    const safeOwner = (ownerName || user.displayName || \'Curator\').trim().slice(0, 80);\\n    const accessCode = generateAccessCode(user.uid);\\n    const title = `${safeOwner.split(\' \')[0]}\'s Museum`.slice(0, 100);\\n    const description =\\n      \'Personal 3D architectural gallery showcasing curated artworks and chronological photographic memories.\';\\n\\n    const batch = writeBatch(db);\\n    const museumRef = doc(db, \'museums\', museumId);\\n    batch.set(museumRef, {\\n      ownerId: user.uid,\\n      ownerName: safeOwner,\\n      title,\\n      description,\\n      accessCode,\\n      wallTheme: \'alabaster\',\\n      isOpenByCode: false,\\n      memberEmails: [],\\n      curatorEmails: [],\\n      artworkCount: 0,\\n      roomNames: {},\\n      createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n      updatedAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n    });\\n\\n    const codeRef = doc(db, \'museumCodes\', accessCode);\\n    batch.set(codeRef, {\\n      accessCode,\\n      museumId,\\n      ownerId: user.uid,\\n      title,\\n      createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n    });\\n\\n    await batch.commit();\\n\\n    return {\\n      id: museumId,\\n      ownerId: user.uid,\\n      ownerName: safeOwner,\\n      title,\\n      description,\\n      accessCode,\\n      wallTheme: \'alabaster\',\\n      isOpenByCode: false,\\n      memberEmails: [],\\n      curatorEmails: [],\\n      artworkCount: 0,\\n      roomNames: {},\\n    };\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    handleFirestoreError(error, opType, museumPath);\\n  }\\n}\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":266, \"ReplacementContent\":\"export function subscribeAccessibleMuseums(\\n  user: User,\\n  onUpdate: (museums: MuseumMeta[]) => void\\n): Unsubscribe {\\n  let owned: MuseumMeta[] = [];\\n  let shared: MuseumMeta[] = [];\\n  let trustedShared: MuseumMeta[] = [];\\n\\n  const emit = () => {\\n    const byId = new Map<string, MuseumMeta>();\\n    for (const m of [...owned, ...trustedShared, ...shared]) {\\n      byId.set(m.id, m);\\n    }\\n    onUpdate(Array.from(byId.values()));\\n  };\\n\\n  const ownedQ = query(collection(db, \'museums\'), where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', user.uid));\\n  const unsubOwned = onSnapshot(\\n    ownedQ,\\n    (snap) => {\\n      owned = snap.docs.map((docSnap) => mapMuseumDoc(docSnap.id, docSnap.data()));\\n      emit();\\n    },\\n    (err) => handleFirestoreError(err, OperationType.LIST, \'museums\')\\n  );\\n\\n  let unsubShared: Unsubscribe = () => {};\\n  let unsubTrusted: Unsubscribe = () => {};\\n  if (user.emailVerified && user.email) {\\n    const sharedQ = query(\\n      collection(db, \'museums\'),\\n      where(\'memberEmails\', \'array-contains\', user.email.toLowerCase())\\n    );\\n    unsubShared = onSnapshot(\\n      sharedQ,\\n      (snap) => {\\n        shared = snap.docs.map((docSnap) => mapMuseumDoc(docSnap.id, docSnap.data()));\\n        emit();\\n      },\\n      (err) => handleFirestoreError(err, OperationType.LIST, \'museums\')\\n    );\\n\\n    // Pre-authorized trusted circle automatically discovers Abid\'s shared museum in real time\\n    if (isTrustedAbidVisitorEmail(user.email)) {\\n      const trustedQ = query(\\n        collection(db, \'museums\'),\\n        where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', ABID_PRIMARY_OWNER_UID)\\n      );\\n      unsubTrusted = onSnapshot(\\n        trustedQ,\\n        (snap) => {\\n          trustedShared = snap.docs.map((docSnap) => mapMuseumDoc(docSnap.id, docSnap.data()));\\n          emit();\\n        },\\n        (err) => {\\n          console.warn(\'Trusted shared museum lookup skipped:\', err);\\n        }\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return () => {\\n    unsubOwned();\\n    unsubShared();\\n    unsubTrusted();\\n  };\\n}\", \"StartLine\":220, \"TargetContent\":\"export function subscribeAccessibleMuseums(\\n  user: User,\\n  onUpdate: (museums: MuseumMeta[]) => void\\n): Unsubscribe {\\n  let owned: MuseumMeta[] = [];\\n  let shared: MuseumMeta[] = [];\\n\\n  const emit = () => {\\n    const byId = new Map<string, MuseumMeta>();\\n    for (const m of [...owned, ...shared]) {\\n      byId.set(m.id, m);\\n    }\\n    onUpdate(Array.from(byId.values()));\\n  };\\n\\n  const ownedQ = query(collection(db, \'museums\'), where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', user.uid));\\n  const unsubOwned = onSnapshot(\\n    ownedQ,\\n    (snap) => {\\n      owned = snap.docs.map((docSnap) => mapMuseumDoc(docSnap.id, docSnap.data()));\\n      emit();\\n    },\\n    (err) => handleFirestoreError(err, OperationType.LIST, \'museums\')\\n  );\\n\\n  let unsubShared: Unsubscribe = () => {};\\n  if (user.emailVerified && user.email) {\\n    const sharedQ = query(\\n      collection(db, \'museums\'),\\n      where(\'memberEmails\', \'array-contains\', user.email.toLowerCase())\\n    );\\n    unsubShared = onSnapshot(\\n      sharedQ,\\n      (snap) => {\\n        shared = snap.docs.map((docSnap) => mapMuseumDoc(docSnap.id, docSnap.data()));\\n        emit();\\n      },\\n      (err) => handleFirestoreError(err, OperationType.LIST, \'museums\')\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return () => {\\n    unsubOwned();\\n    unsubShared();\\n  };\\n}\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":325, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  let q;\\n  if (\\n    museum.ownerId === user.uid ||\\n    (isAbidMuseum(museum) && user.emailVerified && isTrustedAbidVisitorEmail(user.email))\\n  ) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', museum.ownerId));\\n  } else if (museum.isOpenByCode) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'isOpenByCode\', \'==\', true));\\n  } else {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'viewerEmails\', \'array-contains\', (user.email || \'\').toLowerCase()));\\n  }\", \"StartLine\":314, \"TargetContent\":\"  let q;\\n  if (museum.ownerId === user.uid) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', user.uid));\\n  } else if (museum.isOpenByCode) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'isOpenByCode\', \'==\', true));\\n  } else {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'viewerEmails\', \'array-contains\', (user.email || \'\').toLowerCase()));\\n  }\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":678, \"ReplacementContent\":\"export async function upsertPresence(\\n  museum: MuseumMeta,\\n  user: User,\\n  avatar: AvatarConfig,\\n  x: number,\\n  z: number,\\n  yaw: number,\\n  isOnline = true\\n): Promise<void> {\\n  if (!user.emailVerified) return;\\n  const path = `museums/${museum.id}/presence/${user.uid}`;\\n  const memberKey = computeMemberKey(user.email);\\n  const boundedYaw = normalizeAngle(yaw);\\n  try {\\n    const payload: Record<string, unknown> = {\\n      museumId: museum.id,\\n      ownerId: museum.ownerId,\\n      uid: user.uid,\\n      displayName: avatar.displayName.trim().slice(0, 80) || \'Visitor\',\\n      gender: avatar.gender,\\n      skinTone: avatar.skinTone,\\n      hairStyle: avatar.hairStyle.slice(0, 32),\\n      hairColor: avatar.hairColor,\\n      outfitStyle: avatar.outfitStyle.slice(0, 32),\\n      outfitColor: avatar.outfitColor,\\n      accentColor: avatar.accentColor,\\n      accessory: avatar.accessory,\\n      x: Math.max(-50, Math.min(50, Number(x.toFixed(2)))),\\n      z: Math.max(-590, Math.min(50, Number(z.toFixed(2)))),\\n      yaw: Math.max(-9.9, Math.min(9.9, Number(boundedYaw.toFixed(3)))),\\n      isOnline: Boolean(isOnline),\\n      isOpenByCode: museum.isOpenByCode,\\n      viewerEmails: museum.memberEmails.slice(0, 10),\\n      updatedAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n    };\\n    if (memberKey) {\\n      payload.memberKey = memberKey;\\n    }\\n    await setDoc(doc(db, \'museums\', museum.id, \'presence\', user.uid), payload);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    // Non-fatal presence errors are logged without crashing navigation\\n    console.warn(\'Presence update skipped:\', error);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Marks the visitor\'s 3D model as standing offline at their last position rather than deleting it,\\n * so other visitors continue to see their 3D model standing calmly in place until they reconnect.\\n */\\nexport async function markPresenceOffline(\\n  museum: MuseumMeta,\\n  user: User,\\n  avatar: AvatarConfig,\\n  x: number,\\n  z: number,\\n  yaw: number\\n): Promise<void> {\\n  await upsertPresence(museum, user, avatar, x, z, yaw, false);\\n}\\n\\nexport async function removePresence(museumId: string, uid: string): Promise<void> {\\n  try {\\n    await deleteDoc(doc(db, \'museums\', museumId, \'presence\', uid));\\n  } catch {\\n    // Ignore cleanup errors on unmount\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function subscribePresence(\\n  museum: MuseumMeta,\\n  user: User,\\n  onUpdate: (visitors: VisitorPresence[]) => void\\n): Unsubscribe {\\n  const colPath = `museums/${museum.id}/presence`;\\n  const colRef = collection(db, \'museums\', museum.id, \'presence\');\\n\\n  let q;\\n  if (\\n    museum.ownerId === user.uid ||\\n    (isAbidMuseum(museum) && user.emailVerified && isTrustedAbidVisitorEmail(user.email))\\n  ) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', museum.ownerId));\\n  } else if (museum.isOpenByCode) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'isOpenByCode\', \'==\', true));\\n  } else {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'viewerEmails\', \'array-contains\', (user.email || \'\').toLowerCase()));\\n  }\\n\\n  return onSnapshot(\\n    q,\\n    (snap) => {\\n      const list: VisitorPresence[] = snap.docs\\n        .map((docSnap) => {\\n          const d = docSnap.data();\\n          const updatedAtMs =\\n            d.updatedAt && typeof d.updatedAt.toMillis === \'function\'\\n              ? (d.updatedAt.toMillis() as number)\\n              : Date.now();\\n          return {\\n            uid: String(d.uid ?? docSnap.id),\\n            museumId: String(d.museumId ?? museum.id),\\n            ownerId: String(d.ownerId ?? museum.ownerId),\\n            memberKey: typeof d.memberKey === \'string\' ? d.memberKey : undefined,\\n            displayName: String(d.displayName ?? \'Visitor\'),\\n            gender: (d.gender === \'woman\' ? \'woman\' : \'man\') as Gender,\\n            skinTone: String(d.skinTone ?? \'#D49E76\'),\\n            hairStyle: String(d.hairStyle ?? \'taper\'),\\n            hairColor: String(d.hairColor ?? \'#1E1B18\'),\\n            outfitStyle: String(d.outfitStyle ?? \'blazer\'),\\n            outfitColor: String(d.outfitColor ?? \'#233447\'),\\n            accentColor: String(d.accentColor ?? \'#EFECE6\'),\\n            accessory:\\n              d.accessory === \'glasses\' || d.accessory === \'scarf\' || d.accessory === \'lanyard\'\\n                ? d.accessory\\n                : \'none\',\\n            x: typeof d.x === \'number\' ? d.x : 0,\\n            z: typeof d.z === \'number\' ? d.z : 2,\\n            yaw: typeof d.yaw === \'number\' ? d.yaw : 0,\\n            isOnline: typeof d.isOnline === \'boolean\' ? d.isOnline : true,\\n            updatedAt: updatedAtMs,\\n          };\\n        })\\n        .filter((v) => v.uid !== user.uid);\\n      onUpdate(list);\\n    },\\n    (err) => handleFirestoreError(err, OperationType.LIST, colPath)\\n  );\\n}\", \"StartLine\":583, \"TargetContent\":\"export async function upsertPresence(\\n  museum: MuseumMeta,\\n  user: User,\\n  avatar: AvatarConfig,\\n  x: number,\\n  z: number,\\n  yaw: number\\n): Promise<void> {\\n  if (!user.emailVerified) return;\\n  const path = `museums/${museum.id}/presence/${user.uid}`;\\n  try {\\n    await setDoc(doc(db, \'museums\', museum.id, \'presence\', user.uid), {\\n      museumId: museum.id,\\n      ownerId: museum.ownerId,\\n      uid: user.uid,\\n      displayName: avatar.displayName.trim().slice(0, 80) || \'Visitor\',\\n      gender: avatar.gender,\\n      skinTone: avatar.skinTone,\\n      hairStyle: avatar.hairStyle.slice(0, 32),\\n      hairColor: avatar.hairColor,\\n      outfitStyle: avatar.outfitStyle.slice(0, 32),\\n      outfitColor: avatar.outfitColor,\\n      accentColor: avatar.accentColor,\\n      accessory: avatar.accessory,\\n      x: Math.max(-50, Math.min(50, Number(x.toFixed(2)))),\\n      z: Math.max(-590, Math.min(50, Number(z.toFixed(2)))),\\n      yaw: Math.max(-9.9, Math.min(9.9, Number(yaw.toFixed(3)))),\\n      isOpenByCode: museum.isOpenByCode,\\n      viewerEmails: museum.memberEmails.slice(0, 10),\\n      updatedAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n    });\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    // Non-fatal presence errors are logged without crashing navigation\\n    console.warn(\'Presence update skipped:\', error);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function removePresence(museumId: string, uid: string): Promise<void> {\\n  try {\\n    await deleteDoc(doc(db, \'museums\', museumId, \'presence\', uid));\\n  } catch {\\n    // Ignore cleanup errors on unmount\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function subscribePresence(\\n  museum: MuseumMeta,\\n  user: User,\\n  onUpdate: (visitors: VisitorPresence[]) => void\\n): Unsubscribe {\\n  const colPath = `museums/${museum.id}/presence`;\\n  const colRef = collection(db, \'museums\', museum.id, \'presence\');\\n\\n  let q;\\n  if (museum.ownerId === user.uid) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', user.uid));\\n  } else if (museum.isOpenByCode) {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'isOpenByCode\', \'==\', true));\\n  } else {\\n    q = query(colRef, where(\'viewerEmails\', \'array-contains\', (user.email || \'\').toLowerCase()));\\n  }\\n\\n  return onSnapshot(\\n    q,\\n    (snap) => {\\n      const list: VisitorPresence[] = snap.docs\\n        .map((docSnap) => {\\n          const d = docSnap.data();\\n          return {\\n            uid: String(d.uid ?? docSnap.id),\\n            museumId: String(d.museumId ?? museum.id),\\n            ownerId: String(d.ownerId ?? museum.ownerId),\\n            displayName: String(d.displayName ?? \'Visitor\'),\\n            gender: (d.gender === \'woman\' ? \'woman\' : \'man\') as Gender,\\n            skinTone: String(d.skinTone ?? \'#D49E76\'),\\n            hairStyle: String(d.hairStyle ?? \'taper\'),\\n            hairColor: String(d.hairColor ?? \'#1E1B18\'),\\n            outfitStyle: String(d.outfitStyle ?? \'blazer\'),\\n            outfitColor: String(d.outfitColor ?? \'#233447\'),\\n            accentColor: String(d.accentColor ?? \'#EFECE6\'),\\n            accessory:\\n              d.accessory === \'glasses\' || d.accessory === \'scarf\' || d.accessory === \'lanyard\'\\n                ? d.accessory\\n                : \'none\',\\n            x: typeof d.x === \'number\' ? d.x : 0,\\n            z: typeof d.z === \'number\' ? d.z : 2,\\n            yaw: typeof d.yaw === \'number\' ? d.yaw : 0,\\n          };\\n        })\\n        .filter((v) => v.uid !== user.uid);\\n      onUpdate(list);\\n    },\\n    (err) => handleFirestoreError(err, OperationType.LIST, colPath)\\n  );\\n}\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/src/services/museumService.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating museumService for trusted circle & live/standing presence\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update src/services/museumService.ts\"}"
