  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 5
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Application**: **\"My Museum\"** \342\200\224 a 3D personal & shared virtual art museum built with React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Three.js, Firebase Auth + Firestore (`ai-studio-4448e632-eec0-4913-b187-f3889bfb35d4`), and Gmail API.\n- **Core Identifiers**:\n  - Owner Email & Exclusive 3D Character Owner: `abidsarker213@gmail.com` (Primary Owner UID: `CwufCmYF1kOQRybSTFLoktJuo8b2`, Primary Museum ID: `museum_CwufCmYF1kOQRybSTFLoktJuo8b2`)\n  - Trusted Circle Emails (also configured as OAuth Test Users): `abidsarker213@gmail.com`, `abidsarker098@gmail.com`, `suraia475@gmail.com`\n  - GCP / Firebase Project ID: `gen-lang-client-0648146997`\n  - Dev URL: `https://ais-dev-joduy6dwiquofhbaal2niv-406307866378.asia-northeast1.run.app`\n  - Shared URL: `https://ais-pre-joduy6dwiquofhbaal2niv-406307866378.asia-northeast1.run.app`\n- **Current User Request (3 Deliverables)**:\n  1. **Automatic Shared Access for the 3 Emails** (`abidsarker213@gmail.com`, `abidsarker098@gmail.com`, `suraia475@gmail.com`): When `suraia475@gmail.com` or `abidsarker098@gmail.com` logs in, they automatically get access to Abid\'s museum, can walk around inside it, see every artwork Abid added, and see live co-visitor movement both ways.\n  2. **Active When Logged In vs. Standing Straight in Place When Offline**: When any member logs in and enters the museum, their 3D model wakes up (`Active \302\267 Live`) and walks/turns smoothly in real time on everyone\'s screen. When offline or not yet signed in, their 3D model stands straight and calmly in one spot (`Standing \302\267 Offline`) with ZERO fake patrolling \342\200\224 and leaving the museum or signing out preserves their last position (`isOnline: false`) instead of deleting their presence doc.\n  3. **Synchronized Screen / Camera Rotation on Left/Right Movement**: When turning left or right (`A`/`D`, `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight`, `Q`/`E`, or mobile Left/Right pad), BOTH the 3D model AND the camera/screen rotate smoothly left and right together.\n- **Previous Turn Completed**: Added `/public/privacy.html` (verified via `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, and Playwright screenshot) to unblock OAuth Branding Publish.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed Code & Rules Edits (NOT YET compiled/linted/browser-verified since final edits!)\n1. **Pure Logic + Unit Tests (Created & Passed)**:\n   - `/src/museum/cameraSteering.ts`: `normalizeAngle`, `shortestAngleDelta`, `computeForwardYaw`, `stepPlayerSteering` (rotates both `camYaw` and `avatarYaw` smoothly on left/right input; triggers subtle pivot-step animation when turning in place; preserves manual mouse orbit when idle).\n   - `/src/museum/cameraSteering.test.ts`: 5 unit tests covering angle wrapping, `\302\261\317\200` shortest delta, left turn rotating both camera & avatar, forward+right curve, and idle mouse-orbit preservation.\n   - `/src/museum/trustedCircle.ts`: `ABID_PRIMARY_OWNER_UID`, `ABID_PRIMARY_MUSEUM_ID`, `ABID_TRUSTED_MEMBERS` (`suraia475@gmail.com`, `abidsarker098@gmail.com`), non-PII `computeMemberKey()` (FNV-1a hash `mk_xxxxxxxx`), `isTrustedAbidVisitorEmail`, `isAbidMuseum`, `isPresenceActive` (28s heartbeat window + `isOnline`), `pickPreferredInitialMuseumId`, and `resolveMuseumCompanionAvatars` (merges Firestore active/offline presence + standby avatars, deduplicated by `uid` & `memberKey`, zero fake patrol).\n   - `/src/museum/trustedCircle.test.ts`: 5 unit tests covering trusted email matching, auto-selecting Abid\'s museum for `suraia475`/`abidsarker098`, non-PII deduplication even when display name differs, stale/offline transition, and Abid\'s host signature avatar standing when Suraia visits while Abid is offline.\n   - Ran `npx --yes tsx --test src/museum/cameraSteering.test.ts src/museum/trustedCircle.test.ts src/museum/exclusiveAvatar.test.ts src/museum/layout.test.ts src/services/gmailService.test.ts` \342\206\222 **25/25 passing**.\n2. **Firebase Blueprint & Security Rules (Updated, Linted, & Deployed!)**:\n   - `/src/types/museum.ts`: Added optional `memberKey?: string` and `isOnline?: boolean` to `VisitorPresence`.\n   - `/firebase-blueprint.json`: Added optional `isOnline` (bool) and `memberKey` (string `<= 32`, `^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]+$`) to `VisitorPresence`.\n   - `/firestore.rules`: Added verified helpers `isAbidTrustedCircleVisitor()` (`email_verified == true` + `abidsarker098@gmail.com` or `suraia475@gmail.com`) and `isAbidPrimaryOwner(ownerId)` (`CwufCmYF1kOQRybSTFLoktJuo8b2`); extended `canAccessMuseumData`, `museums` `allow list`, `artworks` `allow list`, and `presence` `allow list`; updated `isValidPresence` and `presence` `affectedKeys().hasOnly(...)` to allow optional `isOnline` and non-PII `memberKey`.\n   - Verified `npx eslint firestore.rules` \342\206\222 **0 errors** (and removed temporary `/DRAFT_firestore.rules`).\n   - Deployed live via `rpc_action` (`service_name: \"fax\"`, `method_name: \"DeployRules\"`) \342\206\222 **succeeded**.\n3. **Application Wiring (Completed, Pending Final Compile/Lint/Browser Verification)**:\n   - `/src/services/museumService.ts`:\n     - `ensurePersonalMuseum`: When `abidsarker213@gmail.com` signs in, automatically registers `suraia475@gmail.com` and `abidsarker098@gmail.com` in `memberEmails`, deterministic `members/{seed.id}` docs, and syncs `artworks.viewerEmails`.\n     - `subscribeAccessibleMuseums`: For `suraia475@gmail.com` & `abidsarker098@gmail.com`, also subscribes to `where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', ABID_PRIMARY_OWNER_UID)` so Abid\'s museum appears immediately in real time.\n     - `subscribeArtworks` & `subscribePresence`: For Abid\'s trusted circle visiting Abid\'s museum, queries `where(\'ownerId\', \'==\', museum.ownerId)` so all artworks & all visitors\' presence records load immediately.\n     - `upsertPresence`: Normalizes `yaw` via `normalizeAngle`, writes `isOnline` and non-PII `memberKey`. Added `markPresenceOffline(...)` (writes `isOnline: false` at last position instead of deleting).\n   - `/src/three/proceduralTextures.ts`: Updated `createNameplateTexture` with static `statusTone: \'default\' | \'active\' | \'standing\'` (emerald `#6EE7B7` for Active, muted stone `#A8A29E` for Standing, no pulsing).\n   - `/src/three/avatarBuilder.ts`: Added `AvatarBuildOptions` (`nameplateSubtitle`, `statusTone`) to `buildAvatarRig` & `buildAbidSignatureRig`; added `options?: { standStill?: boolean }` to `animateAvatarRig` so offline models stand straight and still at rest.\n   - `/src/components/Museum3DView.tsx`:\n     - Replaced old strafe-only `A`/`D` with `stepPlayerSteering` so `A`/`D`, `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight`, `Q`/`E`, and mobile Left/Right pad rotate BOTH the 3D character AND camera/screen smoothly left and right.\n     - Exposes `data-cam-yaw` and `data-player-yaw` on the WebGL container for verification.\n     - Replaced fake sine-wave companion patrol with `resolveMuseumCompanionAvatars` + 5s heartbeat refresh: active visitors smoothly interpolate position & shortest-angle `yaw` (`shortestAngleDelta`) with walking animation; offline/standby visitors stand straight in place (`standStill: true`).\n     - Faster presence broadcast (`260ms` when moving/turning, `6000ms` heartbeat) + `pagehide` / unmount `onPresenceOffline` callback.\n     - Updated HUD placard (`X Active \302\267 Y Standing`), mobile D-pad aria-labels (`Turn left`/`Turn right`), and bottom dock hint.\n   - `/src/App.tsx`:\n     - Auto-selects Abid\'s shared museum upon sign-in for `suraia475@gmail.com` and `abidsarker098@gmail.com` (unless they manually switch via `manualMuseumChoiceRef`).\n     - Replaced `removePresence` on view leave / sign-out with `markPresenceOffline` preserving `lastKnownPosRef`.\n     - Passes `selfUid`, `selfEmail`, and `onPresenceOffline` to `Museum3DView`.\n   - `/src/components/HomeStudio.tsx`: Added a clean inline `<select aria-label=\"Switch active museum\">` in the top utility ribbon whenever `accessibleMuseums.length > 1`.\n\n### Skills Read in This Session\n- `/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` + `references/firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md` + `references/interaction.md`\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Root Cause of Camera Not Rotating Left/Right**: Previously `Museum3DView.tsx` mapped `A`/`D` and mobile Left/Right to sideways `strafeIn` without modifying `ps.camYaw`, and mapped `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` to `ps.camYaw` without turning the stationary 3D avatar. Also remote companion yaw interpolation lacked `shortestAngleDelta` wrapping (causing 360\302\260 spins across `\302\261\317\200`). Both are now fixed via `src/museum/cameraSteering.ts`.\n- **PII Isolation (Firestore Pillar 6)**: To deduplicate live/offline Firestore presence docs against invited members even when a user\'s Google Display Name differs from their invited name *without* exposing raw email addresses in `/presence`, we store a deterministic FNV-1a hash `memberKey` (`mk_xxxxxxxx`) instead of raw email.\n- **Zero-Wait Access Before Owner Re-Login**: Adding `isAbidPrimaryOwner(ownerId) && isAbidTrustedCircleVisitor()` to `firestore.rules` (enforcing `email_verified == true`) ensures `suraia475@gmail.com` and `abidsarker098@gmail.com` can access Abid\'s museum, artworks, and presence immediately even if Abid hasn\'t signed back in yet to sync `memberEmails`.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **Minor path typo during read**: Called `view_file` on `/src/types.ts` instead of `/src/types/museum.ts`; immediately recovered by reading `/src/types/museum.ts`.\n2. **All other steps succeeded with 0 errors**: ESLint on `DRAFT_firestore.rules` and `firestore.rules` passed cleanly; `fax.DeployRules` succeeded; 25/25 unit tests passed.\n3. **Note**: `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and Playwright browser verification have **NOT yet been run** after the edits to `museumService.ts`, `proceduralTextures.ts`, `avatarBuilder.ts`, `Museum3DView.tsx`, `App.tsx`, and `HomeStudio.tsx`!\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- All planned code edits and Firestore rule deployments are complete.\n- Firestore rules are already deployed live via `fax.DeployRules`.\n- Dev server is still running the *previous* build (`DISABLE_HMR=true`), so it MUST be compiled and restarted before Playwright verification.\n- Note in `src/components/Museum3DView.tsx`: `removePresence` is no longer imported in `App.tsx`, check if any unused symbols or TypeScript errors exist when running `compile_applet` + `lint_applet`.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Exact Priority Order)\n1. **Compile & Type-Check**: Run `compile_applet` (and fix any TypeScript/Vite errors if found).\n2. **Restart Dev Server**: Run `restart_dev_server` so port 3000 serves the new build.\n3. **Re-run All Unit Tests**: Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/museum/cameraSteering.test.ts src/museum/trustedCircle.test.ts src/museum/exclusiveAvatar.test.ts src/museum/layout.test.ts src/services/gmailService.test.ts` (verify all 25+ tests pass).\n4. **Targeted Playwright Browser Verification (1 round per Ultra Mode follow-up rule)**:\n   - Remember `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`, headless Chromium (`--browser=chromium`), unique filenames inside `.playwright-cli/`.\n   - Open `http://localhost:3000/?autostart=1` at `1440x900`.\n   - Wait for WebGL canvas frames (`data-frames`), read initial `data-cam-yaw`, `data-player-yaw`, `data-player-x`, `data-player-z`, and capture `.playwright-cli/verify-start.png`.\n   - **Test Left/Right Synchronized Rotation**: Hold `KeyA` (left) ~900ms, release, verify `camYaw` increased (> 0.5 rad) AND `playerYaw` rotated left to match, capture `.playwright-cli/verify-turn-left.png`. Then hold `KeyD` (right) ~1400ms, release, verify `camYaw` rotated right AND `playerYaw` followed, capture `.playwright-cli/verify-turn-right.png`. Also test `KeyW` + `KeyD` forward-right curve and confirm `playerZ`/`playerX` moved smoothly.\n   - **Test Standing Offline Companions**: Verify invited companion avatars in Guest preview stand calmly in place with `STANDING \302\267 OFFLINE` nameplate (no fake patrolling drift), and check `playwright-cli console` for **0 errors**.\n   - Inspect screenshots carefully; fix any visual or behavioral defects if found, and re-verify.\n5. **Final Co-Executed Verification**: If any fixes were made during Step 4, re-run unit tests, then co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in the final check before finishing. (Even if no fixes were needed in Step 4, co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together if `lint_applet` hasn\'t been run after the last edit!)\n6. **Concise Summary to User (Banglish + English)**:\n   - Clearly explain all 3 fixes implemented & verified:\n     1. `abidsarker213@gmail.com`, `abidsarker098@gmail.com`, and `suraia475@gmail.com` now have automatic access to Abid\'s museum (and `suraia475`/`abidsarker098` land directly in Abid\'s museum on sign-in, with a dropdown switcher to visit their own museum anytime).\n     2. Real-time Active vs. Standing Offline 3D models (logged-in users\' models wake up as `Active \302\267 Live` and walk/turn live in real time; offline users stand straight in place as `Standing \302\267 Offline` at their last spot with no fake wandering).\n     3. Left/Right turning (`A`/`D`, `\342\206\220`/`\342\206\222`, or mobile pad) now rotates BOTH the 3D character AND the screen/camera smoothly together.\n   - Include a humble reminder to review the Firestore rules before sharing broadly (per `firebase-integration-rpc` final steps), and remind them to re-share/update the app so the shared link gets the latest code.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Strict Exclusivity**: NEVER let guests or any email other than `abidsarker213@gmail.com` select/control Abid\'s exclusive `abid_signature` 3D model or custom `.glb` as their own avatar. (As a host companion standing in Abid\'s museum when Suraia visits, Abid\'s own host avatar uses `abid_signature`, while Suraia controls her own woman avatar.)\n- **No Pulsating Dots / No `backdrop-blur` over WebGL**: Keep all 3D HUD & nameplate status indicators clean and static.\n- **No Unnecessary Re-edits**: Do NOT re-run `DeployRules` unless `firestore.rules` is actually modified again.\n- **Ultra Mode Honesty**: Only report checks actually run and observed after the last edit.\n</summary>"
