  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Initial Request**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the initial request. It seems a central point is an exit door in the starting room that leads to the real world. I need to ensure a careful translation from the \"Banglish\" into exact requirements, paying attention to every detail provided.\n\n\n**Implementing the Exit Door**\n\nI\'m making progress on the exit door. I am replacing the static `southPortal` with a functional double-leaf door. This includes creating the doorway opening, adding the walnut-and-glass doors with clear signage, and ensuring interaction using `[F]`, `[Space]`, or a click. The door will smoothly transition the player from Room 1 to the real world.\n\n\n**Adding the Exit\'s Behavior**\n\nI\'ve made the exit a functional double-leaf door. I\'m focusing on ensuring it seamlessly transports the player to the real world. While maintaining existing inter-room door functionality, I\'m integrating the exit door, and making sure existing tests still pass. This includes a new constant for the outdoor door while ensuring the current tests for room transitions remain intact. I\'m now testing the smooth transition from the current room to the real world.\n\n\n**Defining the External Space**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the external space leading from the exit. I\'m visualizing the museum\'s grand facade with its stone steps and gilded architrave. This includes detailed coordinates and features: a classical portico, sandstone facade, marble entrance steps, and warm wall sconces. I\'m also planning the beautiful garden with a central travertine walkway, lush lawns, flowerbeds, and a tiered fountain.\n\n\n**Constructing the Landscape**\n\nI\'m now building out the garden and roadside environment, starting with diverse tree models. I\'m focusing on the orange blossom, mango, banyan, and royal palm trees, each a layered, composite `THREE.Group`. I\'ve added instanced grass tufts and shrubs for ground cover. Next is the north footpath with tiled pavers and a curb edge.\n\n\n**Populating the Roadway**\n\nI am now focusing on the road environment beyond the museum garden, specifically the vehicles and street features. I\'m adding colorful cycle-rickshaws with detailed hoods and passenger benches. I\'ve also incorporated street motorcycles and various sedans/hatchbacks. I\'m refining the south footpath and adding street lamp posts along both sidewalks, complete with light pools. Finally, I will sculpt varied architectural buildings to populate the opposite side.\n\n\n**Designing the Cityscape**\n\nI\'m now focusing on populating the opposite side of the road with distinct buildings. I\'m prioritizing diverse architectural styles to avoid repetitive designs. I\'m considering a curved glass tower, a colonial arcade, a Brutalist plaza, a dome-inspired pavilion, a boutique row, and a contemporary apartment building. Each is being meticulously designed. I\'m ensuring they will contribute to a vibrant and unique cityscape.\n\n\n**Adding Highway Direction**\n\nI\'m now integrating the highway direction signs and landmarks. I\'ve placed a highway gantry pointing to Chittagong with a hilly backdrop, and a coastal blue one to Cox\'s Bazar with a beach scene. These highway signs are complete with Bangla/English text and distinctive icons. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements clearly mark the start and end of the highway segment.\n\n\n**Implementing Vehicle Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on vehicle interaction. I\'m adding the functionality for players to hail and stop vehicles like cycle-rickshaws, motorbikes, and cars that come within range. Pressing \'E\' or \'T\' (or clicking a button) will stop the nearest vehicle, enabling the player to negotiate fares or even seize it. This is designed to be intuitive and responsive.\n\n\n**Refining Vehicle Interactions**\n\nI\'m now refining vehicle interaction. I\'ve remapped the interact key to \'E\' and confirmed it\'s available. Pressing \'E\' or \'T\' near a vehicle will smoothly stop it directly in front of the player, triggering the driver conversation panel. I\'m focusing on ensuring this interaction is both intuitive and non-blocking, pausing movement keys during conversation.\n\n\n**Developing the Ride Dialogue**\n\nI\'m now implementing the vehicle interaction dialogue system. This involves a UI panel displaying vehicle details like type and driver\'s name, along with initial fare quotes for different destinations. I\'ve designed interactive options for destination selection, fare negotiation, payment, and starting the ride. The system should deduct the fare from my wallet and allow the player to ride smoothly toward the destination.\n\n\n**Adding Vehicle Hijacking**\n\nI\'m now implementing vehicle hijacking. If I use the new \'Y\' key, I can forcefully take over a cycle-rickshaw, bike, or car, immediately entering the driver\'s seat. The original driver jumps out, shouting in Banglish, and runs off. I\'ve enabled free driving with \'W/S\', \'A/D\', \'Shift\', and \'E/F\'. I\'m also allowing conversations with pedestrians if no vehicle is close.\n\n\n**Constructing the Minimap**\n\nI\'m now focused on constructing the side minimap. I\'m building a top-right corner component for live location display. It will have sharp architectural borders, a solid background, and a display of the entire horizontal world layout. I\'m adding a Museum symbol with a label \"MUSEUM,\" and indicators for Chittagong (CTG) and Cox\'s Bazar (COXS).\n\n\n**Designing the Minimap Detail**\n\nI\'m now adding essential details to the minimap. I\'m incorporating coastal cyan/amber markers for Cox\'s Bazar, rendering opposite-side buildings as architectural footprints, and including live traffic blips. I\'m also adding a rotating player marker to show position and heading with a Zone Badge. The minimap should provide a crisp, at-a-glance view.\n\n\n**Verifying the Transition**\n\nI\'m now shifting focus to comprehensive verification. This involves ensuring that every feature works flawlessly: the exit door, outdoor garden, highway, vehicles, cityscape, minimap, and vehicle interactions. I\'m prioritizing unit tests to validate the `clampWorldPosition` across multiple environments. The Playwright tests will verify all of the new features.\n\n\n**Validating Environmental Boundaries**\n\nI am now focused on validating the environmental boundaries. I\'m ensuring collisions with opposite-side buildings and the museum outer walls are implemented correctly. I\'m testing `getWorldZone(x, z)` for various zones: museum, garden, road, Chittagong, and Cox\'s Bazar. I\'m also verifying minimap projections.\n\n\n**Testing the Journeys**\n\nI\'m now putting the entire experience to the test. I\'m focusing on the player journeys, ensuring smooth transitions and correct interactions. I\'ll walk from the starting room to the garden exit, press \"F\" to exit and step into the outdoor world. I\'ll test the \"E\" interaction near passing vehicles and the ensuing dialogue for negotiation and fare. Finally, I\'ll check that the minimap updates correctly with symbols as I head toward Chittagong and Cox\'s Bazar.\n\n\n**Structuring the World Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on cleanly structuring the world\'s logic into a modular file. I\'m building `src/museum/outdoorWorld.ts`, with constants defining the world bounds and zone definitions. I\'m particularly ensuring the seamless collision of `clampWorldPosition(x, z)` across the environment. I\'m excited about this unit testable design. I have to make sure there are no console errors when I verify the results.\n\n\n**Defining World Boundaries**\n\nI am now adding the world boundaries and minimap projections. I\'m focusing on collision with museum walls, fountain areas, and roadside buildings and implementing `clampWorldPosition` to ensure I cannot drive inside the museum. I\'m also now mapping the world to the minimap canvas via `projectWorldToMinimap`. I\'m verifying boundary logic now and building the initial traffic vehicles and defining vehicle fare negotiation logic.\n\n\n**Implementing Vehicle Interaction**\n\nI\'m now implementing the complete vehicle interaction. I\'ve focused on creating a fleet of various vehicles and functions like `findNearestHailVehicle`, `createTalkSession`, and `negotiateTalkSession`. The system now includes realistic fare negotiation with authentic Banglish dialogue. I\'m also adding functionality for the player to accept a ride, take over vehicles, and drive them smoothly, all with unit tests.\n\n\n**Generating Procedural Textures**\n\nI\'m now generating procedural textures. I\'m focusing on creating an asphalt highway texture, a garden stone walkway, brick sidewalk tiles, and crisp Bangladeshi highway signboards. I\'m also ensuring the outdoor daylight sky smoothly integrates with a warm golden-hour tone when the player steps outside.\n\n\n**Refining the Museum Facade**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the museum\'s grand facade. I want a majestic building visible from the garden, so I\'m paying attention to details like emerald lawns, stone walkways, and vibrant flower beds. The composite trees and varied buildings are coming along nicely, too. I\'m excited about how the warm, glowing lanterns and procedural textures enhance the scene.\n\n\n**Expanding the Landscape**\n\nI\'m now expanding the landscape with detailed landmarks. I\'m adding a Bookshop Row with striped awnings, and other structures. I\'m building out a Chittagong Port Tower and Beachfront Resort Villa. I\'m placing highway gantries and road signs with distances, and coastal markers and trees. I\'m refining composite interactive vehicles with driver groups.\n\n\n**Adding Pedestrian Interaction**\n\nI\'m now integrating walking footpath pedestrians. I\'ve placed 10 composite characters with realistic animations along the North and South paths. I\'m excited about the addition of an angry NPC that appears when the player ejects a driver (as a result of vehicle hijacking).\n\n\n**Designing the Dialogue Systems**\n\nI\'m now integrating UI elements for vehicle interactions. The `VehicleTalkModal` is interactive, showing vehicle details, and fare information in Banglish. The destination selector and bargain fare options are functional, and I\'m ensuring smooth UI/UX. The next step will be to seamlessly connect the modal to the player\'s wallet and the ride\'s initiation, ensuring clear feedback for each step.\n\n\n**Refining UI Interactivity**\n\nI\'m now integrating the modal with payment and ride initiation. I\'ve added \"Pay & Ride\" and \"Take Vehicle\" buttons to the dialogue UI. The \"Pay & Ride\" option now deducts the agreed fare from my wallet and starts the vehicle movement, while \"Take Vehicle\" is more dynamic, allowing immediate control after vehicle seizure. I\'m focusing on ensuring clear UI/UX feedback for these steps, making sure all the text is in Banglish.\n\n\n"
