  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing a Precise Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the architecture. I\'m aiming for mathematical precision so that every component: the floor plan, walls, ceilings, skylights, flower vases, doors, eighteen artworks, collision clamping, and teleportation all align perfectly and work together seamlessly.\n\n\n**Refining Spatial Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the spatial logic, ensuring no gaps, wall clipping, or overlapping frames. The architectural blueprint now consists of two small rooms (8 artworks each) alternating with one grand Cross/X-shaped hall (18 artworks). I\'m meticulously checking the math to ensure this pattern holds and the artwork indexing is flawless. The intention is unmistakable Cross/X grandeur.\n\n\n**Validating Artwork Distribution**\n\nI\'m now validating the artwork distribution algorithm\'s accuracy, confirming the mathematical precision of the room cycles. The museum layout function, when provided different numbers of artworks, creates the expected room arrangements, always resulting in a total wall slot count matching the artwork count. Each Cross/X-shaped hall promises genuine grandeur and spaciousness, thanks to its cruciform plan and diagonal X-Pavilion geometry!\n\n\n**Defining Cross Hall Dimensions**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining the precise dimensions of the grand Cross/X hall. I\'ve calculated the depth of the north-south arm to be 28.0 meters. The central nave is 16.4 meters wide, connecting to the smaller rooms via double doors. The wide east and west transept wings are a total of 36.4 meters wide, extending 10 meters outwards on both sides. I\'m focusing on the z-span of the transept wings.\n\n\n**Visualizing Hall Interior**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the hall interior, focusing on the visual motif. On the floor, there\'s a gilded brass and travertine Cross, plus a diagonal X starburst mosaic inlay. Overhead, an elevated vaulted X-cross skylight dome creates a striking architectural effect. I\'m imagining the effect of the light, the materials, and the shape. The X and Cross geometry is starting to feel very substantial. I\'m keen to ensure the visual impact is as intended.\n\n\n**Detailing the X-Hall**\n\nI\'m currently detailing the X-Hall. I\'m focusing on the ceiling, with intersecting gilded arch ribs forming a giant illuminated X/Cross directly above the central crossing, and linear skylights stretching into both West and East wings! I\'m also considering the four grand fluted classical columns flanking the central crossing corners with diagonal sculpted chamfer pilasters accenting the X-crossing, and a monumental octagonal gilded centerpiece plinth with a grand imperial floral vase. I\'m trying to visualize how the light falls on those forms.\n\n\n**Calculating Wall Slot Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now calculating precise wall slot coordinates for artwork placement, meticulously mapping them in relation to the X-Hall geometry. I\'ve pinpointed locations, including West Arm and West Wing walls, determining rotations and standpoints for optimal viewing angles and maintaining the desired flow. Clearances are verified for an even distribution.\n\n\n\n**Mapping Artwork Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now mapping artwork coordinates, focusing on the East and West wings of the Cross/X-Hall, specifically detailing Slots 5 through 10. The West Wing North and End walls are defined as well as East wing walls, with standpoints and rotations calculated, ensuring proper spacing and viewing angles. Calculations include coordinates, rotations and viewpoints to create a seamless viewing experience.\n\n\n**Calculating Final Slots**\n\nI\'m now calculating artwork locations for slots 11 through 16. The East Wing end and north walls are set, along with the North Arm walls, including their rotation and standpoints. I\'ve ensured correct spacing and viewing angles. Calculations include the precise coordinates, rotations, and viewpoints. I am meticulously confirming each coordinate, ensuring the viewing experience is seamless.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Slot Accuracy**\n\nI\'m now verifying slot accuracy, specifically slots 17 and 18, focusing on the north-east and north-west flanking walls of the cross/X hall. I\'ve confirmed their precise x and z coordinates, along with rotation values. I\'ve also added the \"south\" wall side to the ArtworkPlacement enum. Now I\'m double-checking the camera lookYaw, ensuring the teleportation look angle is spot-on for both west and east facing directions.\n\n\n**Confirming Look Angles**\n\nI\'m now confirming look angles for optimal artwork viewing, specifically for the East/West Wing South and North wall slots. I\'ve re-evaluated and revised the `wallSide`, `rotY`, `camYaw`, and `avatar.yaw` calculations, ensuring that the player\'s viewing experience aligns perfectly with the intended artwork placement and facing direction, guaranteeing a comfortable and immersive interaction. I\'ve also re-confirmed those calculations.\n\n\n**Refining Construction Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the construction logic to build per-room elements. Instead of one continuous rectangle for the floor, ceiling, and outer walls, I\'m building them per room in `museumBuilder.ts`. This includes separate floors, ceilings, and outer walls for each standard room and X-Hall. This should prevent sealing off the West and East wings of the cross-hall.\n\n\n**Defining Floor Construction**\n\nI\'m now defining the floor construction, dividing the Cross/X-Hall floor into three non-overlapping pieces. I\'ve calculated the central north-south nave floor, the west wing, and the east wing, ensuring no Z-fighting. The ceiling, at HALL_HEIGHT, mirrors this cruciform design, with the central elevated X-dome lantern. I\'m focused on the precise dimensions.\n\n\n**Verifying Hall Geometry**\n\nI\'m now focusing on verifying the hall geometry, specifically the dimensions. I\'ve re-confirmed coordinates for the East and West Wing walls, ensuring they are correctly placed within the cruciform structure. The calculations ensure that there are no overlaps. I\'m checking the parameters again to rule out Z-fighting.\n\n\n**Unifying Collision Logic**\n\nI\'m now unifying collision logic. I\'ve created `clampIndoorPosition` in `layout.ts` for consistent indoor collision across the board. Both `clampPlayerPosition` and `clampWorldPosition` now call it. I\'ve also addressed the cruciform room collision, clamping Z to the valid range and enforcing inter-room doors. For cross-hall rooms, I\'ve defined the walkable regions as a union of two rectangles, handling X and Z clamping accordingly. I\'m aiming for seamless collision handling.\n\n\n**Defining Cross Hall Collision**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the precise collision handling for the Cross/X-Hall. The nave and wing rectangles are defined: `|x| <= naveMaxX` and `|x| <= wingMaxX`, respectively. I\'m implementing a clamping mechanism to resolve potential diagonal corner violations, ensuring smooth and predictable wall sliding along all hall walls.\n\n\n\n**Refining Mobile UI**\n\nI\'m now refining the mobile UI, specifically imap\'s responsive design and the top-left placard\'s positioning to prevent overlap. I\'ve re-adjusted the imap layout on mobile screens, and re-verified both layouts. I\'m focusing on ensuring responsiveness without sacrificing clarity on either screen size.\n\n\n\n**Adding Cross Hall to Types**\n\nI\'m now adding `\'cross_hall\'` to `RoomShape` within `/src/types/museum.ts`, preparing for implementation. I\'m also now implementing the new repeating room engine in `/src/museum/layout.ts`, defining `RoomDefinition` with relevant properties and supporting both room types. I\'m focusing on unified cruciform `clampPlayerPosition` and seamless delegation to `clampPlayerPosition` in `/src/museum/outdoorWorld.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing Cruciform Structure**\n\nI\'m now fully implementing the cruciform structure with per-room floors, ceilings, and walls, plus the Grand Cross/X-Hall 3D architecture, including the X-starburst floor mosaic, intersecting ceiling arch ribs, skylight dome, and other details. I\'ve updated the world minimap for responsive sizing with an optional Cross-Hall footprint. I\'m ensuring mobile UI adjustments, accurate artwork slot capacity copy, and comprehensive unit tests. I\'m focusing on defining `RoomShape` and adding `\'cross_hall\'` to `/src/types/museum.ts` for room implementation.\n\n\n"
