  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Core Insight**\n\nI\'ve hit a breakthrough! I now understand the whole issue with perfect clarity. Setting `renderer.setPixelRatio(0.65)` on `isSoftwareGl` is the key. This maintains a crisp 936\303\227585 internal render, cleanly scaled to 1440\303\227900, using significantly fewer pixels! It solves the problem and it\'s elegant.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "1O8Ca7DjFcD4-8YPwOWkgAo"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4628009547403847111"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Optimize software WebGL fragment cost (pixelRatio 0.65, skip PMREM lookup on software rasterizers while boosting hemisphere fill) so outdoor rendering stays responsive on SwiftShader and low-end GPUs\", \"Instruction\":\"Adjust pixelRatio and RoomEnvironment only when isSoftwareGl is true, and safely dispose envTex\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":535, \"ReplacementContent\":\"    renderer.setSize(width, height);\\n    renderer.setPixelRatio(isSoftwareGl ? 0.65 : Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\\n    renderer.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\\n    renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;\\n    renderer.toneMappingExposure = 0.94;\\n    renderer.shadowMap.enabled = !isSoftwareGl;\\n    renderer.shadowMap.type = THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;\\n    renderer.domElement.style.display = \'block\';\\n    renderer.domElement.style.width = \'100%\';\\n    renderer.domElement.style.height = \'100%\';\\n    container.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\\n    rendererRef.current = renderer;\\n\\n    const scene = new THREE.Scene();\\n    const fogHex = THEME_FOG_COLOR[museum.wallTheme];\\n    renderer.setClearColor(fogHex, 1);\\n    scene.background = new THREE.Color(fogHex);\\n    scene.fog = new THREE.FogExp2(fogHex, 0.01);\\n    sceneRef.current = scene;\\n\\n    // Studio environment map for metallic bronze frames, marble & glazed flower vases (hardware GPU)\\n    let envTex: THREE.Texture | null = null;\\n    if (!isSoftwareGl) {\\n      const pmrem = new THREE.PMREMGenerator(renderer);\\n      envTex = pmrem.fromScene(new RoomEnvironment(), 0.04).texture;\\n      scene.environment = envTex;\\n      pmrem.dispose();\\n    }\\n\\n    const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(56, width / height, 0.1, 260);\\n    camera.position.set(0, 2.2, 7.8);\\n    camera.lookAt(0, 1.7, -4);\\n\\n    // Calibrated architectural + outdoor sunlight rig (<= 1 shadow caster, <= 4 dynamic room lights)\\